{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated","id":1107411,"title":"Humanity Is Overrated","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-24T14:00:44-07:00","id":1107411,"title":"Humanity Is Overrated","content":"A continuation thread from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1104161-why-do-you-think-beast-is-good-bad/page8\">this discussion</a>, in which we point out that humanity as a species may not be as great as it portrays itself to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> Long story short, we're talking about why human ingenuity and willpower overcoming powerful enemies is nothing but trite propaganda in the Chronicles of Darkness!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T14:15:45-07:00","id":1107414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated#post1107411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Long story short, we're talking about why human ingenuity and willpower overcoming powerful enemies is nothing but trite propaganda in the Chronicles of Darkness!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the reason is the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> And they're not limited to humanity. Most supernaturals think about local problems, and that's only if they can lift their head up from personal problems. In Dave Brookshaw's mage games, the world was on the verge of ending at least two times and mages outside of the consilium involved didn't even believe it, let alone offer help. When an idigam stomped across the Rockies, no one banded together to defeat it until Max Roman forced some of them to.<br /> <br /> The idea that the monsters will overcome all powerful enemies, or are some organized threat, is just as much trite propaganda. There's a reason there are clans and orders that have died out and why every game line has antagonists coming from the same template as the players. If storytellers are going to ignore these problems and tout monsters as some collective threat, then storytellers can also ignore the more cynical and problematic parts of humanity that keep tropes tropes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-24-2017, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T15:10:37-07:00","id":1107422,"title":"","content":"Perhaps I should have clarified. In the previous discussion topic, we brought up the fact that humanity believes itself to be the dominant species because of their intellectual capacity and their technological progress. But how we almost never stop to consider what would happen if one or more supernatural entities possessed the same level of intelligence, had access to our technology, and possessed a host of abilities that humanity deemed scientifically impossible.<br /> <br /> In other words, the various playable splats across the CoD who blend in with human society and learn to use its resources as their own. At that point, it becomes less about humanity's ability to adapt to their enemy and more about a war of attrition. Humanity's strength lies in its overwhelming numbers; they can defeat their enemies by outlasting them in battle. And most of the books I've read seem to agree on this subject. They all confirm that humans don't pose much of a threat in small numbers, it's what happens when you've got a mob of them chasing after you that they become a problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> So if the only thing standing between the monsters and global domination is that their enemy breeds faster than they can kill them, then one has to question whether humans are really as awesome as they hyped themselves up to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-24-2017, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T15:24:19-07:00","id":1107428,"title":"","content":"I've always felt that... Humanity has a massive advantage over a lot of monsters, in that a lot of monsters NEED humanity for their survival. Vampires need blood. Werewolves need families. Mages come from humanity (if Mages don't count as &quot;human&quot; for this conversation). Even Beasts need to feast.<br /> <br /> But humanity... Humanity only needs to be lucky once, time and time again. It doesn't matter if a werewolf can kill a hundred people, just one in the right place, at the right time, can end it. <br /> <br /> And so if there is a grand conflict... Ultimately, it is a war of attrition. A war of biding ones time until the moment comes to strike. <br /> <br /> The monsters are handicapped if they hope to preserve themselves, because ultimately, the monsters need humanity. But humanity doesn't necessarily need the monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T17:56:48-07:00","id":1107455,"title":"","content":"Except for the fact that several of the species don't really require one or both parents to be of that species in order for new ones to arise. I know it was explicitly pointed out that Beasts don't. Garou last I heard do require someone in a person's bloodline to have been one, but since a werewolf can also start off as a wolf I guess you'd need to kill ever single member in both extremes. <br /> <br /> Also the argument that humanity only needs to be lucky once I think gives the wrong impression. This isn't Penguin only needing to get lucky with one bullet to end Batman. That kind of makes it sound like a human getting lucky can end the vampire threat forever, as opposed to needing to being lucky and ending a vampire, or a werewolf, a demon, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T18:35:02-07:00","id":1107477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107422#post1107422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if the only thing standing between the monsters and global domination is that their enemy breeds faster than they can kill them, then one has to question whether humans are really as awesome as they hyped themselves up to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, as I pointed out, global domination would be hindered by the supernaturals just as much as by the humans. They are not nearly as organized as you seem to think, while even in real life we have vast governments and organizations that are dedicated to dealing with threats. Just about every nation on the planet has an army, and none of the supernaturals do. It's well enough if a vampire can get a bomber and a nuclear weapon, entire nations of humanity make those, they have the infrastructure to do so, and have been for decades for their defense.<br /> <br /> I really wouldn't say humans have hyped themselves up to be awesome, either. If they consider themselves the dominant species it's because they are. Mages, vampires, Beasts, Changelings, they aren't species of their own. Just like there are athletes and soldiers and scientists and cult leaders among humans who are individually better in certain focuses, they don't say that athletes, soldiers, scientists and cult leaders are the 'dominant species.' All these tropes that humanity would all gather together to defeat a great threat or that some super genius with the solution would be able to rise to the top and fix everything? That's what your argument relies on the monsters having. When in truth, at least as posed by the setting, they're just as disorganized, just as self serving, just as frequently incorrect and just as able to fail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107455#post1107455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for the fact that several of the species don't really require one or both parents to be of that species in order for new ones to arise. I know it was explicitly pointed out that Beasts don't. Garou last I heard do require someone in a person's bloodline to have been one, but since a werewolf can also start off as a wolf I guess you'd need to kill ever single member in both extremes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou isn't a Chronicles term. Uratha, werewolf. And they can't start as a wolf and don't need someone in a person's bloodline to have been one. You may be thinking old World of Darkness, though you did mention Beasts.<br /> <br /> All that said, as a war of attrition, if you killed off all of humanity then vampires would have no food, the astral would likely rot, the gentry would have no dreams or stories, prometheans would have nothing to strive to be, demons would have no place to hide, beasts would have no one to teach. And they would turn on each other. Because any monster could look at another supernatural and say it's 'close enough.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107455#post1107455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the argument that humanity only needs to be lucky once I think gives the wrong impression. This isn't Penguin only needing to get lucky with one bullet to end Batman. That kind of makes it sound like a human getting lucky can end the vampire threat forever, as opposed to needing to being lucky and ending a vampire, or a werewolf, a demon, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they could. Each splat has things dedicated to ending it. Demons have the God Machine, Changelings the True Fae and huntsmen, Werewolves the Pure or idigam, Vampires the strix, Mages banishers, and a variety of other extraneous beings who just need a leg up to simply end an entire gameline.<br /> <br /> If for some reason everything did get amped up and let loose, humanity and the gamelines would lose, at the 'hands' of the beings that are to them what the gamelines are to humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-24-2017, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T19:10:34-07:00","id":1107486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107455#post1107455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for the fact that several of the species don't really require one or both parents to be of that species in order for new ones to arise. I know it was explicitly pointed out that Beasts don't. Garou last I heard do require someone in a person's bloodline to have been one, but since a werewolf can also start off as a wolf I guess you'd need to kill ever single member in both extremes.<br /> <br /> Also the argument that humanity only needs to be lucky once I think gives the wrong impression. This isn't Penguin only needing to get lucky with one bullet to end Batman. That kind of makes it sound like a human getting lucky can end the vampire threat forever, as opposed to needing to being lucky and ending a vampire, or a werewolf, a demon, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I thought that Werewolves were like Beasts in that anybody could randomly become one. Wolf Blooded families just have a higher chance of doing so than human bloodlines. I have only a bare bones basic information on 2nd edition Werewolf, though, so if that was changed at some point, I'm not aware of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> But even if Werewolves do need families, there's nothing stopping them from breeding with each other (at least in 2nd edition). So they don't need humans around for that to happen.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> As for vampires not having access to an army, I believe that may be a woeful misconception. Vampires have been orchestrating a shadow government for thousands of years. They have not one, but two clans who are specifically dedicated to manipulating / dominating the population. Adding to that is their ability to offer power and immortality to anybody who drinks just a few drops of their blood each month and you've got a species that could very easily seize control of military assets.<br /> <br /> <br /> Prometheans.... are exactly the point we're arguing against, so I don't know how to respond to that.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not saying that monsters should wipe out the human population. That would be like humans wiping out their own food supply. I'm saying that humanity is not the superior species and its claims to being so are ludicrous.<br /> <br /> Paradim, you said that a single werewolf might be able to kill a hundred humans, but one lucky human positioned in the right spot can take them down. Here's the thing, if a human needs to rely on luck, then it's not superiority. It's a blind fluke.<br /> <br /> Also, Werewolves travel in packs, so if a single werewolf can kill a hundred humans, then 5 werewolves increases the dangers exponentially. Sure that 'lucky' human might be able to bring down one werewolf, possibly 2 of them, but once the pack finds out they're under attack, they need to haul ass before the wolves use their canine senses to hunt them down.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> As for humans being the dominant species because they are able to claim it, that is not a valid argument. That's just human arrogance talking; the species who commits all manner of atrocities and then condemns other life forms for behaving in a similar fashion. Anybody can claim to be the dominant species, but you're going to have to prove it if you want people to take you seriously. And humans relying on overwhelming numbers and blind luck is not proving anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> Without their vaunted technology, humans are extremely vulnerable.<br /> <br /> You take technology away from the monsters, however, and they're still powerful enough to end you in the blink of an eye.<br /> <br /> <br /> Humans NEED technology to defend themselves. Monsters don't need technology, they just realize the benefits of having it around.<br /> <br /> So who's really the dominant species? The one who can take down prey with their bare hands, or the ones who can't survive without artificial assistance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T19:19:15-07:00","id":1107488,"title":"","content":"How are we measuring humans' &quot;superiority&quot; or lack thereof though? If it's in ability to kill other splats or in kewl powerz, then yeah, they're overrated. Humanity's strength in the CofD setting is in their... I don't know if &quot;purity&quot; is quite the right word, but they're among the few things in CofD that have souls, and most non-human souls are messed up in one way or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T19:33:20-07:00","id":1107493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107486#post1107486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So who's really the dominant species? The one who can take down prey with their bare hands, or the ones who can't survive without artificial assistance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think people are coming in here with different definitions of &quot;dominant.&quot; You could argue Mages are &quot;dominant&quot; because they have the most raw power, and a Mage specialized for something could blow almost anything else out of the water in that arena. Vampires could be argued to be &quot;dominant&quot; because of how deeply-entrenched they are in world governments, you could say Werewolves are &quot;dominant&quot; as apex predators. You could say Mummies are dominant simply on raw power. And you could say humans are dominant because of their overwhelming numerical superiority and the fact that their existence isn't anathema to reality and they don't break down in contact with relatively mundane substances.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, Vampires, Magi, Mummies, Beasts, and Changelings are arguably not different species from humans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T19:35:57-07:00","id":1107494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107488#post1107488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are we measuring humans' &quot;superiority&quot; or lack thereof though? If it's in ability to kill other splats or in kewl powerz, then yeah, they're overrated. Humanity's strength in the CofD setting is in their... I don't know if &quot;purity&quot; is quite the right word, but they're among the few things in CofD that have souls, and most non-human souls are messed up in one way or another.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The comparison is a fight between humans and monsters who are possessed of similar level intelligence and have access to the same technological development as each other. The monsters are just as smart as humans, just as advanced as humans, but their supernatural powers make them many times more capable than humans. So, in short, humanity is overrated, and their superiority is a work of popular fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T20:18:33-07:00","id":1107499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107494#post1107494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The comparison is a fight between humans and monsters who are possessed of similar level intelligence and have access to the same technological development as each other. The monsters are just as smart as humans, just as advanced as humans, but their supernatural powers make them many times more capable than humans. So, in short, humanity is overrated, and their superiority is a work of popular fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's your metric, then yeah. Go figure monsters would be better at doing murder than humans. That's not, however, the metric by which CofD ranks humans as superior.<br /> <br /> As a wise muppet once said, &quot;wars not make one great.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T20:46:43-07:00","id":1107504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107499#post1107499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that's your metric, then yeah. Go figure monsters would be better at doing murder than humans. That's not, however, the metric by which CofD ranks humans as superior.<br /> <br /> As a wise muppet once said, &quot;wars not make one great.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If it's the one I'm thinking of, that muppet and the rest of his collection of samurai space wizards couldn't recognize a monster poised to topple their entire society when it was standing 3 feet in front of their faces. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T20:51:51-07:00","id":1107505,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> I don't play Werewolf, so I'll admit I'm not sure on how the Garou thing shows up and the last I'd heard from from a freind there was the implication that it was just passed down. Wasn't sure myself, so if I'm wrong there my mistake. It probably doesn't help that I'm unsure how much of my information on Werewolf is CoD or WoD and that probably gets things screwed up a bit.<br /> <br /> As for the rest of the thread I think it probably would have been served better by pointing out that the inciting line was that we had someone arguing humans were the literal top of the food chain and how the only group that weren't inferior to humans were mages and that's barely since mages still had to deal with paradox. Then it just went on from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T21:00:19-07:00","id":1107506,"title":"","content":"And yet said monster couldn't see the huge disadvantage of manipulating one of those samurai space wizards into his own personal monster via lies and subterfuge, and then had maaaasively bad judgment over that human's capacity to connect with humanity (specifically the son said monster lied about) and got his ass thrown down a space-shoot and exploded at the literal cusp of victory...all because he was a prideful sob who underestimated humanity. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> My point: Any monster who dismisses humans as not dangerous are doomed to the same fate as the Emperor. Never that humans are superior, but that they are the dominant species in both our world and the WoD for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish. 06-25-2017, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T21:04:10-07:00","id":1107507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107486#post1107486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that Werewolves were like Beasts in that anybody could randomly become one.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's this persistent fandom myth that needs to go away right quick if anyone's to have a clear understanding of how the default settings work: For the vast and overwhelming majority of ex-mortal monsters, there is nothing random about how they became what they are to those who take the time to look. Even if it involved a dice roll. (<i>Especially</i> if it involved a dice roll. Coincidence is a sucker's bet.)<br /> <br /> And go figure, the two splats that stand to understand this the best \u2014 mages and Beasts \u2014 are the ones that retain the most of their outward humanity; vampires and changelings and Prometheans have a secondary view of the matter by virtue of how they're made, and werewolves exist alongside what remains perhaps the most porous and meddlesome otherworld in the Chronicles of Darkness setting over more than a decade of published material. (Mummies and demons each get different halves of the whole reason and a whole lot of distractions to keep that understanding from being their top priority, and Deviants explicitly become what they are because plain human meddling in the supernatural with no guiding force is as close as the games get to random while still being a game about people turned into monsters by conspiracies.)<br /> <br /> In short, a monster is made for a purpose and born from circumstances that, while sometimes arbitrary in theory, justify and foreshadow the creation of Frederica The Sin-Eater. Like attracts like, the gods make instruments of people who catch their fancy, and the whims of fate are built upon patterns and confluences and aesthetics. &quot;Anyone&quot; tends to mean &quot;Whoever happens to be appropriate and unclaimed&quot; over &quot;Whoever comes up on an unbiased dice roll.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T21:07:48-07:00","id":1107508,"title":"","content":"I'll give you one metric that makes humanity superior-the fact that all monsters exists as a commentary on the species.<br /> <br /> Enthralled as I am by our shadows, they are shadows on papyrus nevertheless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T22:32:48-07:00","id":1107517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107504#post1107504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's the one I'm thinking of, that muppet and the rest of his collection of samurai space wizards couldn't recognize a monster poised to topple their entire society when it was standing 3 feet in front of their faces. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately they were able to explain this away in Rogue One with a single off-hand line. The dark side of the force gathers around someone when they are about to take a life. Palpatine was giving orders that would lead to the loss of thousands of lives. The Jedi probably perceived the dark side all around him, along with every other senator in the republic at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T23:03:32-07:00","id":1107529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107517#post1107517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fortunately they were able to explain this away in Rogue One with a single off-hand line. The dark side of the force gathers around someone when they are about to take a life. Palpatine was giving orders that would lead to the loss of thousands of lives. The Jedi probably perceived the dark side all around him, along with every other senator in the republic at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they tried handwaving it in the novelizations by saying they figured Palpatine was a puppet if he was involved with the Sith and that it would make no sense for him to be the Sith Lord trying to take over because he was already in charge of everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T23:06:15-07:00","id":1107530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107529#post1107529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they tried handwaving it in the novelizations by saying they figured Palpatine was a puppet if he was involved with the Sith and that it would make no sense for him to be the Sith Lord trying to take over because he was already in charge of everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the &quot;politicians are always surrounded in the dark side during wartime&quot; explaination better - it also explains the distrust the Jedi openly display towards politicians in Attack of the Clones as a nice bonus. But this is getting very off-topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T00:46:14-07:00","id":1107565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107505#post1107505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> I don't play Werewolf, so I'll admit I'm not sure on how the Garou thing shows up and the last I'd heard from from a freind there was the implication that it was just passed down. Wasn't sure myself, so if I'm wrong there my mistake. It probably doesn't help that I'm unsure how much of my information on Werewolf is CoD or WoD and that probably gets things screwed up a bit.<br /> <br /> As for the rest of the thread I think it probably would have been served better by pointing out that the inciting line was that we had someone arguing humans were the literal top of the food chain and how the only group that weren't inferior to humans were mages and that's barely since mages still had to deal with paradox. Then it just went on from there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't play it either, I bought the 1st edition book, but couldn't get my mind around it. But, basically yeah. Anybody could potentially become a Werewolf, just like anybody could potentially become a Beast. Wolf Blooded people just have a higher chance of undergoing the First Change because they're predisposed to it.<br /> <br /> In second edition, a human can even become wolf blooded through suffering the effects of Lunacy, which is caused by witnessing a Werewolf in any of its partial forms. Which lends credence to the myths of somebody becoming a werewolf after encountering one.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------<br /> <br /> As for Palpatine being seared to a crisp, he actually managed to survive that.... before the retcon. Palpatine figured out how to clone force sensitives, and transferred his soul into a clone body, allowing him to cheat death and come back in a state that didn't look like a 172 year old. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I didn't see Rogue One... I'm tired of prequels, I want a god damn sequel. And NO, combining the original trilogy into one movie doesn't count, Episode 7! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T01:40:14-07:00","id":1107577,"title":"","content":"I'm not entirely sure what the aim for this thread is. There's concepts like war and an apparent number of egocentric displays on the part of humanity being tossed around, as if wars didn't needed terms like sides, or as if the vast majority of people didn't truly believed that the only intelligent form of life on the planet is the Homo Sapiens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T07:56:40-07:00","id":1107636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107577#post1107577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not entirely sure what the aim for this thread is. There's concepts like war and an apparent number of egocentric displays on the part of humanity being tossed around, as if wars didn't needed terms like sides, or as if the vast majority of people didn't truly believed that the only intelligent form of life on the planet is the Homo Sapiens.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were to hazard a guess, I'd say it's a thinly disguised humanism vs posthumanism argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T07:59:54-07:00","id":1107637,"title":"","content":"It this only in a context of open conflict? Because I kinda agree with Arc and might have something relevant to say if the discussion is not only about war between humans and monsters<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107530#post1107530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the &quot;politicians are always surrounded in the dark side during wartime&quot; explaination better - it also explains the distrust the Jedi openly display towards politicians in Attack of the Clones as a nice bonus. But this is getting very off-topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I can get even more off topic for a second, there's a moment in Nioh, which is essentially a game where all monsters and spirits of the Japanese Mythology are true, where Tokugawa Ieyasu, while still portrayed as a positive character and big good of the setting, is, to the eyes of the main character who can spot ephemeral creatures, completely surrounded by negative resonance and vengeful spirits because of all the tough choices he made and deaths he caused while trying to unify Japan. I thought that was a clever and cool touch when I saw it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-25-2017, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T12:22:07-07:00","id":1107709,"title":"","content":"As individuals, supernaturals are often times superior to a mortal or even a set of mortals. That's simplicity in of itself - we are ultimately a very squishy race of very squishy people. That said.<br /> <br /> We are not at the top of the food chain because of our biological superiority to other races. If that was the determining factor, the ultimate race would probably be something like bears, lions, or sharks. We wouldn't even rank.<br /> <br /> But we do rank, and we are at the top of the food chain. Why? Because of ingenuity. Because we adapt using our minds and the tools around us. Were the humans to become aware of the supernaturals existence, it would threaten all supernaturals - not because of things like bombs, or the superior weaponry, or really any of the technology that we have now.<br /> <br /> It's because humans evolve the fastest during any time of war, especially when they have something to hate - or fear. It's because humans haven't yet captured a werewolf and put them into a lab to study all the most effective ways in which to utilize silver to kill them, easily and efficiently without killing normal humans. It's because no one's studied what kind of UV ray lights are required to sear a vampire into ash and publicized that information to put it into a standard for a city's street lights. It's because 'raw numbers' isn't a feature of strength, but of the raw number of ideas that people can come up with to eliminate their enemies.<br /> <br /> Humans are not superior because they have things that can blow up a supernatural that supernaturals don't have. It's because supernaturals have all the tools they would need and don't -need- to get better, stronger, or smarter - and humans not only do, but -can-. Better to let the humans live in ignorance, so they never know the need to adapt to defend themselves from what is -currently- a superior threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 06-25-2017, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T13:08:28-07:00","id":1107726,"title":"","content":"People also seem to be kind of glossing over the biggesty, and most clear advantage that Humans have over supernaturals: They don't have a lot of weaknesses. Wolves have silver, Mages have Paradox, vampires are comatose for hours at a time and burn under the light of something that's overhead for about 50% of the time, Prometheans and Vampires both share a weakness to fire, Demons have to contend with the God-Machine, the God-Machine has to contend with its own madness and incompetence, Changelings have to worry about maintaining their Bulwark and Hunntsmen in general, Beasts need to feed and have a whole class of people who are naturally predisposed to find, weaken and kill them, and so on.<br /> <br /> Really, the only major splats that don't have a clear, exploitable disadvantages are Sin-Eaters and Mummies.<br /> <br /> Yeah, humans don't really have many powers (although supernatural humans do exist), but they also don't have any glaring weak points. A werewolf pack is scary unless you have a few silver-lined grenades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T13:18:17-07:00","id":1107732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107726#post1107726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People also seem to be kind of glossing over the biggesty, and most clear advantage that Humans have over supernaturals: They don't have a lot of weaknesses. Wolves have silver, Mages have Paradox, vampires are comatose for hours at a time and burn under the light of something that's overhead for about 50% of the time, Prometheans and Vampires both share a weakness to fire, Demons have to contend with the God-Machine, the God-Machine has to contend with its own madness and incompetence, Changelings have to worry about maintaining their Bulwark and Hunntsmen in general, Beasts need to feed and have a whole class of people who are naturally predisposed to find, weaken and kill them, and so on.<br /> <br /> Really, the only major splats that don't have a clear, exploitable disadvantages are Sin-Eaters and Mummies.<br /> <br /> Yeah, humans don't really have many powers (although supernatural humans do exist), but they also don't have any glaring weak points. A werewolf pack is scary unless you have a few silver-lined grenades.</div> </div> </div> </div>They actually already covered that in the post before this one, that's connected by the hyperlink. Supernaturals have supernatural weaknesses, but in exchange they lose a lot of the common weaknesses that humans have. Yes, fire burns a vampire more and sunlight will kill them, but they can take a bullet to the head and laugh at it. A human can't. Moreover, a single bullet might not kill a human, but can have crippling permanent damage. A vampire's going to eventually recover from the fire if they survive, but a human who took a shot to the knee might never be the same again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T13:46:19-07:00","id":1107747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107636#post1107636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I were to hazard a guess, I'd say it's a thinly disguised humanism vs posthumanism argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's exactly what this argument is. It's dressed up with logistical warfare questions, but basically we might as well just ask &quot;would you want to stay human or gain one of the templates?&quot;<br /> <br /> I think people know my stance on that by now, as an aside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T14:41:24-07:00","id":1107765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107747#post1107747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's exactly what this argument is. It's dressed up with logistical warfare questions, but basically we might as well just ask &amp;quot;would you want to stay human or gain one of the templates?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I think people know my stance on that by now, as an aside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I preferred the open arguments about it over beating around the bush like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T15:06:26-07:00","id":1107768,"title":"","content":"*Whispers: &quot;Also Palpatine surviving the fall is no longer Canon. It's part of the Star Wars Legends lore limbo so until otherwise stated it's apocryphal at best...&quot;*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T15:15:25-07:00","id":1107770,"title":"","content":"Quite a few supernaturals would side with humans in a conflict. How many vampires would be willing to make concessions to keep their loved ones? Prometheans <i>want</i> to become human. Demons often have ties to mortals. Mages and Geists, despite all their powerful magic and supernatural abilities, are still living, breathing, humans (mages less so, but still).<br /> <br /> In a fight between supernaturals and humans, humans would win. Not just because of things like bombs and stuff (mages have answers for those, and many splats are ingrained in human society). No, they would win because, in the grand scheme of things, most of their own kind don't want humans to die (that's not even getting into the fact that mages are weaker around humans, vampires and geists need them for survival, etc).<br /> <br /> A 'Chronicles of Darkness: World War Unmasqued' setting would be neat. A world where supernaturals have been revealed, and there are dozens of groups, each with different ideas of how it should be dealt with... all the while, there is a war going on. I would totally buy that book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","name":"Belac93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10751_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T16:26:03-07:00","id":1107789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107726#post1107726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, humans don't really have many powers (although supernatural humans do exist), but they also don't have any glaring weak points. A werewolf pack is scary unless you have a few silver-lined grenades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note: The heat produced by a High Explosive charge, like a normal frag grenade, would make the silver unable to penetrate anything. It'd burn a bit tho. And I mean silver pure enough to actually inflict grievous wounds on Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 06-25-2017, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T16:34:20-07:00","id":1107794,"title":"","content":"* peeks in expecting a debate about how humans relate to the supernatural world<br /> * sees another aspect of the transhumanism vs. humanism topic<br /> * leaves","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T16:39:21-07:00","id":1107798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107709#post1107709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's because humans evolve the fastest during any time of war, especially when they have something to hate - or fear. It's because humans haven't yet captured a werewolf and put them into a lab to study all the most effective ways in which to utilize silver to kill them, easily and efficiently without killing normal humans. It's because no one's studied what kind of UV ray lights are required to sear a vampire into ash and publicized that information to put it into a standard for a city's street lights. It's because 'raw numbers' isn't a feature of strength, but of the raw number of ideas that people can come up with to eliminate their enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find myself thinking about Hunter when I read this. No coincidence, either, because that's the gameline that's geared towards humans opposing monsters. It's worth noting, though, that in ChroD hunters are the exceptions to the mass of humanity we react to the monsters by emulating ostriches. It's also worth noting Dave Brookshaw's stated opinion about mages vs. hunters (short form: hunters would get trounced). Basically, regular humans have their own weakness in the ChroD; and it's a doozy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: of course, a case could be made that the designers gave humanity that handicap because without it, the monsters would be hunted to extinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-25-2017, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T18:28:54-07:00","id":1107833,"title":"","content":"Honestly? In a one-on-one <i>anything</i>, a human is likely to lose. I mean, just look at all those hyper-intelligent, hyper-powerful superbeings that they're competing with!<br /> <br /> Actually, wait a second: since when was this a competition? Last time I checked, Misty Mage had a crush on Sam Sleepwalker, Vinny Vampire still hangs around to see that his kids are doing alright, Wally Werewolf was happy to have mortals in his pack, and Petra Promethean wanted to be a real girl.<br /> <br /> Because, honestly, for all of their power, baseline humans have something important that they don't.<br /> <br /> And that's <i>stability</i>.<br /> <br /> To quote something (granted, this is for Unknown Armies, but it's pretty relevant):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greg Stolze</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things the Freak can do that you can't: Go into a gunfight bare-handed and confident. Shift appearance. Make money rapidly by selling psychic surgery. Kill with minimal effort.<br /> <br /> Things the Freak can't do that you can: Have friends. Trust. Look at its own face in the mirror without psychological effort.<br /> <br /> -G.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T18:58:46-07:00","id":1107847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belac93</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107770#post1107770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite a few supernaturals would side with humans in a conflict. How many vampires would be willing to make concessions to keep their loved ones? Prometheans <i>want</i> to become human. Demons often have ties to mortals. Mages and Geists, despite all their powerful magic and supernatural abilities, are still living, breathing, humans (mages less so, but still).<br /> <br /> In a fight between supernaturals and humans, humans would win. Not just because of things like bombs and stuff (mages have answers for those, and many splats are ingrained in human society). No, they would win because, in the grand scheme of things, most of their own kind don't want humans to die (that's not even getting into the fact that mages are weaker around humans, vampires and geists need them for survival, etc).<br /> <br /> A 'Chronicles of Darkness: World War Unmasqued' setting would be neat. A world where supernaturals have been revealed, and there are dozens of groups, each with different ideas of how it should be dealt with... all the while, there is a war going on. I would totally buy that book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This was covered in the previous thread. And sure, some of them might side with / need humanity to survive, but that doesn't mean they all do.<br /> <br /> Also, you're looking at the monsters from the point of view of the (anti) hero side of things. Remember that most (if not all) of the splats have a few factions who couldn't give a shit about humanity.<br /> <br /> So saying that most of the splats want to keep humans around is inaccurate.<br /> <br /> Rather, it's more appropriate to say <b>certain groups</b> within the splats want to keep humanity around<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T21:04:06-07:00","id":1107875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107847#post1107847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This was covered in the previous thread. And sure, some of them might side with / need humanity to survive, but that doesn't mean they all do.<br /> <br /> Also, you're looking at the monsters from the point of view of the (anti) hero side of things. Remember that most (if not all) of the splats have a few factions who couldn't give a shit about humanity.<br /> <br /> So saying that most of the splats want to keep humans around is inaccurate.<br /> <br /> Rather, it's more appropriate to say <b>certain groups</b> within the splats want to keep humanity around<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. But, here are my estimates for who wants to keep humans around:<br /> <br /> 99% of vampires (which I believe are the most common supernaturals, and need humans)<br /> 15% of all werewolves (half the ones who do what they're supposed to)<br /> 50% of prometheans (they want to be human)<br /> 80% of sin-eaters (they were human, and still are very similar)<br /> 15% of mages (being cynical here, it's almost certainly more)<br /> 80% of demons (as a whole, they have strong connections with humans, and need them to hide from the god-machine)<br /> 50% of beasts (they generally need humans)<br /> 15% of changelings (they also need humans, to a lesser degree, and like them. Although a lot probably wouldn't care.)<br /> 5% of mummies (dunno much about them, but I don't think they would care a lot either way)<br /> <br /> Even with all that, that's 45.44% of all supernaturals (excluding antagonists, template merits, and hunters). It's not the majority, but this also isn't taking into account the fact that things like mummies are way less plentiful than things like vampires, so their 5% doesn't matter nearly as much as the vampire's 99% (aside from the fact that mummies are more powerful).<br /> <br /> Sure, they might not want to keep humanity as a whole around. But keeping their touchstones and families safe? I think that would be enough for them to at least stand out of the fight.<br /> <br /> Not all of them would, sure. But enough supernaturals are going to care enough about people that they'll at least take a neutral stance in a fight between the two. All supernaturals (with the possible exception of mummies, I don't know a lot about them), have a significant portion of their population who at least has a human friend they'll fight to protect, if not actively protecting humans as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","name":"Belac93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10751_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T21:24:43-07:00","id":1107880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belac93</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107875#post1107875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough. But, here are my estimates for who wants to keep humans around:<br /> <br /> 99% of vampires (which I believe are the most common supernaturals, and need humans)<br /> 15% of all werewolves (half the ones who do what they're supposed to)<br /> 50% of prometheans (they want to be human)<br /> 80% of sin-eaters (they were human, and still are very similar)<br /> 15% of mages (being cynical here, it's almost certainly more)<br /> 80% of demons (as a whole, they have strong connections with humans, and need them to hide from the god-machine)<br /> 50% of beasts (they generally need humans)<br /> 15% of changelings (they also need humans, to a lesser degree, and like them. Although a lot probably wouldn't care.)<br /> 5% of mummies (dunno much about them, but I don't think they would care a lot either way)<br /> <br /> Even with all that, that's 45.44% of all supernaturals (excluding antagonists, template merits, and hunters). It's not the majority, but this also isn't taking into account the fact that things like mummies are way less plentiful than things like vampires, so their 5% doesn't matter nearly as much as the vampire's 99% (aside from the fact that mummies are more powerful).<br /> <br /> Sure, they might not want to keep humanity as a whole around. But keeping their touchstones and families safe? I think that would be enough for them to at least stand out of the fight.<br /> <br /> Not all of them would, sure. But enough supernaturals are going to care enough about people that they'll at least take a neutral stance in a fight between the two. All supernaturals (with the possible exception of mummies, I don't know a lot about them), have a significant portion of their population who at least has a human friend they'll fight to protect, if not actively protecting humans as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go quite a bit higher on Mages, probably bump Beasts up a little, and probably increase Changelings.<br /> <br /> Mages, in general, want and often <i>need</i> normies around. Without normal humans, there's nobody to run their anciallary cults and far fewer grunt-level mystics in the Orders, since, as I understand, 2E has a lot more non-Mage magicians in the Orders now. The Exarchs want mortals to rule over, The Silver Ladder wants mortals to rule over (totes benevolently we swear), and the Libertines are an entire Order of &quot;Humanity, FUCK YEAH.&quot;<br /> <br /> Beasts kind of <i>need</i> humans to exist, considering they exist withing the human gestalt of the Temenos. Allowing humanity to die out would likely render the Beasts extinct, or make them into something like the Insatiates.<br /> <br /> Changelings need humans to help them keep a grip on reality, and I'm sure quite a few Freeholds place some importance on human interaction, and may also put them into their Bulwarks. Personally, if I were a Changeling, I'd probably try to kepp to humanity, even if only to try and stop a human from gettingdragged off by Gentry, but that's just me.<br /> <br /> I might also knock Sin-Eaters up to 90%, just because human extinction means a shitload of ghosts, of varying levels of unfriendliness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T21:24:46-07:00","id":1107881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belac93</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107875#post1107875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5% of mummies (dunno much about them, but I don't think they would care a lot either way)<br /> <br /> Not all of them would, sure. But enough supernaturals are going to care enough about people that they'll at least take a neutral stance in a fight between the two. All supernaturals (with the possible exception of mummies, I don't know a lot about them), have a significant portion of their population who at least has a human friend they'll fight to protect, if not actively protecting humans as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummies would, in my opinion, be almost 100% on the side of humans. Everything about them revolves around humans. They are worshipped by human cultists, who provide the easiest ways for Mummies to become active. Their mission in, ahem, life, is to retrieve relics and deliver them to the Judges of Duat. Humans make those relics, Mummies explicitly can't. Those rare Mummies who want to throw off their shackles, free their cults, and abandon their purpose want to achieve an Apotheosis that brings them <i>closer</i> to humanity, rather than separate them.<br /> <br /> And that's all just what happens of the Mummy's own volition. When a Mummy is raised by a cultist it is the cultist, the human, who gives the Mummy their mission. These cultists are normally indoctrinated in the mythology of Irem, or whatever is convenient to the Mummy, so that the order given is what aligns with the Mummy's purpose, but I'm sure the overwhelming majority of human cultists when threatened with extinction would go to their god and beg them for help. And if a newly woken Mummy is good at anything, it's mindlessly following such tasks.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107726#post1107726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, the only major splats that don't have a clear, exploitable disadvantages are Sin-Eaters and Mummies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, the part of the Mummy Diasporic Code that addresses going public with the existence of Mummies (&quot;Grasp not the sunlit flail&quot;, a code that says Mummies should never publicly rule humans) is basically because it's just a whole lot easier for Mummies to do what they're meant to do if humans aren't aware of them. It's real hard to be a ruler if you're only able to boss people around in person every other decade or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T22:59:16-07:00","id":1107906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107880#post1107880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd go quite a bit higher on Mages, probably bump Beasts up a little, and probably increase Changelings.<br /> <br /> Mages, in general, want and often <i>need</i> normies around. Without normal humans, there's nobody to run their anciallary cults and far fewer grunt-level mystics in the Orders, since, as I understand, 2E has a lot more non-Mage magicians in the Orders now. The Exarchs want mortals to rule over, The Silver Ladder wants mortals to rule over (totes benevolently we swear), and the Libertines are an entire Order of &quot;Humanity, FUCK YEAH.&quot;<br /> <br /> Beasts kind of <i>need</i> humans to exist, considering they exist withing the human gestalt of the Temenos. Allowing humanity to die out would likely render the Beasts extinct, or make them into something like the Insatiates.<br /> <br /> Changelings need humans to help them keep a grip on reality, and I'm sure quite a few Freeholds place some importance on human interaction, and may also put them into their Bulwarks. Personally, if I were a Changeling, I'd probably try to kepp to humanity, even if only to try and stop a human from gettingdragged off by Gentry, but that's just me.<br /> <br /> I might also knock Sin-Eaters up to 90%, just because human extinction means a shitload of ghosts, of varying levels of unfriendliness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also, I wasn't suggesting that monsters should whole sale slaughter humanity, nor that they should cast aside their beliefs / customs. I'm saying that humanity <b>as a species</b> (not a culture) is overrated.<br /> <br /> Why wouldn't somebody choose to become one of the supernatural splats if they were still able to retain their personalities after the transformation was complete? Heck, vampires even have an entire covenant who are dedicated to overcoming the weaknesses of vampirism. Meaning that you could gain all the benefits and none of the drawbacks (<i>theoretically</i>)!<br /> <br /> <br /> Not gonna argue about Prometheans, because I honestly don't know how to approach the subject. I know they want to become humans, but I do not understand why. Apparently it has something to do with them not fitting in with humanity because people get freaked out when they hang around for too long? They're trying to imitate something that they're not, just so they can feel accepted by a group of people who hate and ridicule them. In real life, this is a horrible message to teach, and the proper course of action should be to look for people who will accept you for who you are... <i>such as your fellow supernaturals.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> The only splat I can see that makes any kind of sense on why they'd want to reclaim their humanity is the Changelings. The vast majority of them didn't exactly have any say in the matter and they're being constantly hunted by Lovecraftian slave owners who want to do things to them that makes reality itself have a stroke. Also, without humans, they can't harvest glamour, which they need to defend themselves against being captured again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Oh, and Sin Eaters, too, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-26-2017, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T23:08:03-07:00","id":1107909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107906#post1107906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not gonna argue about Prometheans, because I honestly don't know how to approach the subject. I know they want to become humans, but I do not understand why. Apparently it has something to do with them not fitting in with humanity because people get freaked out when they hang around for too long? They're trying to imitate something that they're not, just so they can feel accepted by a group of people who hate and ridicule them. In real life, this is a horrible message to teach, and the proper course of action should be to look for people who will accept you for who you are... <i>such as your fellow supernaturals.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Supernaturals are affected by Disquiet too, so that doesn't actually help.<br /> <br /> The central message of Promethean is difficult for me too, because it is very easy to look at it the wrong way and get exactly that message out of it. I don't believe that's the way that the metaphor is meant to be taken. Prometheans though are incomplete, and their myriad problems arise from that unfinished nature. They aren't hated for their difference, but because they aren't yet done. If I had to relate it to any single metaphor I would connect it to the experience of growing up. You can't stay a child forever, and attempting to do so can have horrible consequences and cause people to turn on you. What Promethean does explicitly empower you to do is decide what kind of adult you want to be. You don't need to grow up to become normal, a suburbanite middle class white man with a wife and 2.5 children, but you do need to grow up to be human.<br /> <br /> Since the various effects of being a Promethean cause real and tangible harm to everyone around them (both subjecting them to involuntary mind control that makes them hate the Promethean and physically corrupting the land in ways that can cause actual injury to people) then remaining as one does strike me as unconscionable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T23:20:20-07:00","id":1107913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107906#post1107906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't somebody choose to become one of the supernatural splats if they were still able to retain their personalities after the transformation was complete?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because doing so means God is real and wants to fuck with you for an art project. High-stakes gambling with your autonomy on a regular basis is not most people's idea of a good time.*<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* That many mages might consider it such while in the gap between functional and desperate addiction is a huge part of why the splat is rightly considered a bunch of dangerous assholes.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T23:55:38-07:00","id":1107919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107913#post1107913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because doing so means God is real and wants to fuck with you for an art project. High-stakes gambling with your autonomy on a regular basis is not most people's idea of a good time.*<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* That many mages might consider it such while in the gap between functional and desperate addiction is a huge part of why the splat is rightly considered a bunch of dangerous assholes.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeahhhh, I never agreed with that way of thinking. &quot;Oh, vampires are real. I guess that means God is, too!&quot;<br /> <br /> Finding evidence of vampires is proof of the existence of vampires. It is NOT proof in the existence of a totally unrelated entity.<br /> <br /> Even if it was, we literally have millions (possibly billions?) of deities scattered across human culture. Many of which would be perfectly okay with you being a monster, so long as you didn't go around doing anything too stupid.<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Sadly, I know practically nothing about Promethean aside from them being artificial humans without a soul of their own. I know that bad shit happens if they hang around for too long, but I don't know any specific details beyond that.<br /> <br /> But if they're a danger to everybody (supes included), then I could understand their reasons for wanting to fix their problem; since nobody is safe in the mean time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T00:36:58-07:00","id":1107927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107919#post1107919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Yeahhhh, I never agreed with that way of thinking. &quot;Oh, vampires are real. I guess that means God is, too!&quot;<br /> <br /> Finding evidence of vampires is proof of the existence of vampires. It is NOT proof in the existence of a totally unrelated entity.<br /> <br /> Even if it was, we literally have millions (possibly billions?) of deities scattered across human culture. Many of which would be perfectly okay with you being a monster, so long as you didn't go around doing anything too stupid.<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Sadly, I know practically nothing about Promethean aside from them being artificial humans without a soul of their own. I know that bad shit happens if they hang around for too long, but I don't know any specific details beyond that.<br /> <br /> But if they're a danger to everybody (supes included), then I could understand their reasons for wanting to fix their problem; since nobody is safe in the mean time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need the Christian God for the Curses to be a suitable stand-in, and that's before you account for groups like the Circle of the Crone who literally summon gods every once in a while.<br /> <br /> Even if changelings weren't made by the psychotic man-children that are the Gentry, they are literally powered by a force that might as well be a god and therefore cannot avoid suffering under the ebb and flow of the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> You don't need a Christian God in a world where Luna brands people, the Exarchs are the ones most likely fiddling with your existence, the Principle burns villages because you just don't fucking get humanity, Death has a thousand faces and million ideas bout what your afterlife should be like, Literal Fucking Judges think you aren't Suffering enough and Ammut isn't getting enough food and drink, and the vast towering hunger over existence chewing on reality in the form of the Dark Mother, and none of that accounts for the literal God whose biggest beef with the Bible is probably that the Old Testament portrayal wasn't brutally efficient enough. And that's just the biggest tier things along the gamelines, never mind the vast forces that don't fit into those neat boxes or the fact that there are literally thousands of millions equivalents of household gods, ancestor spirits, and more along those lines that, while maybe not what the Western world is used ot thinking of as gods anymore, can never the less effectively be the god of your small and limited world.<br /> <br /> The Chronicles world is <i>lousy</i> with gods and forces that behave like gods, and <i>none of them</i> are exactly things a sane individual wants to have sticking their fingers into their eyes, ears, and up their asses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T04:19:28-07:00","id":1107966,"title":"","content":"I'm one of the people that sees this thread and thinks: &quot;False Choice. They're all humans except Prometheans and Demons.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, you want to start arguing about humanity versus the God-Machine or Exarchs or destroying the True Fae? I'm down with that (humans lose). But the PC splats? They're all just variations of humanity (except created/unchained) with a bit extra. They're defined by humans exposed to something else. They're written to tell very human stories. That's how we relate to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-26-2017, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T10:37:17-07:00","id":1108066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107966#post1107966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm one of the people that sees this thread and thinks: &quot;False Choice. They're all humans except Prometheans and Demons.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, you want to start arguing about humanity versus the God-Machine or Exarchs or destroying the True Fae? I'm down with that (humans lose). But the PC splats? They're all just variations of humanity (except created/unchained) with a bit extra. They're defined by humans exposed to something else. They're written to tell very human stories. That's how we relate to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the Machine, the Exarchs, and the Strangers are all variations of humanity, due to certain origins as fictional constructs.<br /> <br /> Gods are always in service to humanity, seeing as we create them for just that reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T11:50:04-07:00","id":1108087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107906#post1107906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't somebody choose to become one of the supernatural splats if they were still able to retain their personalities after the transformation was complete? Heck, vampires even have an entire covenant who are dedicated to overcoming the weaknesses of vampirism. Meaning that you could gain all the benefits and none of the drawbacks (<i>theoretically</i>)!</div> </div> </div> </div>And, there it is. Yeah, I'm really, <i>really</i> fed up with having this argument. But I'd rather have it directly than dance around the issue by talking about pointless stuff like who would win in a fight or who would side with humans in a war.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107906#post1107906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not gonna argue about Prometheans, because I honestly don't know how to approach the subject. I know they want to become humans, but I do not understand why. Apparently it has something to do with them not fitting in with humanity because people get freaked out when they hang around for too long? They're trying to imitate something that they're not, just so they can feel accepted by a group of people who hate and ridicule them. In real life, this is a horrible message to teach, and the proper course of action should be to look for people who will accept you for who you are... <i>such as your fellow supernaturals.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Disquiet affects other supernaturals too. But beyond that, it's not just a matter of fitting in, it's a matter of being okay with <i>yourself</i>. Disquiet is only half the story. (Less than half the story, actually, it's an unpleasant secondary effect of half the story, which is that the Promethean's animating force is harmful to the World around it. But I digress.) The other half is Torment. Promethean is about not being okay with what your creator made you to be, and finding a way to become something you are okay with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107906#post1107906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only splat I can see that makes any kind of sense on why they'd want to reclaim their humanity is the Changelings. The vast majority of them didn't exactly have any say in the matter and they're being constantly hunted by Lovecraftian slave owners who want to do things to them that makes reality itself have a stroke. Also, without humans, they can't harvest glamour, which they need to defend themselves against being captured again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Oh, and Sin Eaters, too, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine, you don't have to get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T13:10:20-07:00","id":1108123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107847#post1107847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So saying that most of the splats want to keep humans around is inaccurate.<br /> <br /> Rather, it's more appropriate to say <b>certain groups</b> within the splats want to keep humanity around<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Saying that the splats as a whole would benefit or wish humanity's extinction, beyond misguided fanatism, is also inaccurate and simplistic, bordering on a strawman argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T13:36:40-07:00","id":1108130,"title":"","content":"Not wanting for humanity to disappear might be the most notable point of agreement between Pentacle and Seers since &quot;magic is cool&quot;, just to say one<br /> <br /> As for the other splats, I can't think of even one as a whole that would not prefer for humanity to be there (and that's counting even almost all the the antagonists). I mean, even those who feed on it, have fun playing with humanity or obtain powers from its dark urges will still want mankind around. Even several Idigams and Abyssals cultists would rather avoid humanity's extinction .The <b>certain groups </b>notion you propose is the inaccurate one, sorry.<br /> <br /> And that's by merely speaking in immediate, practical terms, not even going for more philosophical, nuanced or metaphorical approaches to the topic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-26-2017, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T14:33:15-07:00","id":1108146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108123#post1108123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Saying that the splats as a whole would benefit or wish humanity's extinction, beyond misguided fanatism, is also inaccurate and simplistic, bordering on a strawman argument.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I wasn't saying that. In fact, I've stated at least twice that I wasn't advocating the supernaturals wipe humanity out. I was just stating how they're typically superior as a species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T14:46:49-07:00","id":1108153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108146#post1108146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't saying that. In fact, I've stated at least twice that I wasn't advocating the supernaturals wipe humanity out. I was just stating how they're typically superior as a species.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the credit of those misinterpreting you, your core thesis is pretty weird -<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107494#post1107494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in short, humanity is overrated, and their superiority is a work of popular fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>The existence of other intelligent entities for humans to be superior to is itself a work of fiction, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T14:51:29-07:00","id":1108158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108153#post1108153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The existence of other intelligent entities for humans to be superior to is itself a work of fiction, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T15:10:15-07:00","id":1108164,"title":"","content":"Probably because I was more of a lurker until recently and generally avoided the transhumanism topics as a whole, but I'm sincerely having issues wrapping my head around the arguments you're using to support your idea.<br /> <br /> Might be because I fundamentally disagree with it and my ability to get into different perspectives is failing me at the moment, might be because I made mistakes while reading or even that I I'm in the middle of exams days and the stress is killing my brain, but I'd rather fade away than cluttering the discussion with my nonsense.<br /> <br /> Apologies for not giving at least a valid contribution to this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T15:19:07-07:00","id":1108165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107919#post1107919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeahhhh, I never agreed with that way of thinking. &quot;Oh, vampires are real. I guess that means God is, too!&quot;<br /> <br /> Finding evidence of vampires is proof of the existence of vampires. It is NOT proof in the existence of a totally unrelated entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pay attention to what becoming a monster entails, because the &quot;God&quot; I'm talking about is the furthest thing from totally unrelated. This isn't &quot;if aliens, then Jesus,&quot; it's &quot;if Prometheans, then Pyros.&quot;<br /> <br /> You keep bringing up the Ordo Dracul as though the Defiant didn't have an institutional taboo against bending the knee to other monsters and an organizational framework of &quot;pursue power for the practical reasons of gaining full immortality to spite God.&quot; The base state of the Curse is not an uplifting one and the means of converting it thus are squirreled away in the esoteric cracks of bloody sacrifice and human folly rather than healthy boundaries and the refinement of skill.<br /> <br /> Supernatural entities are plagued with the need for a driving purpose in a way that mortals aren't \u2014 the balancing act between intelligent consciousness and the ruinous energies of your power is a series of dangerous trades that only come up through immersion in an ecosystem that gradually disintegrates human self-concept.<br /> <br /> One does not lose their vulnerability to fire without a great deal of burning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T15:30:09-07:00","id":1108168,"title":"","content":"The original reason why I got into the New World of Darkness (before it turned into Chronicles), as opposed to the old one, was that it didn't drum the &quot;humanity is inherently powerless and worthless&quot; message quite as hard. The existence of Hunter: the Vigil, which would never work in oWoD, was a major part of this. Chronicles has of course never got close to oWoD's derisive treatment of humans, but it does seem to move back towards their being powerless and helpless in face of the supernatural. We'll see how Vigil 2e tackles this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T15:52:30-07:00","id":1108174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1107906#post1107906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't somebody choose to become one of the supernatural splats if they were still able to retain their personalities after the transformation was complete?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I don't resent my flesh or flaws, and don't think embracing any of the variations of more literal predacity will actually lead to a happier, fuller life?<br /> <br /> Like, I'm down for arguing for transhumanism and posthumanism, but the Chronicles splats are <i>not</i> where I'd go for that fix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T16:01:15-07:00","id":1108178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108174#post1108174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, I'm down for arguing for transhumanism and posthumanism, but the Chronicles splats are <i>not</i> where I'd go for that fix.</div> </div> </div> </div>This pretty much sums up my attitude as well, at least regarding the various forms of supernatural transcendence in the Chronicles.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah of course I'd go for immortality and reality-warping powers... <i>if they don't come with any strings attached</i>. And considering what those strings tend to look like and where they come from in the Chronicles... I'd rather play it safe and stay human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T19:30:29-07:00","id":1108230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108165#post1108165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pay attention to what becoming a monster entails, because the &quot;God&quot; I'm talking about is the furthest thing from totally unrelated. This isn't &quot;if aliens, then Jesus,&quot; it's &quot;if Prometheans, then Pyros.&quot;<br /> <br /> You keep bringing up the Ordo Dracul as though the Defiant didn't have an institutional taboo against bending the knee to other monsters and an organizational framework of &quot;pursue power for the practical reasons of gaining full immortality to spite God.&quot; The base state of the Curse is not an uplifting one and the means of converting it thus are squirreled away in the esoteric cracks of bloody sacrifice and human folly rather than healthy boundaries and the refinement of skill.<br /> <br /> Supernatural entities are plagued with the need for a driving purpose in a way that mortals aren't \u2014 the balancing act between intelligent consciousness and the ruinous energies of your power is a series of dangerous trades that only come up through immersion in an ecosystem that gradually disintegrates human self-concept.<br /> <br /> One does not lose their vulnerability to fire without a great deal of burning.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, I only brought up the Ordo Dracul once (in this thread, anyways). But just to clarify, I don't have any of the expanded material books, the core books alone are already pretty steeply priced for my budget. So whatever information is recorded in the basic rules is the information that I go with. From the sound of it, the Ordo are something along the lines of scientific inclined monks.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------<br /> <br /> As for 21C Hermit, that's probably my take on it, too. If it didn't come with so much drama, there's several splats I'd be somewhat happy with. Like I said, I'm arguing about humanity as a species, not humanity as a society. But I've also noticed that much of the drama comes from outside forces who won't leave them alone, as opposed to a direct result of being what they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T20:05:56-07:00","id":1108243,"title":"","content":"I feel like we need to have Humanity defined in this discussion if we want to discuss whether it is overrated or not. If we're excluding all supernaturals from the humanity definition, then that'd make humanity pretty underrated in my book. Surviving through war, plague, famine, and the like is pretty impressive.<br /> <br /> However, in my personal opinion, the umbrella of humanity should include most of the splats because most of the splats still have very human urges, and every chronicle is generally about people with these very human urges.<br /> <br /> I also fail to see why there would be some large scale war. Sure, both sides have their members that would prefer outright destruction of the other side, but I feel like most splats wouldn't be on board, and there would be dozens of monster rights activists, and the UN would have to get involved because of all the potential human rights violations.<br /> <br /> I just think it'd be a waste to observe only the violence of a world with a masquerade torn down rather than every potential aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T21:27:28-07:00","id":1108257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108230#post1108230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, I'm arguing about humanity as a species, not humanity as a society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's the mistake in this line of thought. We don't have natural weaponry, we have culture which is shaped by our intellect (and vice-versa). That's like attempting to examine a declawed lion without a pride objectively, somehow expecting it to survive like one with those advantages would.<br /> <br /> Otherwise the argument boils down to &quot;Yes, people generally can't open a tank barehanded like it was a mere can (check out the new exoskeleton suits we're developing for that tho), unlike some monsters could&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T21:47:52-07:00","id":1108267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108230#post1108230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for 21C Hermit, that's probably my take on it, too. If it didn't come with so much drama, there's several splats I'd be somewhat happy with. Like I said, I'm arguing about humanity as a species, not humanity as a society. But I've also noticed that much of the drama comes from outside forces who won't leave them alone, as opposed to a direct result of being what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still not sure. All of the monsters have some serious built-in issues that originate from not just their society but their very own supernatural nature that make me think twice about joining them. In fact, most of the monsters' societal structure come from trying to dance around those internal issues.<br /> <br /> Vampires have the Beast urging them to abandon their decency. Which is why their society is riddled with rules, traditions, and etiquette. All those things help to reign in the Beast and at least act like functioning people. The Covenants also give them something to keep them occupied, and something to live worth for, besides the three Fs. (fighting, feeding, fucking)<br /> Werewolves are urged to live a life of hunting, and to keep a precarious balance between their flesh and spirit halves. Which is why their society revolves around compact units geared for the hunt, made of people whom you can trust your backs on. The Tribes also give them a purpose to their hunt, making it truly Sacred.<br /> Mages are overloaded on the signals that the supernatural aspects of the world send and are obsessed in tracking them down and solving them, collateral damage be damned. Their Orders give them something to focus upon and the resources to safely pursue them. And because their brand of magic is so effective at killing people with enough ingenuity, their society tend to look like extended judiciary systems.<br /> <br /> I won't go over every splat, but that's how it is. The monsters aren't some tragic drama figures hounded by malevolent outside factors. They are monsters, and their monstrous nature is what causes havoc around them.<br /> <br /> I assume you were talking about factors such as the Strix and the Idigam when talking about outside forces who won't leave the monsters alone? The Huntsmen, the servants of Ammut, the Insatiables? Yes, those beings cause drama... some times. They give the monsters someone to blame, sure. But... would the monsters be any different without them? Vampires still eat people, werewolves still must hunt, mages still wreck havoc with their magic, changelings still manipulate people, mummies still worship the Judges and create cults, Beasts still... you know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T21:59:20-07:00","id":1108271,"title":"","content":"For the record: Nobody is arguing that being naturally able to emulate a slasher/medium/wizard like some werewolves, vampires and mages could wouldn't be cool, in the rule of cool type of trope. I'm just wondering why we're even discussing as if the argument didn't boiled down to &quot;The sky is blue most of the day, isn't that nice?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T22:58:04-07:00","id":1108289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108257#post1108257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Otherwise the argument boils down to &quot;Yes, people generally can't open a tank barehanded like it was a mere can (check out the new exoskeleton suits we're developing for that tho).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dearly want to, now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> --------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Ever Professional:</b> Once again; humanity <b>as a species</b> being overrated compared to the supernatural splats. Discussing their biology and physiology, as well as levels of psychology, mental capacity, and technological capabilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> In just about every category (except Psychology), humanity is either hopelessly outclassed, or manages to come up equal. The monsters can be just as intelligent as humans, if not more so because they know / comprehend things about the world humans have very little exposure to, many of them also have drastically increased life spans to acquire more knowledge and experience.<br /> <br /> Technologically, anything that humans are capable of manufacturing / wielding, the supernaturals are able to do the same thing. Becoming a monster doesn't make you instantly suffer amnesia about your existence as a human<br /> <br /> Unless you're a mummy... but that's only one particular splat.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Not trying to come across as rude or angry, just want to say that I keep having to repeat myself about this. We are discussing humanity as a physical entity.<br /> <br /> Not as a culture, not as a philosophy, not as a religion or anything metaphysical like that. We're comparing the physical existence of being human in comparison to being a supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T23:40:06-07:00","id":1108301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108289#post1108289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becoming a monster doesn't make you instantly suffer amnesia about your existence as a human</div> </div> </div> </div>The already-low number of Secret Revolutionary Supergeniuses claimed by the various generally exposure-shy strains of monstrosity has its effectiveness skewed lower by the internal and external complications such a state-change affects \u2014 immortality doesn't keep the lights on, drawing directly from the well of aggregated human knowledge isn't an innate source of novel inspiration, and the realities of opportunity cost mean most immortal characters are going to either prioritize their logistical security and emotional well-being over probing the bleeding edge of cultural breakthroughs or personally make new discoveries that they have no capacity or inclination to share.<br /> <br /> The kind of focus necessary to keep ahead of the curve in an ever-advancing body of work without breaking to manage your regular upkeep is the domain of automatons even before addressing the veil of shaken perspective walling you off from mortal society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T23:40:50-07:00","id":1108302,"title":"","content":"I'm not entirely sure why we're excluding most of humanity's strengths in this debate. Based upon just physical capabilities of course the supernatural side has the advantage, but humanity has other capabilities beyond the physical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T23:55:12-07:00","id":1108308,"title":"","content":"so heres the thing you cant forget humanity as a culture or philosophy those are things that are being part of humans as species there part of us so we have to take it into account<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T00:29:13-07:00","id":1108314,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108289#post1108289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not trying to come across as rude or angry, just want to say that I keep having to repeat myself about this. We are discussing humanity as a physical entity.<br /> <br /> Not as a culture, not as a philosophy, not as a religion or anything metaphysical like that. We're comparing the physical existence of being human in comparison to being a supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is now starting to get really confusing here. As people have said - culture is one of humanities strongest points. Technology is culture. Sociology is culture. You brought up culture yourself when you involved the Ordo Dracul (which is a culture, philosophy, and arguably a religion of Vampires). What is it exactly we are comparing here to define that one group is superior? Because it seems to me by the logic we're going turtles are a superior race to humans because they live longer, they bite harder, and their shells are hard as hell to break when compared to humans weak, fleshy skin and therefore we should all opt to be turtley enough to join the turtle club.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 06-27-2017, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T01:24:33-07:00","id":1108317,"title":"","content":"^ seriously.<br /> <br /> (although, to be honest, who wouldn't want to be in the turtle club?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T02:49:14-07:00","id":1108327,"title":"","content":"turtle club for life","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T08:23:30-07:00","id":1108412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108314#post1108314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> See, this is now starting to get really confusing here. As people have said - culture is one of humanities strongest points. Technology is culture. Sociology is culture. You brought up culture yourself when you involved the Ordo Dracul (which is a culture, philosophy, and arguably a religion of Vampires). What is it exactly we are comparing here to define that one group is superior? Because it seems to me by the logic we're going turtles are a superior race to humans because they live longer, they bite harder, and their shells are hard as hell to break when compared to humans weak, fleshy skin and therefore we should all opt to be turtley enough to join the turtle club.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Turtles are also deaf and mute, which are some pretty nasty disadvantages.<br /> <br /> But yeah, this topic was brought up in the last thread. Humans hold the position that is does in this world completely through artificial means. If you strip a human of their technology and place them butt naked in the wild, chances are that they aren't going to survive against most threats they have to face. But if you do the same thing to one of the supernatural splats, they still have a pretty good chance at survival.<br /> <br /> <br /> Humanity's reliance on artificial enhancements such as weapons, tools and shelter has stripped them of their natural defenses and weapons. A basic human outfitted with nothing but what nature itself has graced them with is fragile, short lived, and woefully incapable of defending itself.<br /> <br /> A supernatural in the same situation is much more capable. The supernaturals don't need technology to survive, they have a potentially limitless variety of physical and mental abilities which can compensate for their lack of such resources. Using technology is merely a convenience for the WoD splats, it's not a necessity; like it is for humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> I honestly don't understand what's difficult to understand about how humans as a species are overrated. People keep bringing up how humans have technology and society on their side; but that is not what I was talking about.<br /> <br /> This isn't an argument about societal structure, it's an argument about eugenics. Many of the supernatural splats are objectively superior to humans, and it is only thanks to excessive population that humans pose a threat.<br /> <br /> <br /> Most of the splat books I've read seem to agree on this issue. They don't care if any one human in particular is trying to kill them. They care if an <i>entire town</i> is trying to kill them, because the legions of humanity will eventually wear them down. I even quoted <b>Zap Brannigan</b> about this subject.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Knowing their weakness, I threw wave after wave of my own men at them. Until they reached their limit and shut down!&quot;</i><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T08:51:32-07:00","id":1108415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108412#post1108412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't understand what's difficult to understand about how humans as a species are overrated. People keep bringing up how humans have technology and society on their side; but that is not what I was talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really it's because of the stacking of the deck in ridiculous fashion. You're claiming that fictional humans have a fictional advantage against a fictional opponent, and backing it up by taking humans from everything that makes them humans and not balancing it out by doing the same with the supernaturals, then making them fight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This isn't an argument about societal structure, it's an argument about eugenics. Many of the supernatural splats are objectively superior to humans, and it is only thanks to excessive population that humans pose a threat. </div> </div> </div>I really don't see how eugenics has anything to do with vampires being naked humans stripped of technology and allies in a fistfight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of the splat books I've read seem to agree on this issue. They don't care if any one human in particular is trying to kill them. They care if an <i>entire town</i> is trying to kill them, because the legions of humanity will eventually wear them down. </div> </div> </div>Not sure where that comes from. Vampires don't care if humanity believes in vampires, they care if they know that Maxwell down the street is a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-27-2017, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T09:31:33-07:00","id":1108428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108412#post1108412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, this topic was brought up in the last thread. Humans hold the position that is does in this world completely through artificial means. If you strip a human of their technology and place them butt naked in the wild, chances are that they aren't going to survive against most threats they have to face. But if you do the same thing to one of the supernatural splats, they still have a pretty good chance at survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>As nofather observes, this is an <i>absurd</i> degree of deck-stacking \u2014 a vampire or a mage with no training in how to hunt is going to be no better at hunting than an equivalent mortal, and if they're similarly unequipped then they're SOL on using most of the things that would help them without lasting cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T09:38:10-07:00","id":1108431,"title":"","content":"I get the feeling that there is an effort here to compare apples and oranges, then trying to determine which of either (apple or orange) makes the best watermelon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T09:43:33-07:00","id":1108432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108412#post1108412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Turtles are also deaf and mute, which are some pretty nasty disadvantages.<br /> <br /> But yeah, this topic was brought up in the last thread. Humans hold the position that is does in this world completely through artificial means. If you strip a human of their technology and place them butt naked in the wild, chances are that they aren't going to survive against most threats they have to face. But if you do the same thing to one of the supernatural splats, they still have a pretty good chance at survival.<br /> <br /> <br /> Humanity's reliance on artificial enhancements such as weapons, tools and shelter has stripped them of their natural defenses and weapons. A basic human outfitted with nothing but what nature itself has graced them with is fragile, short lived, and woefully incapable of defending itself.<br /> <br /> A supernatural in the same situation is much more capable. The supernaturals don't need technology to survive, they have a potentially limitless variety of physical and mental abilities which can compensate for their lack of such resources. Using technology is merely a convenience for the WoD splats, it's not a necessity; like it is for humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> I honestly don't understand what's difficult to understand about how humans as a species are overrated. People keep bringing up how humans have technology and society on their side; but that is not what I was talking about.<br /> <br /> This isn't an argument about societal structure, it's an argument about eugenics. Many of the supernatural splats are objectively superior to humans, and it is only thanks to excessive population that humans pose a threat.<br /> <br /> <br /> Most of the splat books I've read seem to agree on this issue. They don't care if any one human in particular is trying to kill them. They care if an <i>entire town</i> is trying to kill them, because the legions of humanity will eventually wear them down. I even quoted <b>Zap Brannigan</b> about this subject.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Knowing their weakness, I threw wave after wave of my own men at them. Until they reached their limit and shut down!&quot;</i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody is arguing that point, your average world citizen would die horribly if left in the middle of the Amazon River with nay a supply for a prolonged length of time. What we're contesting is what value is in re-stating it over and over and over, like you seem to be doing every other thread. IE, your argument is fallacious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 06-27-2017, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T09:46:30-07:00","id":1108433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108412#post1108412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turtles are also deaf and mute, which are some pretty nasty disadvantages.</div> </div> </div> </div>... This sir is a flat out falsehood :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108412#post1108412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity's reliance on artificial enhancements such as weapons, tools and shelter has stripped them of their natural defenses and weapons. A basic human outfitted with nothing but what nature itself has graced them with is fragile, short lived, and woefully incapable of defending itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also a falsehood. We are not stripped of our natural defenses and weapons. Our mind and ability to adapt -is- our natural defense and weapons, and we use those to create the tools which make us superior. Nature graced us with a mind capable of utilizing scenarios and tools to give ourselves an edge we wouldn't otherwise have. It gave us the ability to communicate and work together. We just improved it over the years. We are still improving. You see - here is the real difference there. Over time, vampires, werewolves, prometheans - -most- supernaturals short of mages (who are humans) don't actually grow as a species . They don't contribute to their races as a whole. They just stay the same, and leech off of humanity's progress.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108412#post1108412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A supernatural in the same situation is much more capable. The supernaturals don't need technology to survive, they have a potentially limitless variety of physical and mental abilities which can compensate for their lack of such resources. Using technology is merely a convenience for the WoD splats, it's not a necessity; like it is for humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not always true. Most vampires I've played would say that a house is not a simple convenience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108412#post1108412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't understand what's difficult to understand about how humans as a species are overrated. People keep bringing up how humans have technology and society on their side; but that is not what I was talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is the thing - when you remove a human's culture, technology, and society - you aren't talking about humans anymore. You are talking about apes and monkeys. That isn't a real discussion. This is starting to sound less like &quot;Humans are overrated&quot; and more like &quot;Humans are overrated compared to other supernaturals if you remove what makes them the superior&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 06-27-2017, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T10:21:52-07:00","id":1108441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108412#post1108412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, this topic was brought up in the last thread. Humans hold the position that is does in this world completely through artificial means. If you strip a human of their technology and place them butt naked in the wild, chances are that they aren't going to survive against most threats they have to face.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't think humanity just sprang up with all of the technology we now use already invented and built, do you? We were, at one point, literally butt naked in the wild with no technology, and look where we are now. The average modern human's inability to survive those conditions is <i>because of our culture</i>. We're no longer used to facing such challenges, apart from those who intentionally seek them out as a hobby. But <i>as a species</i>, we have proven ourselves supremely capable of surviving those conditions. So capable in fact, that we were able to alter those conditions to better suit our needs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108412#post1108412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity's reliance on artificial enhancements such as weapons, tools and shelter has stripped them of their natural defenses and weapons. A basic human outfitted with nothing but what nature itself has graced them with is fragile, short lived, and woefully incapable of defending itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humanity's ability to create and utilize weapons, tools, and shelter is itself an advantage that nature graced us with. What makes a house more &quot;artificial&quot; than a beehive or a bird's nest or a rabbit's burrow? The argument you are trying to make relies on a perceived separation between &quot;civilization&quot; and &quot;nature&quot;, which is entirely made up by <i>human culture</i>. Every animal alters its habitat to suit its needs. Humans are just so good at it that we've made the entire planet our habitat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108412#post1108412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A supernatural in the same situation is much more capable. The supernaturals don't need technology to survive, they have a potentially limitless variety of physical and mental abilities which can compensate for their lack of such resources. Using technology is merely a convenience for the WoD splats, it's not a necessity; like it is for humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>But use of technology is a natural mental ability that humans have. You're arbitrarily removing that advantage and then saying &quot;look how weak humans are compared to these made up creatures when they can't use their greates evolution-given strength!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108412#post1108412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't understand what's difficult to understand about how humans as a species are overrated. People keep bringing up how humans have technology and society on their side; but that is not what I was talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not difficult to understand, it's just that what you were talking about is meaningless. It's like &quot;who would win in a fight between Batman and Superman if Batman wasn't allowed to use any of his gadgets?&quot; Of course Superman would win, gadgets are what makes Batman Batman, and if you take them away without also taking away Superman's powers, you're not setting up a fair fight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108412#post1108412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't an argument about societal structure, it's an argument about eugenics. Many of the supernatural splats are objectively superior to humans, and it is only thanks to excessive population that humans pose a threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>You haven't really made any arguments in support of supernaturals being objectively superior though. All you've done is said &quot;if you hamstring humans and don't hamstring supernaturals, supernaturals have more going for them, therefore they're superior.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108412#post1108412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the splat books I've read seem to agree on this issue. They don't care if any one human in particular is trying to kill them. They care if an <i>entire town</i> is trying to kill them, because the legions of humanity will eventually wear them down. I even quoted <b>Zap Brannigan</b> about this subject.<br /> <br /> <i>&amp;quot;Knowing their weakness, I threw wave after wave of my own men at them. Until they reached their limit and shut down!&amp;quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, individual humans generally don't pose a threat to individual supernaturals in this fictional setting. Also in this fictional setting, humans are still presented as superior for reasons that have nothing to do with their ability to commit murdercide on supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Again, your assertion that humans without numbers or technology can't kill most supernaturals isn't wrong. It's just meaningless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T12:13:33-07:00","id":1108467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108412#post1108412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But yeah, this topic was brought up in the last thread. Humans hold the position that is does in this world completely through artificial means. If you strip a human of their technology and place them butt naked in the wild, chances are that they aren't going to survive against most threats they have to face. But if you do the same thing to one of the supernatural splats, they still have a pretty good chance at survival.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because tool making doesn't count despite humans not being the only tool making species on the planet. Yeah, no, you'll have to try a little harder than that to convince me that tool making skills are somehow an artificial advantage. It is a natural advantage, and it's been proven that it's also a very helpful one as regards the dominance of a species in a given eco-system.<br /> <br /> More importantly, the idea that tools should be factored out in a full-scale argument is kind of pointless. Hell, even the original Armory made the point that monsters can make and use tools too, albeit humanity is much more properly motivated to do it, and that it's not so much levelling the field so much as changing the game. If we want to appreciate the conflict, rather than dropping a human, a changeling, a werewolf and a beast naked in the Amazon, why don't we let them bring their equipment to bear?<br /> <br /> Also worth noting is this weird idea of a purely physical, violent-or-survival based definition of excellence. What about the arts, the sciences, the development of communities, the preservation of history? What about innovation and exploration and creation and shit like that? On the subjects that are probably more important to grade against than &quot;Hey, Dave, bet you I can lay around naked in the Amazon longer than you&quot;, monsters (even in a more real world context) would probably fall behind because the have a metric shit ton of problems on their plate that make it hard to focus on the same rapid evolution of things that make up the sort of eco-systemic dominance humanity has acheieved with it's ideas of civilization, even if the most prominent examples are inherently problematice-and that's before we get into discussions about how their inherent advantages do or do not help facilitate that subject(Such as how, yes, Mages would realistically technologically advance super-fucking fast by skipping through steps 1-7 on most projects).<br /> <br /> I'm just saying that a)The priorities and ways with which to see humanity as inferior are messed up here, reducing it to &quot;Naked in the Amazon&quot; when we need to be discussing how eco-systemic dominance is established, and b) fails to recognize that that's not an isolated thing-monsters in the Chronicles world are in a very essential symbiotic relationship with humanity, and the two are going to riff off of each other and build on the others accomplishments.<br /> <br /> PS: However, all of that neglects two things, which is a) monsters have a symbiotic relationship to humanity, but that doesn't mean that humanity has a symbiotic relationship with monsters(I mean, it can be debated, with some compelling cases regarding some of the monsters who can very easily be described as barriers to worse things), and b) the low reproduction rate of most monsters. You can argue that numbers aren't a thing that should be held as a major advantage for humanity in a conflict, and there's some case for that when all a mage has to do is be willing to self implode and otherwise evoke the Sleeping Curse big time-but it falls apart when it comes to becoming a genuinely dominant species. Just because most monsters are inherent predators of humanity, or at least in a position to stand taller than them, doesn't help when humanity just flat out breeds faster than you. Before long, you're going to their grainhouses, their synagogues, and their movie theaters, because they have uniquely spread and dominated in such a way that you find your monstrous self now has to exist within their context. There's just not enough of you to establish a real dominance, even if every single monster can kill 50 humans with ease or individually outlast them in the harshest environments.<br /> <br /> Monsters win on a small scale, but would clearly lose on a large scale. Is that true of all monsters in fiction? No, it's just the way that Chronicles is written, which is kind of universally humanist, in case you forgot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T12:33:00-07:00","id":1108469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108441#post1108441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> It's not difficult to understand, it's just that what you were talking about is meaningless. It's like &quot;who would win in a fight between Batman and Superman if Batman wasn't allowed to use any of his gadgets?&quot; Of course Superman would win, gadgets are what makes Batman Batman, and if you take them away without also taking away Superman's powers, you're not setting up a fair fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You haven't really made any arguments in support of supernaturals being objectively superior though. All you've done is said &quot;if you hamstring humans and don't hamstring supernaturals, supernaturals have more going for them, therefore they're superior.&quot;</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, Batman's ideology is what makes Batman Batman. He's a symbol, not a man.<br /> <br /> And even with all of his gadgets, Batman has personally admitted that if Supes wanted to, he could kill him in an instant. Superman can punch people at the speed of light, which means Batman would be splattered against the wall before he could even reach for that krytponite on his belt. Not only that, but Superman could just snipe him from orbit with telescopic heat vision and Batman would burst into flames before he knew what hit him.<br /> <br /> The only thing your Superman vs Batman argument did was reaffirm my point. The only way Batman could defeat Superman is if he caught him off guard. Because his strength and speed are so far beyond human capabilities that a straight confrontation is suicide. And that's before you take his other super powers into account.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I'm not hamstringing anybody. I am pointing out that in a completely fair fight, the splats have the advantage over humans. Their super powers are instrinsic to their existence. They're natural capabilities, hence the term supernatural.<br /> <br /> But to try and clarify, humans are not the only ones in this scenario who have the ability to use technology and organized society. The supernaturals are just as intelligent (possibly more so) than them, and they also have the ability to organize into societies. Hell, they have at least 5 entire factions per splat, so clearly they have the ability to form their own opinions / philosophies on life.<br /> <br /> <br /> In a straight up fight, we can say that both a human and a werewolf are equipped with a machine gun. There's nothing objectively stopping the werewolf from being able to use a firearm, aside from personal training in such a weapon. So they both have a machine gun, that's cool. But in addition to that, the Werewolf has all the benefits to being a werewolf, such as accelerated healing, enhanced senses, physical prowess. Let's say for the sake of argument the werewolf won't be using fetishes, even though they are basically the same thing as human technology.<br /> <br /> <br /> Emptying the entire clip into a werewolf's torso might be enough to kill them, or it might just stun them long enough for the human to make a break for it while the very pissed off lycanthrope tries to push 30 bullets out of their ventilated flesh. The werewolf, on the other hand, only needs one well placed bullet to end the human's existence, and they'd know where the human is long before they laid eyes on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T13:03:32-07:00","id":1108477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108469#post1108469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Batman's ideology is what makes Batman Batman. He's a symbol, not a man.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought we were talking about capabilities, not philosophy. Yes, Batman's ideology is what makes him Batman, but without his gadgets he's just a guy who doesn't like guns and dresses in a funny costume.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108469#post1108469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even with all of his gadgets, Batman has personally admitted that if Supes wanted to, he could kill him in an instant. Superman can punch people at the speed of light, which means Batman would be splattered against the wall before he could even reach for that krytponite on his belt. Not only that, but Superman could just snipe him from orbit with telescopic heat vision and Batman would burst into flames before he knew what hit him.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, who actually won when they fought in Dark Knight Returns? Oh yeah, Batman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108469#post1108469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing your Superman vs Batman argument did was reaffirm my point. The only way Batman could defeat Superman is if he caught him off guard. Because his strength and speed are so far beyond human capabilities that a straight confrontation is suicide. And that's before you take his other super powers into account.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually he won by hitting Supes with Kryptonite. But no, it does not reaffirm your point, it illustrates why your point is stupid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108469#post1108469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm not hamstringing anybody. I am pointing out that in a completely fair fight, the splats have the advantage over humans. Their super powers are instrinsic to their existence. They're natural capabilities, hence the term supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>And human ingenuity is a natural capability intrinsic to our existence. Would most of us win a one-on-one fight against a fictional superpowered creature? Probably not. But again, that's not the reason the fiction in question presents humans as superior in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108469#post1108469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But to try and clarify, humans are not the only ones in this scenario who have the ability to use technology and organized society. The supernaturals are just as intelligent (possibly more so) than them, and they also have the ability to organize into societies. Hell, they have at least 5 entire factions per splat, so clearly they have the ability to form their own opinions / philosophies on life.<br /> <br /> In a straight up fight, we can say that both a human and a werewolf are equipped with a machine gun. There's nothing objectively stopping the werewolf from being able to use a firearm, aside from personal training in such a weapon. So they both have a machine gun, that's cool. But in addition to that, the Werewolf has all the benefits to being a werewolf, such as accelerated healing, enhanced senses, physical prowess. Let's say for the sake of argument the werewolf won't be using fetishes, even though they are basically the same thing as human technology.<br /> <br /> <br /> Emptying the entire clip into a werewolf's torso might be enough to kill them, or it might just stun them long enough for the human to make a break for it while the very pissed off lycanthrope tries to push 30 bullets out of their ventilated flesh. The werewolf, on the other hand, only needs one well placed bullet to end the human's existence, and they'd know where the human is long before they laid eyes on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you know, dudes with powers win in white room death matches against dudes without powers. What a paradigm-changing revelation that is, you've really opened all of our eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T13:48:21-07:00","id":1108493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108469#post1108469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In a straight up fight, we can say that both a human and a werewolf are equipped with a machine gun. There's nothing objectively stopping the werewolf from being able to use a firearm, aside from personal training in such a weapon. So they both have a machine gun, that's cool. But in addition to that, the Werewolf has all the benefits to being a werewolf, such as accelerated healing, enhanced senses, physical prowess. Let's say for the sake of argument the werewolf won't be using fetishes, even though they are basically the same thing as human technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know this is a far more amusing white room scenario when you replace a werewolf with a vampire and give both combatants flame throwers instead of machine guns.<br /> <br /> Since one of your points was that the human needs to get the drop on the werewolf, let's say for the sake of argument the werewolf isn't getting the drop on the human here (since that defeats the point - a werewolf should, if biologically superior, be capable of defeating the mortal even with all of that werewolf's disadvantages). Both sides are firmly aware of the other side's capabilities rather than one having a hidden ace up their sleeve. They set themselves thirty feet apart from each other in this classic challenge. Human picks a machine gun with silver bullets. Werewolf picks a machine gun with better bullets because silver would be foolish on his end and normal bullets are more effective.<br /> <br /> Now of course the werewolf can utilize all of his werewolf capabilities in this sense, but this is highly situational and most are going to be useless - not only is that silver dealing aggravated damage, but it's crippling essence as well. If the werewolf closes the distance, he wins - hands down. But can he close that distance before that trigger is pulled? In the end, it comes down to who can pull the trigger faster. And in the end, if the first bullet doesn't kill the human, the werewolf -will- die. The silver is doing more damage than the bullets.<br /> <br /> Fun thought here though, for a self-counterpoint: Most werewolf packs are now significantly larger than hunter cells and comprised of more than werewolves. How then does a hunter cell manage to effectively hunt werewolves, if werewolves are universally superior and also larger in number?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 06-27-2017, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T13:53:46-07:00","id":1108498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108493#post1108493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf picks a machine gun with better bullets because silver would be retarded on his end</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Don't use the word &quot;retarded&quot; this way.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T14:16:49-07:00","id":1108509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108498#post1108498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:red\">Don't use the word &quot;retarded&quot; this way.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>NP. Edited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T14:18:57-07:00","id":1108510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108477#post1108477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but without his gadgets he's just a guy who doesn't like guns and dresses in a funny costume.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> EXACTLY what I'm trying to explain, here! Batman without gadgets is just a random guy. A supernatural without gadgets is still supernatural.<br /> <br /> <br /> Although from what I understand, Batman is at the physical peak of humanity. Although sometimes the writers go way too far and forget the fact he's not supposed to have any super powers. I can believe that he's able to lift 1,000 lbs. I can NOT believe that he's able to catch a machine gun barrage with his hands!<br /> <br /> You're right, human ingenuity is a natural part of human existence. The things that we create with that ingenuity, however, are not. They're artificial, we can't draw upon them at will. Unlike the supernaturals who always have access to their powers and abilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------<br /> <br /> As for the vampire and human using flame throwers, you're assuming the vampire is going to stand still in that scenario. Rather than use their powers to outmaneuver / overpower the human. Good luck hitting somebody who can outrun a speeding car with that flamethrower. And good luck surviving the encounter after your spray and pray set the entire area on fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-27-2017, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T15:41:26-07:00","id":1108530,"title":"","content":"I feel like a point in humanity's favor is that humans have fought lots of wars; humanity has so many tactics and so much experience that fighting wars against a greater foe is possible.<br /> <br /> For the sake of argument, if there was any large scale battle between humans and monsters then humans don't have to be the stronger opponent. All they have to do is make winning the war pointless for the monsters; a phhyric victory. Humans invented the scorched earth policy, and if that doesn't say something I don't really know what will.<br /> <br /> Individual humans are also capable of surviving quite a lot of dangers; average people go through natural disasters and similar bad situations and many of them survive these things. It's arguable that humanity's natural instincts and capabilities are still there, it's just that they aren't very relevant to everyone's life anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custo