s=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108567#post1108567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for funsies. I was bored and decided to talk about whatever came to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, mission accomplished. We have now established who wins in a battle to the death between a naked human and a werewolf in a featureless void. Very intellectually stimulating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T17:48:26-07:00","id":1108570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108530#post1108530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like a point in humanity's favor is that humans have fought lots of wars; humanity has so many tactics and so much experience that fighting wars against a greater foe is possible.<br /> <br /> For the sake of argument, if there was any large scale battle between humans and monsters then humans don't have to be the stronger opponent. All they have to do is make winning the war pointless for the monsters; a phhyric victory. Humans invented the scorched earth policy, and if that doesn't say something I don't really know what will.<br /> <br /> Individual humans are also capable of surviving quite a lot of dangers; average people go through natural disasters and similar bad situations and many of them survive these things. It's arguable that humanity's natural instincts and capabilities are still there, it's just that they aren't very relevant to everyone's life anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The supernaturals have fought wars too, most of them used to be humans, after all. And them fighting wars is part of an early claim in the argument in that humanity's only real strength lies in their overwhelming numbers. Supernaturals have squads, humans have armies, but a single supernatural soldier is typically worth 5 human soldiers or more, so that squad may as well be a whole battalion.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, it takes decades to fully master war, and by the time most humans achieve it, they're usually on their way out. Supernaturals, on the other hand, have extended life spans, which means not only can they afford the years it takes to become a master of war, but they can also improve from there. A human soldier has studied the battles of ancient history, a vampire elder has actually lived through them.<br /> <br /> So saying that humans are more experienced when it comes to warfare is just downright silly.<br /> <br /> <b>Especially since the various splats in game have been at war against other supernatural entities for as long as they can remember.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108569#post1108569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, mission accomplished. We have now established who wins in a battle to the death between a naked human and a werewolf in a featureless void. Very intellectually stimulating.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we all learned something here today!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T17:56:47-07:00","id":1108572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108570#post1108570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Especially since the various splats in game have been at war against other supernatural entities for as long as they can remember.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Only the werewolves and Demons, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T18:08:20-07:00","id":1108573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108510#post1108510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlike the supernaturals who always have access to their powers and abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a world of difference between Pattern Restoration and Life 5. Most supernatural powers are not innate from the word &quot;go.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T18:19:31-07:00","id":1108576,"title":"","content":"So, are we done proving just how much vulnerable we puny humans are when stripped of everything that makes us human, in the same way how we often prove that knives are useless when dulled and rusted?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, just remembered this. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a>, have you read the Thyrsus Awakening section in Mage? Specifically, the naturalist who Awakened after not devolving into a feral animal (which would be superior than we puny humans, if we go by your logic), but by regaining the use of tools and technology?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She runs down the beast, stronger and<br /> faster than any human, but claims humanity from the bones<br /> she turns to spears and the hide that fashions clothes and<br /> shelter. Her name is the chop marks of her stone hand-ax on<br /> prey bones. </div> </div> </div>Now, I know that mages themselves are nevertheless monstrous, but they're still of humanity (like all those times how we condemn vicious criminals as 'monsters') and that section does tell us how humanity, nature, and technology are related.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 06-27-2017, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T18:38:17-07:00","id":1108580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108576#post1108576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, are we done proving just how much vulnerable we puny humans are when stripped of everything that makes us human, in the same way how we often prove that knives are useless when dulled and rusted?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, just remembered this. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a>, have you read the Thyrsus Awakening section in Mage? Specifically, the naturalist who Awakened after not devolving into a feral animal (which would be superior than we puny humans, if we go by your logic), but by regaining the use of tools and technology?<br /> <br /> Now, I know that mages themselves are nevertheless monstrous, but they're still of humanity (like all those times how we condemn vicious criminals as 'monsters') and that section does tell us how humanity, nature, and technology are related.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I have not. I was planning to get Mage, but then I learned Changeling 2E was close to completion, so I decided to hold off. I'll probably get mage after Changeling, though.<br /> <br /> Could you explain to me why mages are monstrous though? Because I thought the game was about the dangers of hubris. Basically &quot;hey, I've got all this crazy power, better not abuse it!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T18:47:02-07:00","id":1108582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108580#post1108580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I have not. I was planning to get Mage, but then I learned Changeling 2E was close to completion, so I decided to hold off. I'll probably get mage after Changeling, though.<br /> <br /> Could you explain to me why mages are monstrous though? Because I thought the game was about the dangers of hubris. Basically &quot;hey, I've got all this crazy power, better not abuse it!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Supernal magic is essentially having reality at your fingertips, and mages can easily do monstrous things with such power; ripping out souls, experimenting on other supernaturals, stepping on other people very easily, etc. Mages are monstrous because they can read the source code of reality, and they're crazy enough to play around with it to see what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T18:52:26-07:00","id":1108584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108569#post1108569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have now established who wins in a battle to the death between a naked human and a werewolf in a featureless void.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Demon that used Solitary Confinement on both of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T19:29:32-07:00","id":1108597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108582#post1108582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Supernal magic is essentially having reality at your fingertips, and mages can easily do monstrous things with such power; ripping out souls, experimenting on other supernaturals, stepping on other people very easily, etc. Mages are monstrous because they can read the source code of reality, and they're crazy enough to play around with it to see what happens.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If that's the case, one could argue humans are no less monstrous.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hmm, this hydrogen bomb might create a chain reaction that destroys our planet's atmosphere... LET'S SEE WHAT HAPPENS!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T19:43:00-07:00","id":1108600,"title":"","content":"This thread reminds me the famous Monty Python &quot;what have the romans ever done for us&quot; scene.<br /> <br /> <i>- How could the mortal win the monsters?</i><br /> <b>- Strenght in numbers!!</b><br /> <i>- Ok, but apart from strenght in numbers, how could the mortals win the monsters?</i><br /> <b>- Exploiting the monsters weaknesess!!</b><br /> <b>- Some monsters would support the mortals!!</b><br /> <i>- Ok, but apart from strenght in numbers, exploiting the monsters weaknesess and the support from some monsters... how could the mortals win the monsters?</i><br /> <b>- Their adaptability!!</b><br /> <b>- Their ability to create and use tools!!</b><br /> <i>- Ok, but apart from strenght in numbers, exploiting the monsters weaknesess, the support from some monsters, their adaptability and their hability to create and use tools... how could the mortals win the monsters? Humanity is overrated!!!</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p-fRo5-p9hE\" data-code=\"p-fRo5-p9hE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/p-fRo5-p9hE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T19:51:53-07:00","id":1108603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108580#post1108580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I have not. I was planning to get Mage, but then I learned Changeling 2E was close to completion, so I decided to hold off. I'll probably get mage after Changeling, though.<br /> <br /> Could you explain to me why mages are monstrous though? Because I thought the game was about the dangers of hubris. Basically &quot;hey, I've got all this crazy power, better not abuse it!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages are half-flesh, half-truth beings who are burning reality on a fundamental level, burning everything around them by presence unless they deliberately curtail such effects, and likewise are slowly warped on a spiritual level which also warps many of the base assumptions of their flesh. We are talking about a being that is warping in on itself to become a Mystery by sheer virtue of existing.<br /> <br /> And that's <i>before</i> you account for the active use of magic and it's many possible consequences.<br /> <br /> PS: and yes, I am very definitely not talking about Prometheans, in case you wondered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T20:34:29-07:00","id":1108609,"title":"","content":"Well if we've gotten past the whole 'humans are physically weaker than most supernaturals' aspect of this, I myself am a little interested in the thoughts of people in regards to how humanity is a larger threat in the world of darkness and what tactics they might utilize to be that bigger threat. For instance - in my experience, most hunter cells are actually smaller than the size of a werewolf pack (at least a 2e werewolf pack). How then does a hunter cell become a threat in the world of darkness - what tactics would they take (besides the obvious use of silver, which is a given), in order to eliminate a larger and stronger force (with nasty little spirits on top of it)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T20:51:37-07:00","id":1108612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108609#post1108609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if we've gotten past the whole 'humans are physically weaker than most supernaturals' aspect of this, I myself am a little interested in the thoughts of people in regards to how humanity is a larger threat in the world of darkness and what tactics they might utilize to be that bigger threat. For instance - in my experience, most hunter cells are actually smaller than the size of a werewolf pack (at least a 2e werewolf pack). How then does a hunter cell become a threat in the world of darkness - what tactics would they take (besides the obvious use of silver, which is a given), in order to eliminate a larger and stronger force (with nasty little spirits on top of it)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everybody sleeps, relaxes, or goes home to their family at the end of a long hard day running in the Shadows. The dangerous Hunters aren't the ones who think that they can arrange a simple no-holds-barred throwdown in the woods at midnight against the whole pack at once. Rather, they're the ones who attack the pack when each werewolf is off on their own and not expecting it, or they convince the werewolf's own family members that something is off and turn them on the werewolf, or they come at the werewolf through entirely mundane channels by ensuring evidence from the pack's activities finds its way into the hands of, say, law enforcement. <br /> <br /> The reason so many posters are critical of Nyrufa's dismissal of technology and society is because technology and society are such hideously strong weapons standing foremost in the arsenal of regular humans. Hunters can attack werewolves without ever being face to face with the wolf, whether that be through the scope of a rifle from miles away or because the weapon of choice for that Hunter is actually the IRS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T21:37:43-07:00","id":1108619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108580#post1108580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you explain to me why mages are monstrous though? Because I thought the game was about the dangers of hubris. Basically &quot;hey, I've got all this crazy power, better not abuse it!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/830278-mages-as-monsters\">Here you go.</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T22:03:10-07:00","id":1108624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108597#post1108597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's the case, one could argue humans are no less monstrous.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Hmm, this hydrogen bomb might create a chain reaction that destroys our planet's atmosphere... LET'S SEE WHAT HAPPENS!&amp;quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I've noticed a pattern. Everyone who holds to the &quot;Why wouldn't you choose to become a monster?&quot; view also seems to have this view of Mages being no more monstrous than regular humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T22:06:59-07:00","id":1108625,"title":"","content":"Misanthropy is a hell of a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T22:17:12-07:00","id":1108627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108609#post1108609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if we've gotten past the whole 'humans are physically weaker than most supernaturals' aspect of this, I myself am a little interested in the thoughts of people in regards to how humanity is a larger threat in the world of darkness and what tactics they might utilize to be that bigger threat. For instance - in my experience, most hunter cells are actually smaller than the size of a werewolf pack (at least a 2e werewolf pack). How then does a hunter cell become a threat in the world of darkness - what tactics would they take (besides the obvious use of silver, which is a given), in order to eliminate a larger and stronger force (with nasty little spirits on top of it)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You're right, those things are quite dangerous and would be a daunting threat... <b>if the monsters didn't also have the capacity to access them.</b><br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness, humans aren't dealing with mindless, savage creatures who's only thoughts are hunt, kill, repeat. They are dealing with intelligent creatures who have blended into their society and adapted their resources for their own use. They have been doing this for hundreds, if not thousands of years and have become so proffecient at covering their tracks that the vast majority of humans don't even believe they exist.<br /> <br /> Let's say the monsters pull the same stunt and track the hunters back to their own homes and families. They scout the place out and find an entire room loaded up with military grade weapons and an itinerary of a list of people they plan to target.<br /> <br /> The monster makes an anonymous call to the cops and suddenly the Hunters are being investigated on suspicions of terrorism. The fuck are they gonna tell the judge? That the people they were planning to blow up are shapeshifting wolf people? Or that their neighbor practices witchcraft in his basement on thursdays?<br /> <br /> <br /> You guys are making the mistake of assuming what would happen if humans and monsters went into a full scale war. If monsters just dropped the masquerade and came out into the open. That is not what I was suggesting. We're not discussing a full scale open war conflict between monsters and humans. We're discussing a naturally equipped human's chances of defeating a naturally equipped monster.<br /> <br /> Which is, to say, practically zero chance in the human's favor. Guns, smart phones, body armor, none of these are relevent to the argument. They are not part of a human's natural capabilities, they are not an intrinsic part of your mind / body. Unlike the supernaturals who's powers are ingrained into their very existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108624#post1108624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I've noticed a pattern. Everyone who holds to the &quot;Why wouldn't you choose to become a monster?&quot; view also seems to have this view of Mages being no more monstrous than regular humans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To be fair, humans have a shameful history of seeking out ways to turn our greatest achievements into instruments of death and destruction.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I already explained I don't know much about Mage because I don't have the book. Which is why I asked for an explanation. Though I do find the setting to be intriguing enough to give the book a look through when I've got the money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-28-2017, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T22:37:49-07:00","id":1108631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108627#post1108627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys are making the mistake of assuming what would happen if humans and monsters went into a full scale war. If monsters just dropped the masquerade and came out into the open. That is not what I was suggesting. We're not discussing a full scale open war conflict between monsters and humans. We're discussing a naturally equipped human's chances of defeating a naturally equipped monster.<br /> <br /> Which is, to say, practically zero chance in the human's favor. Guns, smart phones, body armor, none of these are relevent to the argument. They are not part of a human's natural capabilities, they are not an intrinsic part of your mind / body. Unlike the supernaturals who's powers are ingrained into their very existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood isn't an intrinsic part of a vampire's mind/body, so they can't power any of their abilities. Moon and Shadow Gifts aren't an intrinsic part of a werewolf, they are, as the name implies, Gifts, just like rites are a form of technology. Mages without artifacts, Hallows, rotes, mana. You could go even further and point out that simply being a vampire is not intrinsic to them, it's something granted by another vampire or a strix or some other dark power. Just like werewolves and mages and everyone else down the line.<br /> <br /> We've pointed this out repeatedly, you are stacking the deck. Maitrecorbo said it best, I think. I'm not sure if you even notice? Sticking Batman and Superman in a room together naked is not a 'fair fight' any more than sticking a naked human with a fully empowered werewolf or having a boxer fight a vampire who's staked under the open sky at high noon. These 'fair' situations you keep proposing exist solely to hinder the naked human. Which is one of the reasons people have problems with your argument. Yes, they can most likely win a fight. No, this is not some objective determinator of the superiority of anything except the inability of the supernatural to be harmed as easy as the naked human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T22:53:49-07:00","id":1108633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108627#post1108627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're right, those things are quite dangerous and would be a daunting threat... <b>if the monsters didn't also have the capacity to access them.</b><br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness, humans aren't dealing with mindless, savage creatures who's only thoughts are hunt, kill, repeat. They are dealing with intelligent creatures who have blended into their society and adapted their resources for their own use. They have been doing this for hundreds, if not thousands of years and have become so proffecient at covering their tracks that the vast majority of humans don't even believe they exist.<br /> <br /> Let's say the monsters pull the same stunt and track the hunters back to their own homes and families. They scout the place out and find an entire room loaded up with military grade weapons and an itinerary of a list of people they plan to target.<br /> <br /> The monster makes an anonymous call to the cops and suddenly the Hunters are being investigated on suspicions of terrorism. The fuck are they gonna tell the judge? That the people they were planning to blow up are shapeshifting wolf people? Or that their neighbor practices witchcraft in his basement on thursdays?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your response to my quote makes no sense. Are you responding to the person who responded to my query?<br /> <br /> Also... just an observation of this. At the very least, in America it is not a crime to carry most arms - and unless the hunters are operating with weapons they are not licensed to carry... the idea that a person has a whole room loaded with weapons is not just not a crime - its not even uncommon. The term 'a thousand bullets for every gun' comes up a lot with people I talk to. As far as the list of people to kill... first off, what hunter leaves a list of people to kill lying at home with their families? Really? Even on the off chance that they did - unless a body shows up the judge is going to ... what? Not illegal to write a 'wishes-they-were-dead' list. All it gets is the hunters -and- the hunters targets watched by the law. Which, while it seems like it might inconvenience the hunters, it will inconvenience the werewolves -far- more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T23:03:13-07:00","id":1108636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108631#post1108631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blood isn't an intrinsic part of a vampire's mind/body, so they can't power any of their abilities. Moon and Shadow Gifts aren't an intrinsic part of a werewolf, they are, as the name implies, Gifts, just like rites are a form of technology. Mages without artifacts, Hallows, rotes, mana. You could go even further and point out that simply being a vampire is not intrinsic to them, it's something granted by another vampire or a strix or some other dark power. Just like werewolves and mages and everyone else down the line.<br /> <br /> We've pointed this out repeatedly, you are stacking the deck. Maitrecorbo said it best, I think. I'm not sure if you even notice? Sticking Batman and Superman in a room together naked is not a 'fair fight' any more than sticking a naked human with a fully empowered werewolf or having a boxer fight a vampire who's staked under the open sky at high noon. These 'fair' situations you keep proposing exist solely to hinder the naked human. Which is one of the reasons people have problems with your argument. Yes, they can most likely win a fight. No, this is not some objective determinator of the superiority of anything except the inability of the supernatural to be harmed as easy as the naked human.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Saying that blood isn't an intrinsic part of a vampire's body is like saying digested shit isn't a part of a human's body.<br /> <br /> Deny a human food and water for a few days and see how capable they are in a fight.<br /> <br /> Blood is a vampire's form of sustenance, but that doesn't discredit it.<br /> <br /> Also, saying that a vampire's existence isn't intrinsic to them is just grasping at straws here. Even if they weren't born a vampire (nobody is, duh), they're still a completely different species than they were before.<br /> <br /> As for Werewolves and their gifts, I would consider the use of fetishes to be similar to human technology. They need to be in possession of the fetish in order to harness its power. Even without them, however, the Werewolf still has accelerated healing capabilities, claws, fangs, heightened senses, and the ability to transform into an 8 foot tall, 500 lbs killing machine.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not gonna reply on the mages, as I don't know enough about the game to debate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T23:09:00-07:00","id":1108637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108633#post1108633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your response to my quote makes no sense. Are you responding to the person who responded to my query?<br /> <br /> Also... just an observation of this. At the very least, in America it is not a crime to carry most arms - and unless the hunters are operating with weapons they are not licensed to carry... the idea that a person has a whole room loaded with weapons is not just not a crime - its not even uncommon. The term 'a thousand bullets for every gun' comes up a lot with people I talk to. As far as the list of people to kill... first off, what hunter leaves a list of people to kill lying at home with their families? Really? Even on the off chance that they did - unless a body shows up the judge is going to ... what? Not illegal to write a 'wishes-they-were-dead' list. All it gets is the hunters -and- the hunters targets watched by the law. Which, while it seems like it might inconvenience the hunters, it will inconvenience the werewolves -far- more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's not a crime to own a crap ton of guns, heck there are some people who own M60's even though they have no practical use for them. There is, however, a law against having a map of the city marked with key structures and a list of photographs on the wall with red X's marking out the faces of people who have recently gone missing from the local area. It is extremely easy to convince society that the Hunters are violently dangerous criminals. It is much more difficult for the Hunters to convince society that they are fighting literal monsters.<br /> <br /> <br /> And sure, the Hunters might not keep that stuff near their families; unless they're raising their kids to be Hunters, too. But I was just using their families as a possible example. The Hunters might also track them back to a safe house, which is an even worse place to store all your military hardware, because keeping a room full of guns in your house is a hell of a lot less suspicious than keeping an armory of weapons in some undisclosed location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-28-2017, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T23:17:51-07:00","id":1108639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108636#post1108636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying that blood isn't an intrinsic part of a vampire's body is like saying digested shit isn't a part of a human's body.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Deny a human food and water for a few days and see how capable they are in a fight. </div> </div> </div>You're denying them other easily obtainable things to make them incapable of fighting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, saying that a vampire's existence isn't intrinsic to them is just grasping at straws here. Even if they weren't born a vampire (nobody is, duh), they're still a completely different species than they were before. </div> </div> </div>This is another thing you seem to be confused about. Vampires are not a species. Mages, Changelings, Prometheans, Sin-Eaters are not a species. Embraces and Awakenings and Durances, these are things that happen to normal people and outside of two exceptions, they are not capable of reproducing their own kind with any sort of consistency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T23:27:08-07:00","id":1108641,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming this stuff was in response to my post, rather than Jakondite.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108627#post1108627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right, those things are quite dangerous and would be a daunting threat... <b>if the monsters didn't also have the capacity to access them.</b><br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness, humans aren't dealing with mindless, savage creatures who's only thoughts are hunt, kill, repeat. They are dealing with intelligent creatures who have blended into their society and adapted their resources for their own use. They have been doing this for hundreds, if not thousands of years and have become so proffecient at covering their tracks that the vast majority of humans don't even believe they exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree. In fact you can easily go one step further and say that the average monster could be more connected than the average Hunter. The kind of attitude that leads one to monster hunting probably doesn't also lead to a well-functioning social life. It's not exactly relevant though, for the reasons I'm going to detail below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108627#post1108627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say the monsters pull the same stunt and track the hunters back to their own homes and families. They scout the place out and find an entire room loaded up with military grade weapons and an itinerary of a list of people they plan to target.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a big assumption, first and foremost. The point of indirect warfare is to prevent exactly that, the monsters ending up on the Hunters' doorstep. We already established that the Hunters probably lose the straight fight, that's why they're attacking the monsters in this fashion to begin with.<br /> <br /> More importantly though, we need to deal with the matter of profile. The monsters do monstrous things. That attracts attention, attention draws in Hunters. Monsters need to do what makes them monsters because it's part of their nature. The wolf hunters, the vampires feed, and so on. So their standard mode of behaviour puts them in a spotlight for those who know what to look for and also gives cause and grievance for random alienated humans to become their enemy.<br /> <br /> What this means is that there's virtually zero chance of a monster ever getting to a Hunter <i>first</i>. The Hunter may not even be a Hunter until they make the first move. There's no &quot;tell&quot; that a Hunter exists until the first monster is dead. The Hunter's equivalent to the monster's monstrous behaviour is killing monsters. And when the Hunters have the population advantage, and the monsters can't help but create more Hunters, that's the reason a smart monster lives in fear.<br /> <br /> Yes, Hunters can fuck up. A monster could realise it's under observation, or a Hunter could fail its first attempt at killing the monster and the creature could be alerted by that. But in game terms we're all familiar with, it's like Hunters have a permanent Surprise Attack advantage against monsters. They get a free round in which they can do something to the monster before it gets to react, except instead of being a single round of combat that &quot;free round&quot; could translate into any number of things.<br /> <br /> Even in your example, the monsters have to take the hit first <i>and then</i> track the hunters back to their homes and families. The monsters are always reacting, on the defensive. That's an oppressive burden to live under, to say the least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108627#post1108627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The monster makes an anonymous call to the cops and suddenly the Hunters are being investigated on suspicions of terrorism. The fuck are they gonna tell the judge? That the people they were planning to blow up are shapeshifting wolf people? Or that their neighbor practices witchcraft in his basement on thursdays?</div> </div> </div> </div>For most monsters, the law is a lot more dangerous and disruptive than it is for most Hunters. You get a Hunter indicted on conspiracy to commit murder, and he's behind bars for a long time but he can still function as a human being. A vampire probably wouldn't even survive its court dates, and most kinds of monster behaviour are a lot harder to do once they've lost their privacy to the legal system.<br /> <br /> Worse, for a monster, being convicted of a crime raises their profile. It means more people will know of them and about them. That's more potential Hunters. And a Hunter getting convicted? That does the same thing. A man raving in court about wolf people and witchcraft may just give a few select souls who read about it in the paper or see the clip online the clues they need to take up the fight themselves. Less dramatically, it may mean that the details of the case catch someone's eye and in a more mundane fashion and they dig, and uncover the truth.<br /> <br /> In effect, the monster can use the same tactics. They often do. But due to the difference in nature between monster and Hunter they're not going to impact their respective targets in the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T23:39:57-07:00","id":1108642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108637#post1108637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is, however, a law against having a map of the city marked with key structures and a list of photographs on the wall with red X's marking out the faces of people who have recently gone missing from the local area.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... I don't believe that. Prove it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108637#post1108637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is extremely easy to convince society that the Hunters are violently dangerous criminals. It is much more difficult for the Hunters to convince society that they are fighting literal monsters</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why Hunters don't sit around convincing society they are fighting literal monsters. Instead, they accuse the monsters of potentially being violently dangerous criminals. Which, fortunately for the hunter, they usually are!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T01:21:02-07:00","id":1108659,"title":"","content":"Of course a given Supernatural Being trends towards being far more powerful than a given Human Being. That's not actually up for debate, is it? <br /> <br /> Humanity as a whole, though? That has the potential to be a wholly different discussion. Which one is this thread actually supposed to be about? Because I'm seeing posts about naked 1v1 white rooms interspersed among conversations about human culture, etc. This is all over the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T02:18:07-07:00","id":1108668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108659#post1108659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course a given Supernatural Being trends towards being far more powerful than a given Human Being. That's not actually up for debate, is it?<br /> <br /> Humanity as a whole, though? That has the potential to be a wholly different discussion. Which one is this thread actually supposed to be about? Because I'm seeing posts about naked 1v1 white rooms interspersed among conversations about human culture, etc. This is all over the place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, it's a mess. Don't take the thread title at face value. OP shifting the post every other time doesn't helps either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T03:34:34-07:00","id":1108682,"title":"","content":"I think what makes humans superior is that most of them can just ignore what happens in the shadows, and lead a somewhat stable and fulfilling life. This isn't the case for most supernaturals which makes them subject to many stresses, problems and urges almost by default. One could argue that the extra stresses of being a supernatural being are being offset by him being a superior individual that for example does not have to worry about getting sick anymore. But still, I'd rather get sick than have to hunt people for food.<br /> <br /> And before someone points out there are also humans who get exposed to the shadows, yes, they're screwed. But the people who get pulled into the shadows and can't just ignore it and go back to their normal lives are a minority. Humanity should be proud of their ability to just ignore most of the crazy things happening in the Chronicles of Darkness and just live on as if nothing happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T06:23:57-07:00","id":1108735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108659#post1108659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course a given Supernatural Being trends towards being far more powerful than a given Human Being. That's not actually up for debate, is it?<br /> <br /> Humanity as a whole, though? That has the potential to be a wholly different discussion. Which one is this thread actually supposed to be about? Because I'm seeing posts about naked 1v1 white rooms interspersed among conversations about human culture, etc. This is all over the place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's supposed to be about the first one. Those who joined the thread later tried to steer it towards the second.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108641#post1108641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For most monsters, the law is a lot more dangerous and disruptive than it is for most Hunters. You get a Hunter indicted on conspiracy to commit murder, and he's behind bars for a long time but he can still function as a human being. A vampire probably wouldn't even survive its court dates, and most kinds of monster behaviour are a lot harder to do once they've lost their privacy to the legal system.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Assuming that the vampire even receives a court date. Don't forget that vampires run their own shadow governments and have been concealing their existence since the time of the dark ages. The fact that they continue to do so in the electronic age where damn near everybody has a camera is a testament to their skill at subterfuge.<br /> <br /> Those who are talking about humanity's ability to function as a society don't realize that the monsters can do the same. If you expose one vampire, you've pretty much exposed every vampire. So any Prince worthy of his station is going to have several key figures in office on his pay roll. Evidence goes missing, files get corrupted, witnesses are bribed / intimidated, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> And that's assuming they don't have any Ghouls, who are capable of acting during the day, and have a much easier time blending in with humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-28-2017, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T06:49:03-07:00","id":1108741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108735#post1108735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> It's supposed to be about the first one. Those who joined the thread later tried to steer it towards the second.</div> </div> </div> </div>...ok, this happened.<br /> <br /> Just let me say that you going there probably was not a brilliant idea and, I swear, I'm telling you this will all the good will I can muster.<br /> <br /> Not wanting to pick at that nugget myself, here's what you claim to want to hear:<br /> <br /> Very well, in a fight between a human and a monster with the exact same mundane resources, the monster wins because it has the supernatural advantage. You were right all along. In other news, magical powers let you do what normal people can't do, the more dices you roll the more successes you're likely to obtain and if that's the only thing we're meant to discuss here I don't get how we reached 8 pages so far.<br /> <br /> Let's not get the fact you debated against every single one of the points others brought up as if you actually wanted to talk about others things too get in our way. It's other people that derailed the topic.<br /> <br /> Right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T06:59:33-07:00","id":1108745,"title":"","content":"I know I should not be nytrua can be an ass he remands me of myself I always wanted to be right good thing I'm not like that no more","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T07:13:50-07:00","id":1108751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108735#post1108735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming that the vampire even receives a court date. Don't forget that vampires run their own shadow governments and have been concealing their existence since the time of the dark ages. The fact that they continue to do so in the electronic age where damn near everybody has a camera is a testament to their skill at subterfuge.<br /> <br /> Those who are talking about humanity's ability to function as a society don't realize that the monsters can do the same. If you expose one vampire, you've pretty much exposed every vampire. So any Prince worthy of his station is going to have several key figures in office on his pay roll. Evidence goes missing, files get corrupted, witnesses are bribed / intimidated, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> And that's assuming they don't have any Ghouls, who are capable of acting during the day, and have a much easier time blending in with humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow man. Talk about cherry picking. Out of that entire post the only part you're interested in responding to is the throwaway line &quot;A vampire wouldn't even survive its court date&quot;? I guess I can take that as an acknowledgement that you agree with the rest?<br /> <br /> But whatever, if this is all you're interested in, so be it. Vampires have a shadow government. They don't have total control over human government. Complicating matters, most governments have checks and balances and systems created specifically to uncover the kind of corruption you're talking about (operating to varying degrees of effectiveness). Hunters are capable of furthering that process, rooting out the ghoul servants the Vampire is relying on, generally making matters difficult. We're already at a point where a single vampire being targeted has led to the Prince of the city exposing some of their key pawns, risking some of the most highly placed human servants they have just because one vampire got targeted by some Hunters who have mastered the secret art of the anonymous tip-off.<br /> <br /> We can debate back and forth forever how events unfold from there. Sometimes the Hunters will win, sometimes the Vampires will win. We can't state who will win more often to any objective standpoint because we have no baseline reality to draw statistics from, and the situation is complicated enough that I don't think it boils down as simply as &quot;the side with supernatural powers wins&quot; anymore. The fact is that how it unfolds is just 100% dependent on the Chronicle in which these events take place. But we do have a great starting point for a game I think, both from the perspective of a Vampire group and from the perspective of a Hunter group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T09:32:14-07:00","id":1108793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108735#post1108735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those who are talking about humanity's ability to function as a society don't realize that the monsters can do the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>My dude, this is a crass falsehood to anyone with pattern recognition.<br /> <br /> Powerful monsters remain integrated with their societies as a function of their ability and willingness to work with each other, and the greater upkeep and room for abuse more power affords the big kids means tensions run <i>high</i>.<br /> <br /> An elder werewolf whose predatory nature has grown to the point where the only thing that will sustain them is Essence and their spiritual stability all but demands that they undertake a meaningful hunt twice a week or nosedive into cannibalism or full-time Shadow-dwelling. An ancient Promethean makes Wastelands with trivial expenditures of Pyros and has more to gain from giving into Torment than resisting its pull. Powerful changelings outside of a well-kept Hollow are magnets for the fae and need to meddle with emotional byproducts on an increasingly regular basis. Master mages increasingly run up against the limits of their spell control unless they shamelessly grab for resources in the pursuit of their fix and get more weak spots in their Wisdom as the direct cost of gaining more ways to pick up Mana. Vampires above a certain threshold of Blood Potency can't derive sustenance from non-vampires without draining their own Willpower and will regularly set things up on a locale-warping scale to ensure they can stay active for as long as possible. Beasts get hungry faster the stronger they are. Demons pick up special powers and space for more faces by poking around the thing they're all scared of getting betrayed to. Mummies literally start their active cycle insanely powerful and dangerously obsessed. The list goes on.<br /> <br /> Institutional control of a region by monsters is tenuously maintained at the best of times, and poking it hard enough to compel action forces the puppetmasters to run through contingencies that can and will run out with enough strain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T13:14:27-07:00","id":1108904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108745#post1108745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I should not be nytrua can be an ass he remands me of myself I always wanted to be right good thing I'm not like that no more</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Calling another user an ass is pretty much the definition of a personal attack.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T14:31:49-07:00","id":1108944,"title":"","content":"I'mma just say that all I am getting out of this thread is that life is just as shit for monsters as it is for humans in the CoD World and the only reason they shouldn't all just kill themselves is that at least two gamelines prove/suggest the closest thing most people are going to get to an afterlife is either just as bad or worse.<br /> <br /> EDIT: plus, really hard for a Mummy, Vamp or Sin-eater to kill themselves. And the only way I can think of for a Werewolf to do the deed would be silver and that's stupidly more painful than pills or snapping your neck with a noose","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 06-28-2017, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T20:09:49-07:00","id":1109089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108944#post1108944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'mma just say that all I am getting out of this thread is that life is just as shit for monsters as it is for humans in the CoD World and the only reason they shouldn't all just kill themselves is that at least two gamelines prove/suggest the closest thing most people are going to get to an afterlife is either just as bad or worse.<br /> <br /> EDIT: plus, really hard for a Mummy, Vamp or Sin-eater to kill themselves. And the only way I can think of for a Werewolf to do the deed would be silver and that's stupidly more painful than pills or snapping your neck with a noose</div> </div> </div> </div>@werewolf suicide: yep, most would survive a terminal velocity fall too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T22:21:10-07:00","id":1109115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1108944#post1108944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'mma just say that all I am getting out of this thread is that life is just as shit for monsters as it is for humans in the CoD World and the only reason they shouldn't all just kill themselves is that at least two gamelines prove/suggest the closest thing most people are going to get to an afterlife is either just as bad or worse.<br /> <br /> EDIT: plus, really hard for a Mummy, Vamp or Sin-eater to kill themselves. And the only way I can think of for a Werewolf to do the deed would be silver and that's stupidly more painful than pills or snapping your neck with a noose</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything the gamelines suggests there is no afterlife at all. Souls doesn't contain the consciousness of people so the fact that nobody knows what happens with them after death is irrelevant, and ghosts aren't direct continuations of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T00:28:58-07:00","id":1109134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109115#post1109115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If anything the gamelines suggests there is no afterlife at all. Souls doesn't contain the consciousness of people so the fact that nobody knows what happens with them after death is irrelevant, and ghosts aren't direct continuations of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know about that one. IIRC (and it has been a while I'll admit) Geist at the very least was very suggestive about the presence of an afterlife, particularly when it expressed the differences between helping a ghost to resolve its anchors and move on versus simply destroying a ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T01:22:29-07:00","id":1109145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109134#post1109134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't know about that one. IIRC (and it has been a while I'll admit) Geist at the very least was very suggestive about the presence of an afterlife, particularly when it expressed the differences between helping a ghost to resolve its anchors and move on versus simply destroying a ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's great (or terrible) for ghosts, but again, at least in 2E, they are not the person that died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T03:59:12-07:00","id":1109175,"title":"","content":"It'd be even more horrifying if ghosts <i>were</i> the same people since only some people leave ghosts behind when they die (and an extreme minority creates ghosts at near-death experiences).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T05:09:35-07:00","id":1109187,"title":"","content":"Don't mummies prove the existence of an afterlife, though? Considering their origin story is that they literally went to the underworld and met the judges of the dead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T06:02:56-07:00","id":1109200,"title":"","content":"I'm not particularly well-versed in Mummy, but my understanding is that they went to a place that they interpreted as an afterlife due to the Rite of Return, the grandest rite of magic ever performed. Afaik there's nothing that proves that regular people end up there when they die, but I could be severely mistaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T06:14:29-07:00","id":1109204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109200#post1109200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not particularly well-versed in Mummy, but my understanding is that they went to a place that they interpreted as an afterlife due to the Rite of Return, the grandest rite of magic ever performed. Afaik there's nothing that proves that regular people end up there when they die, but I could be severely mistaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all told through unreliable narrators with no first-hand accounts (Anpu seems to be the origin of a lot of this information), but the Book of the Deceived and Dreams of Avarice both indicate that regular human souls pass to Duat as well. There they are judged by the 42 Judges of Life, and those souls who are worthy move on to A'aru. Or at least they did in the time of Irem... there's a very real chance the Rite screwed that up when it supplanted the God of the Dead from his rightful place in the cosmology and created 42 Judges of Death.<br /> <br /> It's real easy to question how reliable this information is (both Dreams and Deceived present their texts as having been written by in-universe characters who are not necessarily the most reliable folk on the planet, and the Book of the Deceived treats it as second-hand information because the Shan'iatu's forms can't pass on from the physical plane), but I hold it to be true enough when I'm running Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T06:50:03-07:00","id":1109221,"title":"","content":"Whether or not a ghost is the person who died is also an interesting question. We're informed it's not, but from the ghost's perspective at least, there's no practical difference. The ghost has the memories of the person, so it might as well be a continuation of that consciousness. The real question is what, if anything, becomes of the original consciousness from its own perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T09:50:22-07:00","id":1109287,"title":"","content":"There's plenty of reason to believe that Duat and Starry A'aru exist, so yeah, there is <i>a</i> afterlife. There's also the Underworld and the states within and beyond it (Particularly beyond if ghosts as people doesn't satisfy you), and a close look at the metaphysical value of Death crossed over with obvious inferences from the Lie of the Psychopomp implies not only are there afterlives, but it is the true nature of people to decide which one is theirs.<br /> <br /> Where there are gods, there are lands of the dead, and the Chronicles world is <i>lousy</i> with gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T11:12:01-07:00","id":1109328,"title":"","content":"I think the question is not &quot;is there an afterlife?&quot;, but &quot;do once-living beings experience themselves existing there?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T11:51:27-07:00","id":1109338,"title":"","content":"I feel like I'm woefully misremembering something. Exactly where does it express that ghosts are a different person, and from whose perspective?<br /> <br /> And, perhaps just as important, what is the tool used to determine that they are entirely different entities, and not simply a changed entity? I mean, it's said that by the time seven years passes, every cell in your body is an entirely different cell - one could argue that you are not the person you were those years ago in a literal sense as much as a psychological sense. So by what metric do we determine there is a separation? What defines you as you, and the ghost as not-you? Is it the presence of a physical body? The presence of a soul? And why would either matter, since you can be you while existing without either?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T14:10:17-07:00","id":1109393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109328#post1109328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the question is not &quot;is there an afterlife?&quot;, but &quot;do once-living beings experience themselves existing there?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, if Ghosts aren't the actual person who died, and yet they're the ones traveling around in the afterlife, then we might just say that once you die, that's it. You just cease to exist. Your ghost is just a psychic impression left to satisfy the unfulfilled desires of the fallen.<br /> <br /> The only other explanation is that there is an <i>after</i>-after life, or that the person who died is reincarnated somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-29-2017, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T14:10:21-07:00","id":1109394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109328#post1109328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the question is not &quot;is there an afterlife?&quot;, but &quot;do once-living beings experience themselves existing there?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't be much of an afterlife without self-consciousness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T14:24:49-07:00","id":1109396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109338#post1109338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I'm woefully misremembering something. Exactly where does it express that ghosts are a different person, and from whose perspective?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can create a Ghost of someone without them dying and you can resurrect someone who died and their Ghost doesn't go poof.<br /> <br /> As for the continuity of consicouness bit, that's what is being discussed in the last few posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T15:06:46-07:00","id":1109420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109393#post1109393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if Ghosts aren't the actual person who died, and yet they're the ones traveling around in the afterlife, then we might just say that once you die, that's it. You just cease to exist. Your ghost is just a psychic impression left to satisfy the unfulfilled desires of the fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, ghosts in CofD <i>are</i> just impressions left to satisfy the unfulfilled desires of the Fallen. They are also conscious, thinking entities that share the memories of the person who's death created them. That really doesn't tell us what happens to the person. And I'm pretty sure that's intentional on the part of the writers. As much as they may detail various afterlives such as the Underworld, Duat, etc., they leave it open to interpretation what happens to &quot;you&quot;. &quot;You&quot; might poof out of existence. Then again, &quot;you&quot; might go to [insert afterlife of your preferred religion here]. CofD doesn't really give us enough information to settle on a definitive answer, and I believe that is to its credit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109393#post1109393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only other explanation is that there is an <i>after</i>-after life, or that the person who died is reincarnated somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is <i>a</i> possible explanation, but not the only one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T15:13:25-07:00","id":1109424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109338#post1109338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I'm woefully misremembering something. Exactly where does it express that ghosts are a different person, and from whose perspective?<br /> <br /> And, perhaps just as important, what is the tool used to determine that they are entirely different entities, and not simply a changed entity? I mean, it's said that by the time seven years passes, every cell in your body is an entirely different cell - one could argue that you are not the person you were those years ago in a literal sense as much as a psychological sense. So by what metric do we determine there is a separation? What defines you as you, and the ghost as not-you? Is it the presence of a physical body? The presence of a soul? And why would either matter, since you can be you while existing without either?</div> </div> </div> </div>What ElvesOfZion said. Also, that thing &quot;they say&quot; about every cell in your body being replaced every seven years isn't actually true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZCiuMomjVx0\" data-code=\"ZCiuMomjVx0\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZCiuMomjVx0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T17:18:28-07:00","id":1109489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109396#post1109396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can create a Ghost of someone without them dying and you can resurrect someone who died and their Ghost doesn't go poof.<br /> <br /> As for the continuity of consicouness bit, that's what is being discussed in the last few posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of making a ghost though, it specifically says the ghost is not the person. Your not making that person's ghost - your just creating something based off of them at that point. If I used life magic to make a person that was in every way another person, that would not be the person either. With resurrection, I can't really make a case since the only resurrection ability I know is Deny the Reaper and it doesn't actually say that a person's ghosts persists (or touch upon ghosts at all).<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, mage only says that ghosts are not the souls of the dead and argue over whether or not they are the person's actual personality or part of the original soul - and Beasts put ghosts in the 'fundamentally human' category - which, if they were never human, is a category they would not actually be in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T19:20:49-07:00","id":1109546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109420#post1109420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, ghosts in CofD <i>are</i> just impressions left to satisfy the unfulfilled desires of the Fallen. They are also conscious, thinking entities that share the memories of the person who's death created them. That really doesn't tell us what happens to the person. And I'm pretty sure that's intentional on the part of the writers. As much as they may detail various afterlives such as the Underworld, Duat, etc., they leave it open to interpretation what happens to &quot;you&quot;. &quot;You&quot; might poof out of existence. Then again, &quot;you&quot; might go to [insert afterlife of your preferred religion here]. CofD doesn't really give us enough information to settle on a definitive answer, and I believe that is to its credit.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, if the books have been intentionally vague and leaves it up to our interpretation, then I'm going to guess that they are all true / untrue. Whatever version of an afterlife does / doesn't exist is entirely up to the Story Teller for that given chronicle.<br /> <br /> Which, if that's the case, then it's a good decision, as it doesn't risk stepping on anybody's toes. Whatever iteration of the here after you feel like implementing, it's your call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T19:46:34-07:00","id":1109553,"title":"","content":"Sorry for derailing the topic with my angry-depressed rant","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T19:50:05-07:00","id":1109556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109393#post1109393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, if Ghosts aren't the actual person who died, and yet they're the ones traveling around in the afterlife, then we might just say that once you die, that's it. You just cease to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Utter cessation of existence sounds like the best option in CoD world. Only oWoD where we got at least 5 active apocalypses going on is worse","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T20:41:08-07:00","id":1109576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109556#post1109556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Utter cessation of existence sounds like the best option in CoD world. Only oWoD where we got at least 5 active apocalypses going on is worse</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. Ascension seems like a good enough afterlife if you can manage it. You basically still cease to exist, but you also get to retroactively rewrite your symbolism into reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T20:47:18-07:00","id":1109578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109221#post1109221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether or not a ghost is the person who died is also an interesting question. We're informed it's not, but from the ghost's perspective at least, there's no practical difference. The ghost has the memories of the person, so it might as well be a continuation of that consciousness. The real question is what, if anything, becomes of the original consciousness from its own perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel it's worth pointing out that in those cases where the distinction between a ghost of a person and its basis is something that might matter, similar types of uncertainty are brought up to those exhibited by a fetch.<br /> <br /> The mnemonic fidelity of supernatural replicants is forever in doubt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T21:29:41-07:00","id":1109600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109556#post1109556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Utter cessation of existence sounds like the best option in CoD world. Only oWoD where we got at least 5 active apocalypses going on is worse</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah, sounds pretty peaceful. I wrote up a fan made 1E bloodline for Requiem involving vampires who are actively searching for a way to achieve just that. They exclusively embraced suicide victims, and were inspired by myths about such people becoming vampires after death.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109578#post1109578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel it's worth pointing out that in those cases where the distinction between a ghost of a person and its basis is something that might matter, similar types of uncertainty are brought up to those exhibited by a fetch.<br /> <br /> The mnemonic fidelity of supernatural replicants is forever in doubt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, I'm curious as to why the heck it even matters If ghosts in CoD are laid to rest properly. If they're not the actual person who died, but just an echo of their lingering desires and the real individual is missing in action somewhere, then it doesn't particularly matter. The real person has moved on somewhere else and the ghost is just floating around the ether because the plot says so. Destroying the ghost outright seems like the faster and more logical option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-30-2017, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T21:35:25-07:00","id":1109603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109556#post1109556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Utter cessation of existence sounds like the best option in CoD world. Only oWoD where we got at least 5 active apocalypses going on is worse</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how the Hounds of Beliar win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T21:43:56-07:00","id":1109607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109556#post1109556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Utter cessation of existence sounds like the best option in CoD world. Only oWoD where we got at least 5 active apocalypses going on is worse</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you I say this as someone who would rather be a human than a supernatural, this is a really bleak response to becoming a monsters. Sure, you may have just gotten the short end of the stick in some ways, but there are still, meaningful, impactful and enjoyable lives to be had as a monster.<br /> <br /> Fatalism is a crap answer, is what I'm saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T21:46:02-07:00","id":1109610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109603#post1109603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's how the Hounds of Beliar win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me guess: Bale Hound Servants of Sloth?<br /> <br /> Funk it, they might have something going there, so long as they eventually take their own advice","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 06-30-2017, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T21:48:58-07:00","id":1109612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109607#post1109607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you I say this as someone who would rather be a human than a supernatural, this is a really bleak response to becoming a monsters. Sure, you may have just gotten the short end of the stick in some ways, but there are still, meaningful, impactful and enjoyable lives to be had as a monster.<br /> <br /> Fatalism is a crap answer, is what I'm saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said this was a response to becoming a monster? I was saying it would be best cade for anyone born into a universe as phenomenally crapped up ad the CoD multiverse. Bear in mind, not sayimg this about the real world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T21:52:10-07:00","id":1109614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109600#post1109600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'm curious as to why the heck it even matters If ghosts in CoD are laid to rest properly. If they're not the actual person who died, but just an echo of their lingering desires and the real individual is missing in action somewhere, then it doesn't particularly matter. The real person has moved on somewhere else and the ghost is just floating around the ether because the plot says so. Destroying the ghost outright seems like the faster and more logical option.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're still (often) a sentient being dude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T21:59:04-07:00","id":1109618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109600#post1109600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'm curious as to why the heck it even matters If ghosts in CoD are laid to rest properly. If they're not the actual person who died, but just an echo of their lingering desires and the real individual is missing in action somewhere, then it doesn't particularly matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inheritance law is a tangle and a half.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The real person has moved on somewhere else and the ghost is just floating around the ether because the plot says so. Destroying the ghost outright seems like the faster and more logical option. </div> </div> </div>This is magic we're talking about; similarity that striking tends to have deeper implications. The fact that nobody's quite sure <i>how</i> ghosts get their personalities means there is a very real possibility that it's a hostage situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T21:59:10-07:00","id":1109619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109614#post1109614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're still (often) a sentient being dude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus it's not something everyone is going to know, especially when said ghost looks and acts like the person and knows things only they could know.<br /> <br /> It's easy to make 'logical' decisions when you have the corebook and the decisions don't affect you. Most characters don't have those advantages..<br /> <br /> As an aside, I like the idea of Taga Dan and keep it real in my settings. Though there's ways around it, like Maeladar. Werewolves only, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T22:47:43-07:00","id":1109635,"title":"","content":"On the whole being a monster (again by that i mean one of the supernatural splat) means becoming a more powerful version of yourself, a strange thoughts occurs to me.<br /> Although i've not played every game, i have read the core of every game and i have always the habit of transposing my own self into whatever monster i'm reading about. The book that made me ... feel i guess, the most empowered, the most superior wasn't any of the monster splat (not even mage). It was Hunter the Vigil (and by extension the regular mortal core book). And i dont even mean the more powerful members of the big conspiracies, really just a regular mortal at the lowest tier is enough. I guess there is something for me that just <i>knowing </i>about the supernatural and deciding that I won't be the prey, nor will i let my loved one being prey to monster, no matter how much more powerful then me they are feel very empowering and makes me feel like i'd become a ... better version of myself perhaps.<br /> In the end I suppose that it means that for me winning a 1v1 fight is not a mesure of superiority in any sense that matters. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T09:08:51-07:00","id":1109784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109578#post1109578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel it's worth pointing out that in those cases where the distinction between a ghost of a person and its basis is something that might matter, similar types of uncertainty are brought up to those exhibited by a fetch.<br /> <br /> The mnemonic fidelity of supernatural replicants is forever in doubt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting notion assuming we define identity as the collection of memories of the individual. Even more difficult to perceive in character with the lack of clear simulacrums to place bets on which identity is the original one.<br /> <br /> Ghosts are ultimately shades of their former selves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T09:46:10-07:00","id":1109800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109784#post1109784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghosts are ultimately shades of their former selves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't we all, though? We all change over time, sometimes dramatically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T09:53:47-07:00","id":1109806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109420#post1109420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, ghosts in CofD <i>are</i> just impressions left to satisfy the unfulfilled desires of the Fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't find a source for this in the CofD core book. Where can I find it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T10:03:39-07:00","id":1109811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109635#post1109635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the whole being a monster (again by that i mean one of the supernatural splat) means becoming a more powerful version of yourself, a strange thoughts occurs to me.<br /> Although i've not played every game, i have read the core of every game and i have always the habit of transposing my own self into whatever monster i'm reading about. </div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's called Self Insertion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I used to do it all the time, even naming characters after myself when I first got into role playing. Gradually weaned off that as I got more experienced, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T13:01:29-07:00","id":1109884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109806#post1109806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't find a source for this in the CofD core book. Where can I find it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really explicitly stated as such, but it can be inferred by the way ghosts work in-setting. As mentioned earlier, not all deaths create ghosts, some ghosts are created without the person from whom they came dying, and being brought back to life doesn't destroy a ghost someone left behind. Also, Mages can clearly observe that ghosts are not souls and do not have souls, and while the soul is not the self in CofD, a soul is needed for a human to maintain a self in the long-term (I like to think of the self as a liquid and the soul as the container that holds the liquid).<br /> <br /> Ghosts are indeed sentient (or at least semi-sentient, in the case of Rank 0 and 1) entities, but they clearly can't be the same entities as the humans that spawn them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T13:35:45-07:00","id":1109909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109884#post1109884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really explicitly stated as such, but it can be inferred by the way ghosts work in-setting. As mentioned earlier, not all deaths create ghosts, some ghosts are created without the person from whom they came dying, and being brought back to life doesn't destroy a ghost someone left behind. Also, Mages can clearly observe that ghosts are not souls and do not have souls, and while the soul is not the self in CofD, a soul is needed for a human to maintain a self in the long-term (I like to think of the self as a liquid and the soul as the container that holds the liquid).<br /> <br /> Ghosts are indeed sentient (or at least semi-sentient, in the case of Rank 0 and 1) entities, but they clearly can't be the same entities as the humans that spawn them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is - and I already pointed this out in response to that - is that at least one book (Beast) actually puts evidence to the fact that ghosts -have- been human. If they were not the same entities as the humans that spawn them, that would mean that they were never in fact human to begin with. The other books don't really seem to imply this kind of a difference between the people who die and their ghosts.<br /> <br /> The problem with the evidence of resurrection or of using magic to create ghosts is... first, resurrection doesn't actually express what it does to ghosts if a ghost is created. As far as &quot;Create Ghost&quot;, that's literally a Making spell, something you are creating wholesale. It's a magically created ghostly homunculus that is specifically -not- the person who you are mimicking - dead or alive - but that does not mean that the naturally created ghosts are not still the humans. All it means is that you can use magic to create a ghost-clone.<br /> <br /> It seems to me kind of a stretch to say that they aren't the same entities as the humans that spawned them. I would agree, however, with the assessment that they are not the <i>complete</i> entities of the humans they were in life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T13:46:07-07:00","id":1109920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109884#post1109884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really explicitly stated as such, but it can be inferred by the way ghosts work in-setting. As mentioned earlier, not all deaths create ghosts, some ghosts are created without the person from whom they came dying, and being brought back to life doesn't destroy a ghost someone left behind. Also, Mages can clearly observe that ghosts are not souls and do not have souls, and while the soul is not the self in CofD, a soul is needed for a human to maintain a self in the long-term (I like to think of the self as a liquid and the soul as the container that holds the liquid).<br /> <br /> Ghosts are indeed sentient (or at least semi-sentient, in the case of Rank 0 and 1) entities, but they clearly can't be the same entities as the humans that spawn them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks much. I may take a different direction in my own game but knowing the default is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T13:56:37-07:00","id":1109926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109909#post1109909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me kind of a stretch to say that they aren't the same entities as the humans that spawned them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts have mortal Anchor Traits and a humanlike appearance, cannot diverge far from human levels of ability without interacting with a markedly unstable supernatural realm, and are principally differentiated from humans given access to chthonic powers and converted to deathly ephemera by what their isolation and obsession does to them. They're closer in nature to mortal psychics (who genre literature happens to also associate with them) and occult-junkie Awakened than the mutative existences of the Kindred, the Created, or the Lost, or the territorial fixations of the Arisen, the Begotten, or the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fundamentally human&quot; is a category that exists in Beast to distinguish a monster as <i>less inhuman</i> than its fellows \u2014 the sad ghost of Isaac Donahue is &quot;mostly human, but&quot; rather than being a chunk of a person that's been totally transformed into or merged with a supernatural being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T15:37:25-07:00","id":1109948,"title":"","content":"Additionally, that a ghost is &quot;fundamentally human&quot; does not mean it's <i>the same human</i> as the one who spawned it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T15:59:09-07:00","id":1109956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109926#post1109926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts have mortal Anchor Traits and a humanlike appearance, cannot diverge far from human levels of ability without interacting with a markedly unstable supernatural realm, and are principally differentiated from humans given access to chthonic powers and converted to deathly ephemera by what their isolation and obsession does to them. They're closer in nature to mortal psychics (who genre literature happens to also associate with them) and occult-junkie Awakened than the mutative existences of the Kindred, the Created, or the Lost, or the territorial fixations of the Arisen, the Begotten, or the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fundamentally human&quot; is a category that exists in Beast to distinguish a monster as <i>less inhuman</i> than its fellows \u2014 the sad ghost of Isaac Donahue is &quot;mostly human, but&quot; rather than being a chunk of a person that's been totally transformed into or merged with a supernatural being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. But that -doesn't- in any way suggest that the sad ghost of Isaac Donahue was not in fact Isaac Donahue at one point. If it wasn't, it was someone - otherwise it would have never been human. If a ghost was just a psuedo-copy of a person rather than the actual person, it'd fall more closely in line with a fetch - which <i>is</i> a pseudo-copy of a person, and qualifies as 'Descended from the dark mother' because of the fact that it was -never human to begin with-, no matter how human-like it may seem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109948#post1109948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, that a ghost is &quot;fundamentally human&quot; does not mean it's <i>the same human</i> as the one who spawned it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is possible. The only problem of course is this still implies that the ghost was a human at one point, and if it was -not- the same human that spawned it, you then have to figure what connection this 'other person' has with the human, and what process it is that one changes from a human to a ghost that also makes it so that you are not the ghost of yourself. There is really nothing to suggest that another person would become someone else's ghost, rather than their own.<br /> <hr /><br /> Edit: Don't get me wrong though - the idea that ghosts might not be a part of the people who they represent is an interesting one - and certainly a horrifying notion to those who put faith in that sort of thing. I just don't see the alleged 'implications' that they aren't - and in fact, can see multiple signs in the books that I would use that seem to suggest the exact opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 06-30-2017, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T17:09:17-07:00","id":1109970,"title":"","content":"Trying to imagine how awkward becoming somebody else's ghost would be, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T17:09:17-07:00","id":1109971,"title":"","content":"<b>Edit: </b>Wow, post reply button just shat its pants!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T17:21:49-07:00","id":1109975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109956#post1109956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. But that -doesn't- in any way suggest that the sad ghost of Isaac Donahue was not in fact Isaac Donahue at one point.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, actually \u2014 the ghost of Isaac Donahue did not exist before Isaac Donahue died and nothing we're told about Isaac Donahue suggests he used to have a ghost inside him rather than something that turned into his ghost or got picked up by something else to make it &quot;the ghost of Isaac Donahue.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it wasn't, it was someone - otherwise it would have never been human. If a ghost was just a psuedo-copy of a person rather than the actual person, it'd fall more closely in line with a fetch - which <i>is</i> a pseudo-copy of a person, and qualifies as 'Descended from the dark mother' because of the fact that it was -never human to begin with-, no matter how human-like it may seem. </div> </div> </div>A fetch is an animate construction of faerie dross made into a placeholder for a real person by the donation of part of that person's shadow. There is a meaningful distinction to be made between that and what happens to part of your spiritual makeup when you die in the wrong way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is possible. The only problem of course is this still implies that the ghost was a human at one point, </div> </div> </div>It does not. Again: &quot;mostly human, but\u2026&quot; A Temenotic Resident is literally just a regular human being who happens to be a Rank 1 invisible entity inhabiting the collective unconscious. Derived humanity does not imply continuity of identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T18:19:39-07:00","id":1109985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109975#post1109975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does, actually \u2014 the ghost of Isaac Donahue did not exist before Isaac Donahue died and nothing we're told about Isaac Donahue suggests he used to have a ghost inside him rather than something that turned into his ghost or got picked up by something else to make it &quot;the ghost of Isaac Donahue.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the very first statements defining what ghosts are in most of the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Core 122, Beast 183</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;When human beings die, especially in a sudden or traumatic fashion, <b>they sometimes leave parts of themselves behind</b>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109975#post1109975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fetch is an animate construction of faerie dross made into a placeholder for a real person by the donation of part of that person's shadow. There is a meaningful distinction to be made between that and what happens to part of your spiritual makeup when you die in the wrong way.</div> </div> </div> </div>See its things like this that make me wonder if we're debating or agreeing here. Because that's part of my point - a fetch never was human. It's an animate construction made from faerie dross and a piece of that person (not necessarily their shadow, but sometimes). It's made -from- a human and from faerie, sure - but never was one. A ghost on the other hand -was- human. So far, no one has bothered to point out where it suggests anything besides the fact that a ghost is not what remained of the human after they died. It's not their soul (proven in mage) but their soul doesn't make them 'them'. But it -is- a part of them. Some mages suggest that it's a piece of their soul. Others suggest that it is their mind and personality. But not once have I seen anything suggesting it's <i>not them at all</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109975#post1109975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does not. Again: &quot;mostly human, but\u2026&quot; A Temenotic Resident is literally just a regular human being who happens to be a Rank 1 invisible entity inhabiting the collective unconscious. Derived humanity does not imply continuity of identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... What? Exactly -how- is a Goetia a regular human being?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, exactly how does 'derived humanity' equate to 'Mostly human, but...'? If one made a robot and gave it a conscious, it would not be mostly human, no matter how much of their heart and soul placed it, nor how much of what we call &quot;humanity&quot; you managed to give it. The book we're referencing here defines the categories as &quot;Born of the Dark Mother&quot;, &quot;Fundamentally Human&quot; or &quot;Kinship does not apply&quot;. It's a very simple metric: Born of the Dark Mother states they either &quot;Were never human&quot; or &quot;Were human but have since been totally transformed or merged with a supernatural being.&quot; Then it has the other, which is &quot;Mostly Human, but...&quot;<br /> <br /> If anything, the fact that they don't fall into the category of &quot;Was never human&quot; or &quot;has been totally transformed&quot; is more suggestive that the ghostly state is a more natural transitionary and supernatural part of being human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 06-30-2017, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T19:02:28-07:00","id":1109998,"title":"","content":"Okay, so going by the CoD explanation on how the hell a person is a person (being that their existence is split between multiple different factors), then I think that pretty much supports the Duat theory. The ancient Egyptians believed the soul was divided into multiple parts, and CoD seems to be having a difficult time explaining what actually constitutes a person's identity and existence.<br /> <br /> So if the CoD says there are multiple parts to who / what a person is, and we've got mummies roaming around who ventured into the Egyptian underworld, then that would logically credit Duat as being the answer here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Outside of Chronicles of Darkness, I consider a person's true existence to be their soul. I have never been told otherwise until I was introduced to this series. Your soul is the very essence of who you are, and without your soul, your body is just a mindless shell.<br /> <br /> In CoD, however, this is clearly not the case, as you people keep pointing out. Meaning that there's this entirely alien concept of existence that I can't wrap my mind around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-30-2017, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T20:53:43-07:00","id":1110037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109985#post1109985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the very first statements defining what ghosts are in most of the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. A part of a thing is not the thing itself. My liver donation is not me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A ghost on the other hand -was- human. </div> </div> </div>A ghost has a reasonable claim on being an ex-aspect of a former human. The part is not the whole, but prior to a dunk in the Below neither is it significantly Something Else. <i>Ceci n'est pas une forumgoer.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But not once have I seen anything suggesting it's <i>not them at all</i>. </div> </div> </div>Nobody's saying &quot;at all.&quot; The ghost of a person does not exist without that person as at minimum a referent. But the snow angel I make flipping end over end out of my windshield on a particularly shitty New Year's Eve is not me no matter how many of my pores it picks up or how much of my blood sticks to the impression. Some liches aim to bind their Awakened souls and their personalities together in pursuit of immortality, but that's both a product of deliberate effort and a thing held together by spit and Mystery rather than the ectoplasmic mold that some poor sod smacked his face into when he kicked the bucket.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Um... What? Exactly -how- is a Goetia a regular human being? </div> </div> </div>They have no supernatural abilities and inhabit a space where the state of Twilight does not exist and serve as slightly more colorful standouts among the throng of &quot;inhabitants&quot; in the Temenos that are literally just extensions of the scenery. They are literally just human personalities with a presented human self-image who happen to have a minor Rank and a PFR Attribute spread.<br /> <br /> You may notice dev and writer observations in some of the Geist 2e threads on the forums that even ghosts as low-spec as Manes are still functionally just people. This is not that weird.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If anything, the fact that they don't fall into the category of &quot;Was never human&quot; or &quot;has been totally transformed&quot; is more suggestive that the ghostly state is a more natural transitionary and supernatural part of being human. </div> </div> </div>Did I somehow not repeatedly point out the <i>giant radioactive hellpit </i>that new ghosts are kept out of for as long as they have an anchor? Was I introduced to some aspect of ghosthood unawares that treats the expression of an established mortal self-image in a supernatural medium as interchangeable with wholesale fabrication of a conscious perspective shoved into an unfamiliar body? Has the titular entity of Geist retroactively changed when I wasn't looking to not be &quot;a human ghost made strange or something strange made passingly human through the energies of the Underworld&quot;?<br /> <br /> Much of the literature does indicate that ghosts aren't &quot;supposed&quot; to happen. The Underworld at the very least does not currently have a guaranteed teleological output line keeping its inhabitants from simply dissolving into the depths as the years wear on. Ghosts happen because something broke off in the door to beyond and remembered what it used to fit into, not because of The Imperishability Of The Complex Human. Entropy calls and something that can fake it really well answers for the absentees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T21:06:28-07:00","id":1110041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109998#post1109998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so going by the CoD explanation on how the hell a person is a person (being that their existence is split between multiple different factors), then I think that pretty much supports the Duat theory. The ancient Egyptians believed the soul was divided into multiple parts, and CoD seems to be having a difficult time explaining what actually constitutes a person's identity and existence.<br /> <br /> So if the CoD says there are multiple parts to who / what a person is, and we've got mummies roaming around who ventured into the Egyptian underworld, then that would logically credit Duat as being the answer here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Outside of Chronicles of Darkness, I consider a person's true existence to be their soul. I have never been told otherwise until I was introduced to this series. Your soul is the very essence of who you are, and without your soul, your body is just a mindless shell.<br /> <br /> In CoD, however, this is clearly not the case, as you people keep pointing out. Meaning that there's this entirely alien concept of existence that I can't wrap my mind around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in CofD, there's kind of multiple levels of &quot;soul.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's the &quot;self-soul&quot;, which is the actual person in question. In Mummy terms, their Ab and Ba.<br /> <br /> Then there's the &quot;essence-soul,&quot; which is the part that produces Essence and/or Mana, gets ripped out by the Embrace, causes the Soul Loss condition when lost, and is the Mummy's Ka.<br /> <br /> Then there's the &quot;attached soul,&quot; which is how the soul connects to the rest of reality and to other souls. It's what becomes a Ghost, what a Demon takes in Soul Pacts, and what's bound by Fairy Oaths. That's the Ren and Sheut.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T22:42:50-07:00","id":1110062,"title":"","content":"While a ghost might not be the same person that it spawned from, it might still be considered a human. It is spawned from a human in the likness of a human. It inherits traits from the human that spawned it, and can be considered alive in the sense that it's both animate and conscious. It's basically reproduction. Ghosts could be considered a different phenotype of human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110041#post1110041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then there's the &quot;essence-soul,&quot; which is the part that produces Essence and/or Mana, gets ripped out by the Embrace, causes the Soul Loss condition when lost, and is the Mummy's Ka.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can point out that ancient Egyptian Mekhet believed that their Ka was severed and caused them to lose their shadow and reflection (as well as having the Ka haunt them in the form of, guess what, a ghost). If that's true then all vampires that aren't Hollow Mekhet would still retain their Ka.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T01:43:59-07:00","id":1110096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110041#post1110041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then there's the &amp;quot;essence-soul,&amp;quot; which is the part that produces Essence and/or Mana, gets ripped out by the Embrace, causes the Soul Loss condition when lost, and is the Mummy's Ka.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since when did that get part of the soul get ripped out during the embrace? As far as I was aware it was at worst damaged unless you were a hollow mekhet, and in that case it was ripped out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T04:31:14-07:00","id":1110122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109998#post1109998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so going by the CoD explanation on how the hell a person is a person (being that their existence is split between multiple different factors), then I think that pretty much supports the Duat theory. The ancient Egyptians believed the soul was divided into multiple parts, and CoD seems to be having a difficult time explaining what actually constitutes a person's identity and existence.<br /> <br /> So if the CoD says there are multiple parts to who / what a person is, and we've got mummies roaming around who ventured into the Egyptian underworld, then that would logically credit Duat as being the answer here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Outside of Chronicles of Darkness, I consider a person's true existence to be their soul. I have never been told otherwise until I was introduced to this series. Your soul is the very essence of who you are, and without your soul, your body is just a mindless shell.<br /> <br /> In CoD, however, this is clearly not the case, as you people keep pointing out. Meaning that there's this entirely alien concept of existence that I can't wrap my mind around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of your soul as another body you have. Sometimes you treat the body as a whole. Sometimes you get a bunch of organs that have to be accounted for separately.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The &quot;essence of what you are&quot; is what mummies refer to as the Ka (Essence), which is also what mages refer to as the Prime-aspect of the soul.<br /> <br /> Your consciousness and your personality, the lack of which would make you a &quot;mindless shell&quot;, is what mummies refer to as the Ba (Spirit), which is also what mages refer to as the Mind-aspect of the soul.<br /> <br /> And then you have your emotions and passions and feelings and the Libido. That is what mummies refer to as the Ab (Heart), which is also what mages refer to as the Spirit-aspect of the soul. (I disagree with malonkey here, in that if the Embrace damages a part of the soul, then this is probably what gets damaged. And that this part is what probably creates Resonance, which in turn creates Essence. The Hollow Mekhet simply have even more of their soul damaged.)<br /> <br /> Then you have... your &quot;karma,&quot; for lack of a better word. Your actions and intentions, and your identity that springs out from those things. That is what mummies refer to as the Ren (Name), which is also what mages refer to as the Fate-aspect of the soul.<br /> <br /> Finally, in your heart you have your darkness. The icky stuff that you'd rather not face, but nevertheless is a part of you and what anchors you to this world. Think of the Shadow Archetype in Jungian psychology, and the Thanatos in Freudian psychology. That is what mummies refer to as the Sheut (Shadow), which is also what mages refer to as the Death-aspect of the soul.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I'm not clear on Mummy lore outside the corebook... but it seems that we also have the True Name (which I think is the objective definition of who you are, rather than the subjective definition of who you are that is the Ka?), and the Will (which I think is that &quot;free will&quot; stuff we often see in fiction?) I'll have to get the Mummy pdfs to know for sure, so don't count me on the last two!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T07:17:20-07:00","id":1110151,"title":"","content":"Note, however, that a person who loses their soul does still retain their personality and memories, at least for a while. It'll eventually all degrade until they become a Thrall if they don't get <i>a</i> soul before long. But it doesn't really matter if it's <i>the same</i> soul as the one they lost. Also, when a human dies, all the various soul parts go *somewhere else*, and even if a ghost is created, it's not made out of the soul or any of its parts. At least, from the way it's described in Mage. I haven't read Mummy, so if something in it contradicts the above... well, then that's CofD for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T07:40:52-07:00","id":1110157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1109800#post1109800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't we all, though? We all change over time, sometimes dramatically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, someone's depressed. Hang in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T08:05:38-07:00","id":1110165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110062#post1110062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a ghost might not be the same person that it spawned from, it might still be considered a human. It is spawned from a human in the likness of a human. It inherits traits from the human that spawned it, and can be considered alive in the sense that it's both animate and conscious. It's basically reproduction. Ghosts could be considered a different phenotype of human.</div> </div> </div> </div>My next exorcist will identify himself as a ghost aborter then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T09:05:39-07:00","id":1110210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110165#post1110165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My next exorcist will identify himself as a ghost aborter then.</div> </div> </div> </div>He going to put that on his business cards?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T09:40:55-07:00","id":1110231,"title":"","content":"You know, I'm not seeing something mentioned in this thread that I always consider a major point in World of Darkness: Humans generally don't know what's going on. 90% or so of humans don't know about the supernatural elements, and those who do often k ow more garbage than useful info. That's why Hunters become a major antagonist of the setting: they don't KNOW that Werewolves hunt demons or that Changelings fight Fae, they don't understand anything about the complex ecology at play nor the greater threats which the &quot;monsters&quot; protect the world from. Sometimes you have an occultist who does understand, but the majority of Hunters are spinning to their wheels to basically do nothing of value in a world where most Humans don't even know what's going on...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T09:53:50-07:00","id":1110236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110231#post1110231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I'm not seeing something mentioned in this thread that I always consider a major point in World of Darkness: Humans generally don't know what's going on. 90% or so of humans don't know about the supernatural elements, and those who do often k ow more garbage than useful info. That's why Hunters become a major antagonist of the setting: they don't KNOW that Werewolves hunt demons or that Changelings fight Fae, they don't understand anything about the complex ecology at play nor the greater threats which the &quot;monsters&quot; protect the world from. Sometimes you have an occultist who does understand, but the majority of Hunters are spinning to their wheels to basically do nothing of value in a world where most Humans don't even know what's going on...</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit to being a stickler about this kind of thing, it's another aspect of the thread that has annoyed me. Nowhere in the books does it claim humanity as some superpowered force everyone must cower away from. Nowhere in the books does it say they know everything there is to know about the supernatural, even collectively. I'd be surprised if it says in any game book that someone should be wary of fighting a human because they're going to get killed for daring to fight something so viciously powerful. Humanity isn't declared to be or depicted as overrated in the books at all. Even their lack of innate drawbacks is balanced out by being oblivious prey for everyone else.<br /> <br /> As others have pointed said it's basically just a poorly thought out 'humans suck' thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T13:04:40-07:00","id":1110315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110236#post1110236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit to being a stickler about this kind of thing, it's another aspect of the thread that has annoyed me. Nowhere in the books does it claim humanity as some superpowered force everyone must cower away from. Nowhere in the books does it say they know everything there is to know about the supernatural, even collectively. I'd be surprised if it says in any game book that someone should be wary of fighting a human because they're going to get killed for daring to fight something so viciously powerful. Humanity isn't declared to be or depicted as overrated in the books at all. Even their lack of innate drawbacks is balanced out by being oblivious prey for everyone else.<br /> <br /> As others have pointed said it's basically just a poorly thought out 'humans suck' thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Their ability to engage in killdeath with supernatural creatures has never been presented as humanity's strong suit in CofD. Humanity is generally presented as a positive quality - vampires struggle not to lose it, Prometheans strive to attain it, Sin-Eaters make the most of their second chance at it, Demons imitate it... but it's not desirable because it makes you better at naked 1-on-1 fights in the woods or whatever we were arguing about. It's desirable because humans have a place in the world. They have peace and security and freedom that monsters lack. A cynnic might say it's desirable because humans are ignorant of what's going on in the world and ignorance is bliss (that's kind of the cWoD view). But to the optimist it's about the ability to self-actualize in a way the monsters of CofD can't, bound as they are to cosmic forces beyond mortal reckoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T14:29:14-07:00","id":1110361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110037#post1110037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. A part of a thing is not the thing itself. My liver donation is not me.</div> </div> </div> </div>No - your liver donation is not you. However, your liver also does not have all your memories, your personality, everything that makes you you. It also does not leave your body and develop consciousness to be it's own entity. Your liver donation is better compared to the soul than to what a ghost is. Now - if you took your mind and had a transplant, and then questioned whether or not that mind was you or not, or if the transplant resulted in a wholly different person - that might be a better comparison here.<br /> <br /> When you die, your soul leaves your body (to go elsewhere or to dissipate) as does typically your consciousness - that last part that defines the 'you'. A ghost is clearly written in as both not being a soul, and lacking a soul - and while your soul is important, it is also not you. Now my default is to use the process of elimination here. A ghost is not your soul, so that's easy enough to eliminate. However - what evidence is there that eliminates a ghost from being the consciousness of the person who died? Now you can claim that the old consciousness either vanished or ceased to exist, and that the ghost is an entirely new consciousness that simply is a perfect mirror of an old consciousness - but there is no real method to prove that this is a distinctly different individual, and that seems an unnecessary overcomplication when it lacks sufficient evidence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110037#post1110037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have no supernatural abilities and inhabit a space where the state of Twilight does not exist and serve as slightly more colorful standouts among the throng of &quot;inhabitants&quot; in the Temenos that are literally just extensions of the scenery. They are literally just human personalities with a presented human self-image who happen to have a minor Rank and a PFR Attribute spread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to need a citation on this one. Far as I was aware, they have influences, numen, and also their own default template which allows for the expenditures of essence - which in of itself is a supernatural ability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110037#post1110037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I somehow not repeatedly point out the <i>giant radioactive hellpit </i>that new ghosts are kept out of for as long as they have an anchor? Was I introduced to some aspect of ghosthood unawares that treats the expression of an established mortal self-image in a supernatural medium as interchangeable with wholesale fabrication of a conscious perspective shoved into an unfamiliar body? Has the titular entity of Geist retroactively changed when I wasn't looking to not be &quot;a human ghost made strange or something strange made passingly human through the energies of the Underworld&quot;?<br /> <br /> Much of the literature does indicate that ghosts aren't &quot;supposed&quot; to happen. The Underworld at the very least does not currently have a guaranteed teleological output line keeping its inhabitants from simply dissolving into the depths as the years wear on. Ghosts happen because something broke off in the door to beyond and remembered what it used to fit into, not because of The Imperishability Of The Complex Human. Entropy calls and something that can fake it really well answers for the absentees.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Technically, no, you somehow did not repeatedly point out the underworld. You brought it up in this discussion once, seemingly offhand, in regards to it being a required location in order for a ghost to gain any form of real power. That said, I'm having trouble connecting how the underworld or geists relate to the topics of a ghosts nature. The underworld is a location that tends to draw forth ghosts who have no anchors and still lack resolution. Geists are things which a ghost may turn into (and probably not the only thing a ghost -can- become)<br /> <br /> Now - I don't actually believe ghosts are supposed to happen - at least not in this plane of existence. But that statement actually suggests that something -is- supposed to happen. One could say that a ghost is not supposed to remain here - it is supposed to move on. This does not actually imply that the state of being a ghost is not something that is supposed to occur - just that the state of the ghost remaining -here- isn't.<br /> <br /> Also, Satchel, towards the end there you started to wax poetic pretty hard. It makes it hard to understand what it is your trying to communicate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110062#post1110062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a ghost might not be the same person that it spawned from, it might still be considered a human. It is spawned from a human in the likness of a human. It inherits traits from the human that spawned it, and can be considered alive in the sense that it's both animate and conscious. It's basically reproduction. Ghosts could be considered a different phenotype of human.</div> </div> </div> </div>This... actually kind of makes sense. I'm not sure I'd agree with it, though. But at this point it seems I'm in my own camp regarding the belief in the nature of ghosts as a continuity of a person rather than a separate and new person with all the memories of them. I don't dismiss offhand the possibility that it isn't, but have yet to really see the same evidence or implications towards the idea. Which is kind of discerning, but more so because I'm hearing that it's the case in 2e from multiple angles, but the only time I actually recall an implication of that was in mage 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110151#post1110151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note, however, that a person who loses their soul does still retain their personality and memories, at least for a while. It'll eventually all degrade until they become a Thrall if they don't get <i>a</i> soul before long. But it doesn't really matter if it's <i>the same</i> soul as the one they lost. Also, when a human dies, all the various soul parts go *somewhere else*, and even if a ghost is created, it's not made out of the soul or any of its parts. At least, from the way it's described in Mage. I haven't read Mummy, so if something in it contradicts the above... well, then that's CofD for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might actually not be true. To quote mage:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mage pg 245</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some believe that a ghost is part of the original soul, separated by traumatic death, and others hold that it contains the person\u2019s actual personality: everything that can be defined as \u201cthem.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>So... it -might- be made out of a souls parts. Or it might just be them. Mages don't know for sure, and it is probably a good Mystery for a Death Mage. I don't know what Mummy says either as I've yet to push through reading that book (so hard to get the motivation to read something when you lack people who want to play the game) - when it comes to souls, I mainly know (or rather, have been informed) that Mummy seems to define the soul in more ways than mages do, and what Mages view as 'the soul' (IE, the thing that you can rip out with Death), Mummy's only view as 'one part of the whole soul'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T14:31:02-07:00","id":1110364,"title":"","content":"Arguably humanity's greatest power, as well as one of our most prevalent struggles, is that of &quot;creating place&quot;. Monsters can do that, but certainly not on the scale humanity can. There's just not enough of them to do that, and many have incentives that keep them further away from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T14:35:53-07:00","id":1110366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110236#post1110236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit to being a stickler about this kind of thing, it's another aspect of the thread that has annoyed me. Nowhere in the books does it claim humanity as some superpowered force everyone must cower away from. Nowhere in the books does it say they know everything there is to know about the supernatural, even collectively. I'd be surprised if it says in any game book that someone should be wary of fighting a human because they're going to get killed for daring to fight something so viciously powerful. Humanity isn't declared to be or depicted as overrated in the books at all. Even their lack of innate drawbacks is balanced out by being oblivious prey for everyone else.<br /> <br /> As others have pointed said it's basically just a poorly thought out 'humans suck' thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know I wanted to reply to this with something intellectual and thought provoking. All I can think of is &quot;exactly.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think it's really vampire that focuses a lot on the whole 'humans must be feared' thing. Werewolf suggests they should be feared, but not for their ability to kill wolves so much as the damage they can have on the hisil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T16:09:55-07:00","id":1110398,"title":"","content":"I mostly lost interest in this thread back on page 5 when it became apparent that it's primarily about \u201cwhite room\u201d comparisons: stuck a human in a white room with a vampire, and who wins? Etc. Not interested in playing that game, because its outcome is meaningless. <br /> <br /> In particular, humanity isn't overrated in this regard, because nobody would argue that humans would win if you stripped them of their benefits and pitted them one-on-one against the monsters. Their argument is that stripping humans of all advantages isn't a reasonable restriction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T16:34:31-07:00","id":1110403,"title":"","content":"Honestly I think part of the problem is the initial starting point. I mean in the thread this sprouted from the argument had been from one person who said humans were the top of the food chain, but then gave odd explanations for their case.* Then later went off on the argument that a smart human can defeat absolutely any supernatural in the setting which I think is where the white room &quot;who wins the extinction war&quot; came in.<br /> <br /> Then this thread started with the premise of humanity being overrated, but didn't give any sort of grounds for it aside from who is more likely to kill who with apparently all things possible to one faction. Which is not helpful since while I think most splats view the whole masquerade thing as preferred, I think most of them are in a &quot;It will cause way more problems than it would be worth&quot; as opposed to humanity being the great destroyer that the splats must avoid disturbing at all cost.<br /> <br /> *I believe the cases were Vampires, Beasts, and Changelings have to feed off humans and are thus inferior. Werewolves have control issues. Demons are in hiding from the God Machine. Mummies are slaves to their gods. Geist started as humans. Prometheans seek to become human. Mages are technically better, but have to deal with paradox and so aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T16:39:33-07:00","id":1110404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110398#post1110398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly lost interest in this thread back on page 5 when it became apparent that it's primarily about \u201cwhite room\u201d comparisons: stuck a human in a white room with a vampire, and who wins? Etc. Not interested in playing that game, because its outcome is meaningless.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to monsters, I think humanity is best compared to the habitat than another species: the environment, the food supply, the sum of selective pressures. Monsters who adapt to humanity survive, those who don't die - but being intelligent beings, monsters can to an extent adapt humanity to them - but they have to judge that extent carefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T21:34:03-07:00","id":1110462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110361#post1110361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No - your liver donation is not you. However, your liver also does not have all your memories, your personality, everything that makes you you. It also does not leave your body and develop consciousness to be it's own entity. Your liver donation is better compared to the soul than to what a ghost is. Now - if you took your mind and had a transplant, and then questioned whether or not that mind was you or not, or if the transplant resulted in a wholly different person - that might be a better comparison here.<br /> <br /> When you die, your soul leaves your body (to go elsewhere or to dissipate) as does typically your consciousness - that last part that defines the 'you'. A ghost is clearly written in as both not being a soul, and lacking a soul - and while your soul is important, it is also not you. Now my default is to use the process of elimination here. A ghost is not your soul, so that's easy enough to eliminate. However - what evidence is there that eliminates a ghost from being the consciousness of the person who died? Now you can claim that the old consciousness either vanished or ceased to exist, and that the ghost is an entirely new consciousness that simply is a perfect mirror of an old consciousness - but there is no real method to prove that this is a distinctly different individual, and that seems an unnecessary overcomplication when it lacks sufficient evidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Everything that makes me me&quot; is not an accurate descriptor of the packet of memory and personality that once belonged to me in the Chronicles of Darkness. My ghost does not have my body, my destiny, or the vast majority of my concerns \u2014 it is a broadly monomaniacal entity wearing my face and tapping into some of my memory and the most uncontentious thing that can be said about its drives is that it believes it pursues them in my name.<br /> <br /> You're relying on a definition of identity that privileges consciousness above all else in a setting where supernatural powers can copy, borrow, or consume abstractions like memories and relationships; you are in a discussion where nobody is arguing that ghosts are a &quot;distinctly different person&quot; \u2014 that they aren't functionally the man who went in for a scan a hundred years ago. The argument is not &quot;ghosts are unrelated to their bases.&quot; The argument is &quot;being a self-aware reflection of a now-dead person does not make a ghost that person itself, because that person is dead.&quot;<br /> <br /> You're also assuming ghosts perfectly mirror their bases, which\u2026 look, I don't know about you, but no matter how obsessive I may get about a thing, I <i>usually</i> don't have that obsession define my entire existence, nor do I generally consider my life-distractions a more rewarding pursuit than self-betterment. A significant number of still-humanlike ghosts <i>do not realize they are dead</i>. Two significant domains in Book of the Dead make it plain that the gods of death can dredge up a blank slate that starts to act like the ghost of someone you desperately want to raise from the dead, that identifiers are fungible, and that it is the nature of human identity to gradually wash away in the tides of time and death.<br /> <br /> A ghost starts out as an imperfect likeness clinging to fidelity through routine and only stands to get weirder as the years wear on. It staves that off by holding onto the world humanity inhabits through the place of a human that inhabited it, but ironclad commitment to the theater does not impart ownership of the role to the actor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm going to need a citation on this one. Far as I was aware, they have influences, numen, and also their own default template which allows for the expenditures of essence - which in of itself is a supernatural ability. </div> </div> </div>It's pretty direct about it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astral Realms, p58, &quot;The Inhabitants of the Temenos&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cResident\u201d is one of the commonly accepted terms for the vast majority of self-willed beings living in the Temenos. The self-willed inhabitants of the Temenos possess the same three traits as ghosts or spirits \u2014 Power, Finesse and Resistance. They are also ranked like spirits (Mage: The Awakening, p. 317). <b>Residents of the Temenos are all Rank 1 beings who lack all Numina and other powers and who most resemble Sleepers in the Fallen World.</b> Using magic on residents of the Temenos is effectively identical to using magic on Sleepers in the Fallen world, except without the risk of Disbelief or Paradox. Unlike scenery people, <b>residents have lives, memories, and desires as powerful and as complex as any mage or Sleeper, and residents consider themselves to be real people.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, Technically, no, you somehow did not repeatedly point out the underworld. You brought it up in this discussion once, seemingly offhand, in regards to it being a required location in order for a ghost to gain any form of real power. That said, I'm having trouble connecting how the underworld or geists relate to the topics of a ghosts nature. </div> </div> </div>You have trouble understanding how the place that draws ghosts into increasingly inhuman forms and mindsets through the incorporation of its substance into their nature relates to your argument that the inclusion of ghosts in a metaphysical category Beast uses to contrast with more conceptually obvious types of monsters like fetches and Prometheans and vampires, who all have direct intervention by a supernatural entity/force in their makeup?<br /> <br /> You have trouble understanding how a thing that <i>can get more inherently inhuman</i> falls into the <i>less inherently inhuman</i> slice of all monsterdom that Beastly power cares about and how this distinction has no bearing on the truth of what a ghost is?<br /> <br /> You have trouble understanding how the rules of &quot;fundamentally human&quot; monsters exist to make monsters that mostly look and behave like humans harder to connect with for Beasts rather than to make a statement about ghostly metaphysics?<br /> <br /> I want to be clear on this: You are leaning on the wording of a category listed in a game where ghosts and their origins are not a central facet of gameplay to claim something that that definition has no interaction with re: ghosts. That is the reason I am bringing up how the Underworld shifts ghosts into the other category and how this transition's relation to the &quot;fundamentally human&quot; descriptor is more relevant to Beast's meditation on monstrosity and the supernatural and the human mindset than it is to the question of whether a packet of ephemera borrowing an old name constitutes a totally legitimate claim on that name's place in the world. &quot;Beast says ghosts count as fundamentally human for the purposes of Begotten magic&quot; has zero things to do with what a ghost really actually is besides &quot;superficially and psychologically human apart from the telekinesis.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T22:10:15-07:00","id":1110470,"title":"","content":"I haven't read through this thread, but I thought I would offer my two cents on the matter of Humanity.<br /> <br /> As far as I'm concerned, Mages, one of the most powerful supernatural types, are entirely Human. They are what Humans are 'supposed' to be like, without the Lie.<br /> Really, acknowledging that Mages are Human is the only way I can reconcile the whole 'Humanity is special' thing with Mage itself. If 'Humanity' refers to Sleepers alone, then there's no way I can really spin it positively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T22:38:33-07:00","id":1110477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110470#post1110470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read through this thread, but I thought I would offer my two cents on the matter of Humanity.<br /> <br /> As far as I'm concerned, Mages, one of the most powerful supernatural types, are entirely Human. They are what Humans are 'supposed' to be like, without the Lie.<br /> Really, acknowledging that Mages are Human is the only way I can reconcile the whole 'Humanity is special' thing with Mage itself. If 'Humanity' refers to Sleepers alone, then there's no way I can really spin it positively.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's, uh... it's been a ride. We first established that the criteria Nyrufa is judging humans by is their ability to fight monsters one-on-one without the benefit of tools. Then we argued for a bit about the usefulness (or lack thereof) of assessing them based on that criteria. Once we reached the point of saying &quot;you're right, monsters are totally better than humans at making naked people in featureless white rooms stop being alive, though it seems a silly thing to make a thread about, since this fact has never been in contention&quot; the discussion kind of broke down into whether or not ghosts are human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T03:36:45-07:00","id":1110505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110462#post1110462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Everything that makes me me&quot; is not an accurate descriptor of the packet of memory and personality that once belonged to me in the Chronicles of Darkness. My ghost does not have my body, my destiny, or the vast majority of my concerns \u2014 it is a broadly monomaniacal entity wearing my face and tapping into some of my memory and the most uncontentious thing that can be said about its drives is that it believes it pursues them in my name.</div> </div> </div> </div>No? Because that was one of the options suggested on mage's perceptions of what a ghost might be - everything that makes them 'them'. Your right - the ghost does not have your body. The statement that it does not have your destiny, however, is a speculation made under the assumption that it is not you. And as far as concerns, death does tend to alter them, change them, or remove them - ghost or no ghost.<br /> <br /> It's very easy to make blanket statements that something is not a continuation of something else. I clearly remember a case where people brought up how vampires might not actually be the person who died before, and instead just something else that took over the body and memories of the vampire and believed that it was the person who they were in life. And it might be true - but there ultimately isn't evidence that would suggest that Tom-the-vampire was not Tom-the-human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110462#post1110462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're relying on a definition of identity that privileges consciousness above all else in a setting where supernatural powers can copy, borrow, or consume abstractions like memories and relationships; you are in a discussion where nobody is arguing that ghosts are a &quot;distinctly different person&quot; \u2014 that they aren't functionally the man who went in for a scan a hundred years ago. The argument is not &quot;ghosts are unrelated to their bases.&quot; The argument is &quot;being a self-aware reflection of a now-dead person does not make a ghost that person itself, because that person is dead.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That really shouldn't be surprising. One of the definitions of identity -is- the character and personality of an individual. And while yes, this is a setting in which supernatural powers can copy, borrow, or consume abstractions, by default a ghost is not created by an application of superpowers.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;that person is dead&quot; is not a quality a that differentiates a ghost from their former self.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110462#post1110462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're also assuming ghosts perfectly mirror their bases, which\u2026 look, I don't know about you, but no matter how obsessive I may get about a thing, I usually don't have that obsession define my entire existence, nor do I generally consider my life-distractions a more rewarding pursuit than self-betterment. A significant number of still-humanlike ghosts do not realize they are dead. Two significant domains in Book of the Dead make it plain that the gods of death can dredge up a blank slate that starts to act like the ghost of someone you desperately want to raise from the dead, that identifiers are fungible, and that it is the nature of human identity to gradually wash away in the tides of time and death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have already pointed this out but - utilizing a power to create a ghost is not quite the same as a ghost naturally forming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110462#post1110462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A ghost starts out as an imperfect likeness clinging to fidelity through routine and only stands to get weirder as the years wear on. It staves that off by holding onto the world humanity inhabits through the place of a human that inhabited it, but ironclad commitment to the theater does not impart ownership of the role to the actor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Change, and factors which create more change, does not inherently imply a different entity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110462#post1110462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty direct about it:<br /> <br /> \u201cResident\u201d is one of the commonly accepted terms for the vast majority of self-willed beings living in the Temenos. The self-willed inhabitants of the Temenos possess the same three traits as ghosts or spirits \u2014 Power, Finesse and Resistance. They are also ranked like spirits (Mage: The Awakening, p. 317). Residents of the Temenos are all Rank 1 beings who lack all Numina and other powers and who most resemble Sleepers in the Fallen World. Using magic on residents of the Temenos is effectively identical to using magic on Sleepers in the Fallen world, except without the risk of Disbelief or Paradox. Unlike scenery people, residents have lives, memories, and desires as powerful and as complex as any mage or Sleeper, and residents consider themselves to be real people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that helps me understand a bit of your case here. I was under the understanding we are discussing 2e ghosts. If we're keeping 1e in this discussion, then we have to have the mage's beliefs that the ghosts are not the person (which as I recall, was heavily implied that that belief was the result of hubris and tradition - yet also not disproven) , and Sin-Eater beliefs that the ghosts -are- the same person. I'll admit, it's a far more vast wealth of information to pull from though. It might even yield different results to the discussion. That said, 2e points out that all ephemeral entities begin with at least 1 dot of influence per dot of rank.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110462#post1110462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have trouble understanding how the place that draws ghosts into increasingly inhuman forms and mindsets through the incorporation of its substance into their nature relates to your argument that the inclusion of ghosts in a metaphysical category Beast uses to contrast with more conceptually obvious types of monsters like fetches and Prometheans and vampires, who all have direct intervention by a supernatural entity/force in their makeup?<br /> <br /> You have trouble understanding how a thing that <i>can get more inherently inhuman</i> falls into the <i>less inherently inhuman</i> slice of all monsterdom that Beastly power cares about and how this distinction has no bearing on the truth of what a ghost is?<br /> <br /> You have trouble understanding how the rules of &quot;fundamentally human&quot; monsters exist to make monsters that mostly look and behave like humans harder to connect with for Beasts rather than to make a statement about ghostly metaphysics?</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably wouldn't have trouble understanding that - if going to the underworld and raising in rank actually changed the fact that they were ghosts, or that those ghosts were 'fundamentally human'. If the ability to become more inhuman by interacting with another creature was a trait unique to creatures that fall into the 'fundamentally human' category. If some of those 'clearly more inhuman' monsters didn't look and behave like humans by virtue of that literally being the point of their existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110462#post1110462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to be clear on this: You are leaning on the wording of a category listed in a game where ghosts and their origins are not a central facet of gameplay to claim something that that definition has no interaction with re: ghosts. That is the reason I am bringing up how the Underworld shifts ghosts into the other category and how this transition's relation to the &quot;fundamentally human&quot; descriptor is more relevant to Beast's meditation on monstrosity and the supernatural and the human mindset than it is to the question of whether a packet of ephemera borrowing an old name constitutes a totally legitimate claim on that name's place in the world. &quot;Beast says ghosts count as fundamentally human for the purposes of Begotten magic&quot; has zero things to do with what a ghost really actually is besides &quot;superficially and psychologically human apart from the telekinesis.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I am pointing out that the categorization of it lists two distinct groups - one which is clearly spelled out, the other which is basically 'everything else but things made by the god machine'. The logic here is simple - if an entity had never been human, it would fall in the category of 'never been human'. One should not need to redefine what 'fundamentally human' means, in order to try to disprove that logic. Fun fact - one of the antonyms of superficial is fundamental. Can't exactly be both superficially and fundamentally human at the same time.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, what I am trying to say is that there is evidence - in both Mage 2e and Beast - that would suggest that in 2e, the ghost is the same person as the person who died, rather than a separate entity spawned from them. It would seem to me that this discussion could be more easily resolved, or at least be less stagnant if one were to supply where there is evidence to the contrary? Your statements have basically repeated that the ghost is a good fake of the person who died - but not necessarily what evidence actually suggests that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 07-02-2017, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T07:14:42-07:00","id":1110535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110505#post1110505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The statement that it does not have your destiny, however, is a speculation made under the assumption that it is not you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually if you're using the optional Fate rules, a ghost does have a different Fate than the human that spawned it. Humans' Fates usually revolve around their death, and ghosts' Fates are always being forgotten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T11:42:14-07:00","id":1110607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110535#post1110535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually if you're using the optional Fate rules, a ghost does have a different Fate than the human that spawned it. Humans' Fates usually revolve around their death, and ghosts' Fates are always being forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Didn't know that. Interesting! I'm not familiar with those, I'll admit. I'll need to take a look at them to form an opinion - where can I find them?<br /> <br /> Also, is there any reference to what happens when one utilizes time on a naturally occurring ghost? Such as when you use postcognition on one for events of before their death, or even rewrite history? I feel like whether or not that worked could actually make or break this particular discussion.<br /> <br /> At the moment, my current theory is that the most likely Truth of a ghost can be found by utilizing the whole 5-parts-of-a-soul-deal you get when dealing with mummy's or... well, really anything Egyption. Kind of leaning towards the ghost being the Ba aspect, separated due to traumatic circumstances - usually, such a strong desire not to die that the shock of the event separates the whole and things more important than life (which is being robbed of them) keep them here.<br /> <br /> Edit: Unfortunately, I haven't read Mummy yet - so this is just a hypothesis from tidbits gathered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 07-02-2017, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T12:12:56-07:00","id":1110619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110607#post1110607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Didn't know that. Interesting! I'm not familiar with those, I'll admit. I'll need to take a look at them to form an opinion - where can I find them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Core book, page 177. A lot of people miss it because it's in the God-Machine Chronicle section of Chronicles of Darkness but wasn't in God-Machine Chronicle. Interesting story there, Fate rules were part of an earlier draft of the CofD 2e rules, back when CofD was called nWoD and 2e was called the World of Darkness Rules Revision. They never made it into the final draft, but a lot of references to them ended up slipping past development and errata. Questions about the Fate rules kept popping up, so when the 2e core rulebook came out (by then called Chronicles of Darkness) and they had some extra space on a page in the GMC section, they decided to put Fate back in as an optional rule.<br /> <br /> ...Man, everything to do with CofD development is weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T12:29:11-07:00","id":1110623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110619#post1110619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Core book, page 177. A lot of people miss it because it's in the God-Machine Chronicle section of Chronicles of Darkness but wasn't in God-Machine Chronicle. Interesting story there, Fate rules were part of an earlier draft of the CofD 2e rules, back when CofD was called nWoD and 2e was called the World of Darkness Rules Revision. They never made it into the final draft, but a lot of references to them ended up slipping past development and errata. Questions about the Fate rules kept popping up, so when the 2e core rulebook came out (by then called Chronicles of Darkness) and they had some extra space on a page in the GMC section, they decided to put Fate back in as an optional rule.<br /> <br /> ...Man, everything to do with CofD development is weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>It gets weirder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T15:09:50-07:00","id":1110670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110623#post1110623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It gets weirder.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not gonna change the name again, are they? XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T16:28:11-07:00","id":1110686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110470#post1110470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I'm concerned, Mages, one of the most powerful supernatural types, are entirely Human. They are what Humans are 'supposed' to be like, without the Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div> As an aside - I'm fairly sure the devloper of Mage game line has said that Sleepwalkers are what humans are supposed to be like, and mages very much transform into inhuman beings. Especially if they pursue Ascension. Most games have you start off as &quot;losing&quot; that human spark. Mage is a game that sends you down the rabbit hole of willingly losing that spark.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T16:39:11-07:00","id":1110689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110670#post1110670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not gonna change the name again, are they? XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Vampire's gonna be called &quot;Sexy bitey people,&quot; Werewolf will be &quot;Dog Spirit Guys,&quot; and Mage will be &quot;Uncle Dave's Philosophical Knife Fights.&quot;<br /> <br /> White Wolf wanted to avoid any brand confusion with the <i>True</i> World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110686#post1110686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As an aside - I'm fairly sure the devloper of Mage game line has said that Sleepwalkers are what humans are supposed to be like, and mages very much transform into inhuman beings. Especially if they pursue Ascension. Most games have you start off as &quot;losing&quot; that human spark. Mage is a game that sends you down the rabbit hole of willingly losing that spark.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To me, it seems more like Mage is what happens when that spark kicks up into a roaring fire, and threatens to burn you out from the inside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T17:12:17-07:00","id":1110695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110670#post1110670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not gonna change the name again, are they? XD</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they are not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T17:31:46-07:00","id":1110699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110689#post1110689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, it seems more like Mage is what happens when that spark kicks up into a roaring fire, and threatens to burn you out from the inside.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nah. Its pretty firmly established that mages are turning you into a monster and you're pretty monstrous. At least officially. You want to do that at your table, more power to you. But that's not the intent of the game, as far as I can tell from what the writers and dev have said. Mages are meant to be a deviation -away- from humanity, not an embodiment of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T20:53:48-07:00","id":1110747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110670#post1110670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not gonna change the name again, are they? XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably to something like &quot;Fates of Darkness&quot; (makes for a better acronym).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110689#post1110689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Vampire's gonna be called &quot;Sexy bitey people,&quot; Werewolf will be &quot;Dog Spirit Guys,&quot; and Mage will be &quot;Uncle Dave's Philosophical Knife Fights.&quot;<br /> <br /> White Wolf wanted to avoid any brand confusion with the <i>True</i> World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Developed by Zak Smith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T22:46:38-07:00","id":1110763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110686#post1110686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As an aside - I'm fairly sure the devloper of Mage game line has said that Sleepwalkers are what humans are supposed to be like, and mages very much transform into inhuman beings. Especially if they pursue Ascension. Most games have you start off as &quot;losing&quot; that human spark. Mage is a game that sends you down the rabbit hole of willingly losing that spark.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I could see that. I mean, there's nothing really good about being a Sleeper, but Sleepwalkers are at least capable of living a genuine life without suffering the Lie.<br /> Still, I fail to see any way in which a Mage is made lesser by their Awakening, they just seem to be better in every way than normal people. Not really judging that by the power available to them, but general capacity to experience and understand the world.<br /> To me it seems that they're either Human, or better than Human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110699#post1110699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nah. Its pretty firmly established that mages are turning you into a monster and you're pretty monstrous. At least officially. You want to do that at your table, more power to you. But that's not the intent of the game, as far as I can tell from what the writers and dev have said. Mages are meant to be a deviation -away- from humanity, not an embodiment of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'd say that Humanity and monstrosity aren't mutually contradictory. While I don't think Mages are inherently monstrous, they become so as any other Human might; through their actions.<br /> I guess my opinion is that even if Mage's aren't literally an embodiment of Humanity, they are thematically so, because their monstrosity arises directly from their most Human aspects.<br /> <br /> When it comes down to it, if we're not including Mages and other mostly Human supernaturals, I find it hard to disagree with the statement that Humanity is Overrated in the Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T23:45:21-07:00","id":1110770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110763#post1110763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes down to it, if we're not including Mages and other mostly Human supernaturals, I find it hard to disagree with the statement that Humanity is Overrated in the Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>As individuals? No, not really. In most cases, the alteration from human to monster tends to be a personal change - and often times, a personal improvement - though often at the expense of others. As a race though? As a species? Barring mages as you said (because for all intents and purposes, mages are humans with godlike power at their fingertips), none of the other groups hold the same capacity for change and adaption. Humanity as a species is malleable and everchanging, which makes them threatening. Dealing with the race of mortals in the year 2017 is not the same battle dealing with them in the year 2027, and their progression is insane through the lens of many supernaturals. Hell, humanity's progression is insane to humanity. So long as the direction of humanities progression isn't in 'being an intentional pain in the ass to supernaturals' though, humanity is manageable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 07-03-2017, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T00:02:36-07:00","id":1110773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110763#post1110763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, I fail to see any way in which a Mage is made lesser by their Awakening, they just seem to be better in every way than normal people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you section off a part of your identity from contact with your mortal life, your magic will gradually attract a diverse and fascinating and awful bunch of thematic maladies to everyone and everything you love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T17:23:34-07:00","id":1111071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110361#post1110361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now you can claim that the old consciousness either vanished or ceased to exist, and that the ghost is an entirely new consciousness that simply is a perfect mirror of an old consciousness - but there is no real method to prove that this is a distinctly different individual, and that seems an unnecessary overcomplication when it lacks sufficient evidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts have a Virtue and Vice that are flipped from the person they were created from so it's unlikely that they're a perfect mirror of their former consciousness. Also, depending on Rank they don't even come close to being a good mirror, Rank 2 being the only one at which they really resemble a former human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T17:41:02-07:00","id":1111076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110763#post1110763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI'd say that Humanity and monstrosity aren't mutually contradictory. While I don't think Mages are inherently monstrous, they become so as any other Human might; through their actions.<br /> I guess my opinion is that even if Mage's aren't literally an embodiment of Humanity, they are thematically so, because their monstrosity arises directly from their most Human aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages suffer from impulses and temptations that no human will ever experience, and even just knowing that those impulses and temptations are there removes them from humanity. The change is gradual, but as a Mage increases in power their monstrousness becomes increasingly evident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T18:45:36-07:00","id":1111096,"title":"","content":"Something I've observed; people who don't think that mages are inherently monstrous and alienated from humanity tend to downplay the narrative aspects of the mage template (Nimbus, Obsessions, Peripheral Mage Sight, etc), over the mechanical aspects of the mage template (Arcana, Attainments, etc)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T19:30:47-07:00","id":1111114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111096#post1111096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've observed; people who don't think that mages are inherently monstrous and alienated from humanity tend to downplay the narrative aspects of the mage template (Nimbus, Obsessions, Peripheral Mage Sight, etc), over the mechanical aspects of the mage template (Arcana, Attainments, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mage presents the idea of &quot;absolute power corrupts absolutely.&quot;<br /> <br /> What happens if you give a random person borderline omnipotence? It's very easy to see how they might become jaded / monstrous in a situation like that.<br /> <br /> Maybe not all at once, but the temptation to take the quick and (relatively) easy approach to solving their problems would become progressively stronger as they honed their skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T19:43:17-07:00","id":1111117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111114#post1111114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Mage presents the idea of &amp;quot;absolute power corrupts absolutely.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> What happens if you give a random person borderline omnipotence? It's very easy to see how they might become jaded / monstrous in a situation like that.<br /> <br /> Maybe not all at once, but the temptation to take the quick and (relatively) easy approach to solving their problems would become progressively stronger as they honed their skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Mages make monsters out of themselves. Which I don't see as mutually exclusive with the idea that they are monstrous by nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T20:14:36-07:00","id":1111126,"title":"","content":"You can even remove the undertones of corruption from absolute power, what happens to a Mage is change on a level that simply removes them from the human experience. It all starts at the moment of Awakening. They're monsters, make no mistake, even if they can fool themselves into thinking that they're not. Heck, one could argue that one of their weaknesses is that they're able to continue to delude themselves that they're people. Even at their lowest Gnosis they experience inhuman drives, and the cosmos confront them with the reality of their own inhumanity. The &quot;ultimate&quot; destination of a Mage is to be a Symbol of the Supernal where they reign over humanity, as a creation of man gone beyond their control. The gods and their scions walk the earth and become legend. That's Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T21:18:27-07:00","id":1111140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111117#post1111117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. Mages make monsters out of themselves. Which I don't see as mutually exclusive with the idea that they are monstrous by nature.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Example of how a small act of hubris can have monstrous consequences is if a Mage is pulled over for a traffic violation. It's a minor one and nobody got hurt, so they decide to use Mind in order to coerce the police officer to let them go and forget about it. Except that the squad car's camera system records the whole thing and eventually the mind controlled cop is being investigated on suspicion of bribery / corruption.<br /> <br /> All because the Mage wanted to get out of a speeding ticket.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T21:34:27-07:00","id":1111149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111071#post1111071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghosts have a Virtue and Vice that are flipped from the person they were created from so it's unlikely that they're a perfect mirror of their former consciousness. Also, depending on Rank they don't even come close to being a good mirror, Rank 2 being the only one at which they really resemble a former human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair - they lack a soul, and therefore should have the soulless condition. One of the aspects of that is a flipped virtue and vice - though, I will confess that the word 'perfect' was the wrong descriptor to use for a blanket description of ghosts - or really anything in truth, when applied to consciousness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T22:14:56-07:00","id":1111164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111140#post1111140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Example of how a small act of hubris can have monstrous consequences is if a Mage is pulled over for a traffic violation. It's a minor one and nobody got hurt, so they decide to use Mind in order to coerce the police officer to let them go and forget about it. Except that the squad car's camera system records the whole thing and eventually the mind controlled cop is being investigated on suspicion of bribery / corruption.<br /> <br /> All because the Mage wanted to get out of a speeding ticket.</div> </div> </div> </div>I once used an analogy almost exactly like this to tell how magic and Wisdom in Mage work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111149#post1111149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, to be fair - they lack a soul, and therefore should have the soulless condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought ghosts don't count as Soulless, though? They're more like remnants or imprints of souls, so a lack of soul is a lack of something they never had in the first place. <br /> <br /> Maybe if the &quot;ghosts are splinters of souls&quot; theory is true, then the part of the soul that makes Virtue 'favored' is certainly not the part that makes up ghosts. <br /> <br /> Another thing to muse: somebody observed that demons are to angels what ghosts are to humans, in the sense that both are remnants of an entity. (I think it was LostLight in their blog?) And guess what being other than ghosts have Vice as their &quot;full Willpower&quot; Anchor trait?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Just remembered that in 1E, the True Fae also had flipped Vices. So we have ghosts, fairies, and demons with flipped Vice &amp; Virtue. The three types of supernatural beings that are often conflated and mixed in real-life folklore. Interesting indeed, no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 07-04-2017, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T04:01:12-07:00","id":1111203,"title":"","content":"Actually, the Demon and Angel comparison isn't quite accurate. The Demon isn't an entirely separate entity, it's an Angel who's achieved conscious will. It didn't splinter off from the Angel, but rather the Angel became the Demon.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't seem to be the case with Ghosts. They weren't created from humans, they were created by humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T04:22:09-07:00","id":1111204,"title":"","content":"&quot;Mage depicts the Awakened, human beings who have unlocked the potential buried deep within everyone to see the many layers of occult symbolism and magical conspiracy influencing everything in the world.&quot; - Mage the Awakening 2e, pg. 11<br /> <br /> &quot;Although mages come to their Gnosis in individual acts of rebellion against the Lie, they're human, and humans are social animals.&quot; - Mage the Awakening, pg. 19<br /> <br /> &quot;In Mage: The Awakening, mages are essentially human, with one major difference; they can choose to wield magic.&quot; - Mage: the Awakening, pg. 79<br /> <br /> I thought I'd point out that the perspective of Mages-as-Humans does have some support in the text, though it might simply be describing things as Mages themselves see it. I think it's debatable and largely a philosophical question; I don't think there's necessarily a right answer.<br /> I do kind of disagree with the third quote though, given that Mages have quite a few other differences to Sleepers and Sleepwalkers than just that.<br /> <br /> With that, I think I'll duck out of the discussion, lest I get too involved and stir up an argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T05:20:22-07:00","id":1111211,"title":"","content":"On the mage matter - mages are still human (pre-archmastery), but that doesn't mean that they're the embodiment of humanity either. Every other gameline (save Hunter), you start off as a &quot;non-human&quot; monster, or were never human. Mages start off as human but travel towards becoming a full non-human (archmastery, lichdom, etc). At least, that's the intent. As I said before, I disagree that most splats shouldn't be considered human, but that view is not supported by the game.<br /> <br /> On the ghost matter - There's a reason why Moros have a theme of alchemy and transformation, and Geist: the Sin Eaters is full of key / door / transition symbology. There's no &quot;created from/by/etc&quot; humans. That doens't make sense, given the themes of the games where ghosts feature. Its always a transition in these cases. I think that ignoring that is rather problematic in this discussion. <br /> <br /> On the matter of actually being the embodiment of humanity - Do psychics count? Is becoming a psychic the ultimate expression of humanity, or is that just another deviation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T05:32:34-07:00","id":1111214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111211#post1111211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the mage matter - mages are still human (pre-archmastery), but that doesn't mean that they're the embodiment of humanity either. Every other gameline (save Hunter), you start off as a &quot;non-human&quot; monster, or were never human. Mages start off as human but travel towards becoming a full non-human (archmastery, lichdom, etc). At least, that's the intent. As I said before, I disagree that most splats shouldn't be considered human, but that view is not supported by the game.<br /> <br /> On the ghost matter - There's a reason why Moros have a theme of alchemy and transformation, and Geist: the Sin Eaters is full of key / door / transition symbology. There's no &quot;created from/by/etc&quot; humans. That doens't make sense, given the themes of the games where ghosts feature. Its always a transition in these cases. I think that ignoring that is rather problematic in this discussion.<br /> <br /> On the matter of actually being the embodiment of humanity - Do psychics count? Is becoming a psychic the ultimate expression of humanity, or is that just another deviation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But if a ghost can be created without the human dying in the process, then can you really say it's a transitional period? The human is still alive, but now they've got some kind of ghostly doppleganger floating around.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd say psychics embody human willpower. Through concentrated effort and focus, they can impose their will upon the world around them in ways that seem impossible.<br /> <br /> Don't forget, humans spent tens of thousands of years believing we'd never be able to fly. And now it's one of our biggest means of transportation. All because a pair of brothers decided to give the middle finger to mother nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-04-2017, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T06:52:46-07:00","id":1111239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111203#post1111203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the Demon and Angel comparison isn't quite accurate. The Demon isn't an entirely separate entity, it's an Angel who's achieved conscious will. It didn't splinter off from the Angel, but rather the Angel became the Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually... let's look in-universe for a moment. What is the reason some see ghosts and the dead person as the same? Because they share memories and an identity. What is the reason some see ghosts and the dead person as different? Because they do not share anything except memories and identity; their personality changes (flipped Vice &amp; Virtue), their priorities in life change (Aspirations), they no longer have a material body (Corpus), they can do stuff that humans simply can't do (Numina, Manifestations, Influences), and they rely on external factors to stay in the mortal world (the need for Anchors).<br /> <br /> What connects a demon to its pre-Fall state? Memories born of service, and an identity born out of it. What separates a demon from its angelic existence? Their changed personality (Vice &amp; Virtue are no longer alien to humans, and are now the inverse of that of humans), their changed life priorities (the Mission traded for an Agenda), their body's composition (Cover bodies are human, and Primum cores are quantum engines), abilities that they simply couldn't do as angels (Exploits, Pact-making, etc), and a reliance on external factors for their continued walking-among-men (the need for Covers).<br /> <br /> Yes, we had no developer clarify the issue, but the resemblances are there, enough to make comparisons on an out-of-game narrative level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T07:00:48-07:00","id":1111244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111214#post1111214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> But if a ghost can be created without the human dying in the process, then can you really say it's a transitional period? The human is still alive, but now they've got some kind of ghostly doppleganger floating around.</div> </div> </div> </div>With regards to naturally occurring ghosts, the element of transition is there but with a twist. The ghost is not the one that needs to make the transition; they're symptoms of a failed transition. That a Master of Death can create them only shows that Awakened magic is indeed a powerful reality-warping force, not that the laws of reality warped externally by Supernal magic is internally faulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T07:49:18-07:00","id":1111262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111203#post1111203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the Demon and Angel comparison isn't quite accurate. The Demon isn't an entirely separate entity, it's an Angel who's achieved conscious will. It didn't splinter off from the Angel, but rather the Angel became the Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Angels are often pretty Big, metaphysically speaking, being major portions of a world-spanning engine. The Fall crams everything of that being that will fit into a human Cover.<br /> <br /> Much of it <i>doesn't</i> fit, which is part of why demons have to relearn Embeds even within their Incarnations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111239#post1111239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their changed personality (Vice &amp; Virtue are no longer alien to humans, and are now the inverse of that of humans)</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons specifically have the same type of Virtues and Vices as angels. They might change in the Fall, but a demon's Anchor Traits still operate the same way as they do for other entities with Traits of the same name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T07:59:01-07:00","id":1111266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111262#post1111262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons specifically have the same type of Virtues and Vices as angels. They might change in the Fall, but a demon's Anchor Traits still operate the same way as they do for other entities with Traits of the same name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strange, I thought angels had weird Vice &amp; Virtue, like Meticulous for Vice and Punctal for Virtue, and recovered full Willpower from Virtue. While demons had the traditional Vice &amp; Virtue, like Prideful for Vice and Charitable for Virtue, but recovered full Willpower from Vice. I should reread the Demon book, it seems.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, my point with the Anchor traits was that they do change significantly upon the Fall. The Fall is the death of an angel, and the birth of a demon. So it makes sense to me that demons exhibit similarities to ghosts, with angels as the equivalent of living people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T08:58:47-07:00","id":1111285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if a ghost can be created without the human dying in the process, then can you really say it's a transitional period? </div> </div> </div> Yes. As far as I know, the only way to do that is through Death Mastery. And that's no different, imho, than making a perfect clone of anyone else, living or dead or otherwise. An artificial creation with a Duration that expires and is subject to Dissonance, and must act as the mage's personal servant (and thus not the same personality as the &quot;donor&quot; in the first place). Hardly a natural ghost that really should have no bearing on this discussion at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-04-2017, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T09:16:14-07:00","id":1111294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111285#post1111285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes. As far as I know, the only way to do that is through Death Mastery. And that's no different, imho, than making a perfect clone of anyone else, living or dead or otherwise. An artificial creation with a Duration that expires and is subject to Dissonance, and must act as the mage's personal servant (and thus not the same personality as the &amp;quot;donor&amp;quot; in the first place). Hardly a natural ghost that really should have no bearing on this discussion at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts can also form when a person experiences a traumatic near death experience, but it is incredibly rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T10:27:55-07:00","id":1111332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111294#post1111294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts can also form when a person experiences a traumatic near death experience, but it is incredibly rare.</div> </div> </div> </div> Do you have a reference? I don't see this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T10:30:01-07:00","id":1111335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111332#post1111332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do you have a reference? I don't see this.</div> </div> </div> </div>If memory serves, I read about it in the mage 2e book about ghosts, or I read about it when people were discussing the second edition of sin eater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T12:04:40-07:00","id":1111376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111285#post1111285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes. As far as I know, the only way to do that is through Death Mastery. And that's no different, imho, than making a perfect clone of anyone else, living or dead or otherwise. An artificial creation with a Duration that expires and is subject to Dissonance, and must act as the mage's personal servant (and thus not the same personality as the &quot;donor&quot; in the first place). Hardly a natural ghost that really should have no bearing on this discussion at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it was teased in the Geist's thread that sometimes a person doesn't needs to die to leave a ghost behind in a &quot;natural&quot; way. I think it was Dave, but I don't remember the place of the exact quote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T13:12:27-07:00","id":1111386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111376#post1111376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it was teased in the Geist's thread that sometimes a person doesn't needs to die to leave a ghost behind in a &amp;quot;natural&amp;quot; way. I think it was Dave, but I don't remember the place of the exact quote.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd actually be really cool if Bound left ghosts the first time they died.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T13:39:08-07:00","id":1111397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111386#post1111386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That'd actually be really cool if Bound left ghosts the first time they died.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think somebody mentioned something about the Bargain being made between your ghost and your Geist, although I don't really have a source.<br /> <br /> I can't prevent you from quoting me on that, but I would recommend that you did not, as I cannot guarantee its accuracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T13:55:09-07:00","id":1111401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111397#post1111397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think somebody mentioned something about the Bargain being made between your ghost and your Geist, although I don't really have a source.<br /> <br /> I can't prevent you from quoting me on that, but I would recommend that you did not, as I cannot guarantee its accuracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was brought up as a possible answer as to who or what the geist enters the Bargain with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T13:58:19-07:00","id":1111402,"title":"","content":"Hmm... That's kind of disappointing, I prefer the Bargain be struck with the person. It is their body after all, they should be the one who agrees to share it with a Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T14:04:10-07:00","id":1111404,"title":"","content":"weird- I, on the other hand, remember that when the topic was brought up, Dave said something like &quot;who told you that?&quot;, in a context of denying that theory. On the other hand, I may misremember things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T14:04:51-07:00","id":1111405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\