mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T14:59:22-07:00","id":1111421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111416#post1111416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> In the same way beloved pets might inherit your fortune...</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that, in many cases, ghosts are sentient, and they are uniquely suited to carry out the post-death wishes of the body's owner, seeing as they possess most if not all of that person's memories and personality, and would probably have an innate desire to carry out their wishes.<br /> <br /> I could not think of a single more desirable heir for the inheritance of my body than somebody who is as close as they could possibly be to being me, with a vested interest in doing things I would want done.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T15:49:38-07:00","id":1111433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111405#post1111405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One could argue that your Ghost has a claim to inheriting it in the event of your passing.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Hey wait a second, the new primary antagonists of GtSE 2E will be those masked ghosts, right? People wear masks when they want to conceal their face... or when they can't reveal their face. What if these masked ghosts are of the latter case, and the reason they can't reveal their own face is that the world doesn't allow them, because someone else is already kicking and alive using their face?<br /> <br /> We also know that &quot;second chance&quot; is a major theme in Geist. What else can emphasize that you are indeed living a second chance at life, than a personification of your first chance at life?<br /> <br /> Okay, now I'm going to use &quot;Your Own Ghost&quot; as antagonists when I ever get to Geist, whatever the 2E primary antagonists for the Bound turn out to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111416#post1111416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> In the same way beloved pets might inherit your fortune...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're getting a bit too focused on the &quot;ghosts are not the same person they remember being&quot; part, to the point of overlooking the &quot;ghosts are people on their own right&quot; part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T15:51:16-07:00","id":1111435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111420#post1111420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It worked for the Aristocats.<br /> <br /> I seriously don't get your post, though. A ghost is nothing like a pet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, maybe using the pet metaphor wasn't that good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> Except that from the subject matter being discussed, and popular mythology of what I know about ghosts, is that your Ghost is largely concerned with whatever emotions / business it was created to fulfill. Your Ghost might retain your memories and your personality, but it's reasons for being in this world are largely driven by a singular purpose. In that sense, the Ghost is nothing more than a cheap, knock off imitation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T16:21:26-07:00","id":1111446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111435#post1111435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that sense, the Ghost is nothing more than a cheap, knock off imitation.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the sense that they make poor substitutes for life-extensions, sure.<br /> <br /> As executors of your life's final housekeeping, though?<br /> <br /> This is the ideal: When something goes wrong and you shed your mortal coil out of joint, when your earthly passions grow thick and twisted in the morass of living and dying? You <i>absolutely</i> want to call up something that can use your identity to pry out the digging hooks of the world from your fading soul, something that <i>wants</i> to do so because it is bound to this pale half-world until its case is solved.<br /> <br /> (That the Underworld is venal and corrupt and sorely lacking in oversight and populated by worms made from men who despair of ever returning to the butterfly dream is unfortunate. That new ghosts are often sorely underequipped and underinformed for their tasks is a pity. That the last gasps of the wicked are seldom denied the same call for &quot;justice&quot; as the innocent is troublesome. That a failsafe of any sort has emerged from the resulting mess is a vital source of comfort for many.)<br /> <br /> Point is, in normal circumstances a ghost is for carrying out your last will and testament, not for being your second chance at living forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T16:35:45-07:00","id":1111455,"title":"","content":"Of course, it was just mentioned as a possibility. And, tbh, I doubt that's how it will be in 2E. I have a hard time seeing the writers presenting the protagonist to GtSE with the same type of personalities that ghosts have. It's more likely the Bargain somehow allows the geist to talk with the actual person (or at least a more accurate representation), resurrecting the actual person, and then the geist filling the metaphysical slot of the soul, removing the effects of soulloss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T17:16:26-07:00","id":1111469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111446#post1111446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the sense that they make poor substitutes for life-extensions, sure.<br /> <br /> As executors of your life's final housekeeping, though?<br /> <br /> This is the ideal: When something goes wrong and you shed your mortal coil out of joint, when your earthly passions grow thick and twisted in the morass of living and dying? You <i>absolutely</i> want to call up something that can use your identity to pry out the digging hooks of the world from your fading soul, something that <i>wants</i> to do so because it is bound to this pale half-world until its case is solved.<br /> <br /> (That the Underworld is venal and corrupt and sorely lacking in oversight and populated by worms made from men who despair of ever returning to the butterfly dream is unfortunate. That new ghosts are often sorely underequipped and underinformed for their tasks is a pity. That the last gasps of the wicked are seldom denied the same call for &quot;justice&quot; as the innocent is troublesome. That a failsafe of any sort has emerged from the resulting mess is a vital source of comfort for many.)<br /> <br /> Point is, in normal circumstances a ghost is for carrying out your last will and testament, not for being your second chance at living forever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But what happens to them after they've fulfilled that purpose and have no more connection to this mortal world? They descend to the Underworld, which is described to me as being a place infinitely worse than simply fading out of existence. And any Ghosts trapped there start to go insane. Geists are the remains of people who have been dead for so long, they don't even remember who they are supposed to be, all they have left is impulsive desires and an all consuming desperation to claw their way back to the world of the living.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's why I ask why a Sin Eater should really care about laying Ghosts to rest, especially since the actual dead person appears to be missing somewhere. If the Ghost is just an echo of them, and one doomed to succumb to madness, then they should just destroy Ghosts on sight to prevent future tragedies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-04-2017, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T17:37:08-07:00","id":1111474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111469#post1111469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But what happens to them after they've fulfilled that purpose and have no more connection to this mortal world? They descend to the Underworld, which is described to me as being a place infinitely worse than simply fading out of existence. And any Ghosts trapped there start to go insane. Geists are the remains of people who have been dead for so long, they don't even remember who they are supposed to be, all they have left is impulsive desires and an all consuming desperation to claw their way back to the world of the living.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's why I ask why a Sin Eater should really care about laying Ghosts to rest, especially since the actual dead person appears to be missing somewhere. If the Ghost is just an echo of them, and one doomed to succumb to madness, then they should just destroy Ghosts on sight to prevent future tragedies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts descend to the Underworld when their Anchors are <i>destroyed</i>. When their Anchors are <i>resolved</i>, they vanish. (Or at least, that's how I remember things working.) The theory is that the latter is the only way for the soul that the ghost spawned out of to be put to rest. Destroying the ghost would be the equivalent of removing all the symptoms of a disease instead of curing the disease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T17:45:30-07:00","id":1111477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111469#post1111469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And any Ghosts trapped there start to go insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the opposite of what the Underworld does to ghosts who wind up there and even in the case of persistence beyond their ostensible role the Great Below provides new things for the unquiet dead to do as denizens of Tartarus. Not having to worry about Being John Doe means you can reinvent yourself in the tunnels after life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Geists are the remains of people who have been dead for so long, they don't even remember who they are supposed to be, all they have left is impulsive desires and an all consuming desperation to claw their way back to the world of the living. </div> </div> </div>Geister are people who've become part archetype of death and thus bear influence over ghosts. This is not a degenerative state.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why I ask why a Sin Eater should really care about laying Ghosts to rest, especially since the actual dead person appears to be missing somewhere. If the Ghost is just an echo of them, and one doomed to succumb to madness, then they should just destroy Ghosts on sight to prevent future tragedies. </div> </div> </div>The number of ghosts who exist solely to try and convey a message to the living suggests this is a counterproductive course of action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T17:53:12-07:00","id":1111478,"title":"","content":"And now I shamelessly quote myself:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111433#post1111433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we're getting a bit too focused on the &quot;ghosts are not the same person they remember being&quot; part, to the point of overlooking the &quot;ghosts are people on their own right&quot; part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nyrufa, with due all respects and no offense, between the &quot;ghosts are cheap imitations,&quot; &quot;ghosts going insane is only a matter of time&quot; and &quot;better to euthanize ghosts than communicate with them,&quot; I'm getting the idea that you're determined to perceive ghosts solely as abominations who shouldn't be treated as anything even close to people. Please correct me if I'm dead wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T19:34:37-07:00","id":1111503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111477#post1111477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the opposite of what the Underworld does to ghosts who wind up there and even in the case of persistence beyond their ostensible role the Great Below provides new things for the unquiet dead to do as denizens of Tartarus. Not having to worry about Being John Doe means you can reinvent yourself in the tunnels after life.<br /> <br /> Geister are people who've become part archetype of death and thus bear influence over ghosts. This is not a degenerative state.<br /> <br /> <br /> The number of ghosts who exist solely to try and convey a message to the living suggests this is a counterproductive course of action.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, well that's the information I was given by watching online reviews of the game. One of them described Geists as being ancient amalgamations of souls who want to experience life and all it has to offer. <i><b>Everything</b></i>, that life has to offer, including the thrill of strangling a man to death as you watch the life fade from his eyes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So first impressions left me with the idea that once you die in CoD, it's a downward spiral to madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-04-2017, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T19:37:07-07:00","id":1111505,"title":"","content":"'Humanity's reliance on artificial enhancements such as weapons, tools and shelter has stripped them of their natural defenses and weapons. A basic human outfitted with nothing but what nature itself has graced them with is fragile, short lived, and woefully incapable of defending itself.&quot;<br /> <br /> Tools, Weapons, and Shelter ARE what nature graced humanity with, the idea that the artificial and nature are separate is an illusion, because nothing that exists can be separate from nature, everything is both a product of nature and a part of nature. <br /> <br /> The resources that go into artificial things all come from nature, using the forces found in nature, guided by minds that evolved into existence by the laws of nature, using and depending on the elements of nature, which utilitize things found in nature, and made up of the elements of nature. The artificial is an illusion, everything is nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T19:43:12-07:00","id":1111510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111478#post1111478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now I shamelessly quote myself:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nyrufa, with due all respects and no offense, between the &quot;ghosts are cheap imitations,&quot; &quot;ghosts going insane is only a matter of time&quot; and &quot;better to euthanize ghosts than communicate with them,&quot; I'm getting the idea that you're determined to perceive ghosts solely as abominations who shouldn't be treated as anything even close to people. Please correct me if I'm dead wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You're not wrong. If the Ghost was the actual continued state of somebody who died and is tormented by business or emotions that went unfulfilled, then that would be different. But you guys have explained that is not the case. The Ghost isn't you. You've gone off somewhere that nobody, including the books themselves seem to know where. The Ghost is just an imitation of the person you used to be, and in some cases doesn't even require you to be dead in order for it to start haunting the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> I was involved in a similar topic about how you would feel if vampirism wasn't a state of existence, but a parasite that kills the host and then subsumes their identity. I feel the same way now as I did then.<br /> <br /> I don't care if a creature shares my memories, personality, and desires. I do not and will not see it as an extension of myself. In order for it to be me, my actual consciousness must inhabit it. Otherwise, it's nothing more than an imposter pretending to be me, and I would destroy it with the same amount of prejudice I would destroy an evil clone.<br /> <br /> Fetches get the same treatment!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-04-2017, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T19:48:31-07:00","id":1111514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111510#post1111510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> You're not wrong. If the Ghost was the actual continued state of somebody who died and is tormented by business or emotions that went unfulfilled, then that would be different. But you guys have explained that is not the case. The Ghost isn't you. You've gone off somewhere that nobody, including the books themselves seem to know where. The Ghost is just an imitation of the person you used to be, and in some cases doesn't even require you to be dead in order for it to start haunting the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the impression that the existing material is actually ambiguous as to whether the ghost is really the person or not.<br /> <br /> Which is preferable to me over outright stating that ghosts aren't really the people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T19:50:15-07:00","id":1111515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111505#post1111505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Humanity's reliance on artificial enhancements such as weapons, tools and shelter has stripped them of their natural defenses and weapons. A basic human outfitted with nothing but what nature itself has graced them with is fragile, short lived, and woefully incapable of defending itself.&quot;<br /> <br /> Tools, Weapons, and Shelter ARE what nature graced humanity with, the idea that the artificial and nature are separate is an illusion, because nothing that exists can be separate from nature, everything is both a product of nature and a part of nature.<br /> <br /> The resources that go into artificial things all come from nature, using the forces found in nature, guided by minds that evolved into existence by the laws of nature, using and depending on the elements of nature, which utilitize things found in nature, and made up of the elements of nature. The artificial is an illusion, everything is nature.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Little late to the party. We're discussing the nature of Ghosts, now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But no, those aren't what nature graced humans with. The earth didn't just erect cottages and huts out of the ground, or fashion rocks and wood into primitive tools for humans to use. That's something they did on their own.<br /> <br /> It's artificial and unnatural, unlike the monsters who's super human abilities are a natural part of what they are. They're not invoking it through artificial means like technology and science. They're drawing upon their own physiology and mental capacities. Unlike humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> The only exception to this would be Mages (and possibly Psychics), and we're not 100% sure if those qualify as monsters or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-04-2017, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T20:22:25-07:00","id":1111531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111515#post1111515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Little late to the party. We're discussing the nature of Ghosts, now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But no, those aren't what nature graced humans with. The earth didn't just erect cottages and huts out of the ground, or fashion rocks and wood into primitive tools for humans to use. That's something they did on their own.<br /> <br /> It's artificial and unnatural, unlike the monsters who's super human abilities are a natural part of what they are. They're not invoking it through artificial means like technology and science. They're drawing upon their own physiology and mental capacities. Unlike humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they're not unnatural. What nature graced humans with is intellect, the ability to create and use tools, the ability to ask &quot;why?&quot;, the ability to understand the universe well enough to build a nuclear bomb, the ability to develop and refine technology and advance constantly.<br /> <br /> This is all natural. It's part of what humans are. It's not something separate that has no place in the world, it is a part of the world.<br /> <br /> What is artificial is saying that this isn't something humans can lay claim to, that it's unnatural and artificial and thus plays no role in humanity's place in the world<i>.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T20:29:55-07:00","id":1111535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111531#post1111531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What is artificial is saying that this isn't something humans can lay claim to, that it's unnatural and artificial and thus plays no role in humanity's place in the world<i>.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>No, &quot;artificial&quot; means that it's man made. It doesn't exist on its own in nature.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------<br /> <br /> Definition 1: Made or produced by human beings, rather than occurring naturally. Typically as a copy of something natural.<br /> <br /> Definition 2: (of a person's behavior or personality) insincere or affected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T21:42:57-07:00","id":1111552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111535#post1111535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, &quot;artificial&quot; means that it's man made. It doesn't exist on its own in nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so citing a dictionary is rarely convincing. Usually, words have much more nuanced and broadly defined meanings that go beyond their dictionary definitions. In this case, calling your argument artificial might make more sense to you if I offered a few synonyms, as harvested from thesaurus.com:<br /> <br /> Bogus, phony, sham, specious, spurious, or false.<br /> <br /> That is to say that arguing that the human ability to use tools is artificial or unnatural is not a valid argument. Certainly, it is fair to point out that things humans make don't exist on their own in nature, but that doesn't make them <i>bad</i> or <i>wrong</i> or <i>unnatural</i> or any other loaded term one might care to use. Humans using our intellect to make things should not be disqualified from any discussion of humanity's advantages or abilities.<br /> <br /> And I mean if we want to talk about <i>artificial</i> I believe there's prometheans, and if you're talking about <i>unnatural</i>, there's vampires. If humans have all our technology disqualified, then vampires and prometheans should be disqualified entirely. Which is also absurd and wouldn't be reasonable in a discussion about whether humanity has advantages to leverage against supernaturals - just as claiming that humanity's tools and technologies shouldn't count is also absurd and unreasonable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T22:12:53-07:00","id":1111555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111515#post1111515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But no, those aren't what nature graced humans with. The earth didn't just erect cottages and huts out of the ground, or fashion rocks and wood into primitive tools for humans to use. That's something they did on their own.<br /> <br /> It's artificial and unnatural</div> </div> </div> </div>By this definition, a beaver damn is unnatural. A beehive is unnatural. A spiderweb is unnatural. A hole dug in the ground by a gopher is unnatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T22:18:14-07:00","id":1111556,"title":"","content":"Okay with the technology thing one thing that's bugged is a few people arguing about tech as an advantage as if it were a unique advantage. Like one person argued that humans could easily conquer vampires because the human could just break out the flamethrower, but the same wouldn't hold for most other splats. On the other hand arguing that technology is inherently off limits isn't really helping since then you also have to argue how far back do we count something as tech? Does the bashing rock count as tech, does the pointed stick count as tech, is language technology since we developed that to communicate and transfer ideas and information?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T23:26:22-07:00","id":1111565,"title":"","content":"I agree that the use of technology is not an inherent advantage of mortals, nothing stops one of the monster splats from using the same tools/tech. But thinking more about it, the use of supernatural abilities is not an inherent advantage of supernaturals either. Mortals have access to many supernatural merits that mimic or approximate the abilities of the various splat. There is also rituals to summon, bind/ward and banish ephemeral entities (like spirits) for a variety of effects. And you have the endowments that Hunters have access to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T00:25:39-07:00","id":1111570,"title":"","content":"Yup I think if we were going to compare then one would have to break it down on criteria vs ease and commonality. Example Demons have an advantage in gathering and disseminating information as the entire splat speaks any language that has native speakers and have perfect memory. While humans have it easier to pass along, since they don't have to worry about cover being blown, that the unchained can swipe between languages on the fly and use exceptionally obscure dialects means it can be harder to crack information and needs not be out as long.<br /> <br /> On the other hand humans have the easiest time organizing with eachother. Not that other splats can't organize and work together, but picking a random person out in a crowd and identifying another of your kind without getting it wrong is something only Beasts have a power that helps with. A human has pretty good odds that anyone they pick is another human and not a splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 07-05-2017, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T00:46:11-07:00","id":1111573,"title":"","content":"Long story shotgunned: this discussion is really about the value of vulnerability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T05:24:55-07:00","id":1111619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111556#post1111556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay with the technology thing one thing that's bugged is a few people arguing about tech as an advantage as if it were a unique advantage. Like one person argued that humans could easily conquer vampires because the human could just break out the flamethrower, but the same wouldn't hold for most other splats. On the other hand arguing that technology is inherently off limits isn't really helping since then you also have to argue how far back do we count something as tech? Does the bashing rock count as tech, does the pointed stick count as tech, is language technology since we developed that to communicate and transfer ideas and information?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Exactly. This argument about humanity's greatest strength laying in its ability to create weapons, tools, shelter and other things associated with their high intellect doesn't hold up because the monsters in this situation can do the exact same thing.<br /> <br /> Humans aren't fighting mindless creatures in the CoD, they're fighting intelligent, thinking creatures who have lived among their population for thousands of years undetected. To use vampires as a basic example, I don't see them going to war with their bare fists, or taking shelter from the sun by burying themselves in the dirt (granted, some do). But no, they used the same arms and armor humans have been using throughout the ages, and they take shelter within human constructs. So to say technology is a trait exclusive to humanity is just bull.<br /> <br /> <br /> Humanity's strength is not its technological progress, it's the sheer numbers with which they overwhelm the supernatural population.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Here's a quote from the Requiem rule book:</b> Yeah, it sucks having to hide from your food. Yeah, you could take any mortal without thinking about it. When you can take out a few thousand of 'em, then you come talk to me. Until then, keep your fucking head down. ~Nosferatu, giving their thoughts about Mortals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111565#post1111565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that the use of technology is not an inherent advantage of mortals, nothing stops one of the monster splats from using the same tools/tech. But thinking more about it, the use of supernatural abilities is not an inherent advantage of supernaturals either. Mortals have access to many supernatural merits that mimic or approximate the abilities of the various splat. There is also rituals to summon, bind/ward and banish ephemeral entities (like spirits) for a variety of effects. And you have the endowments that Hunters have access to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that those abilities are rare and only exist in specially gifted / expertly trained humans. The powers wielded by the supernaturals belong to every member of their species; not divided up among a privileged few. Granted that not every supernatural has access to the same powers and abilities as each other, but every individual member is super human in some way, shape or form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-05-2017, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T05:40:55-07:00","id":1111624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111570#post1111570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand humans have the easiest time organizing with eachother. Not that other splats can't organize and work together, but picking a random person out in a crowd and identifying another of your kind without getting it wrong is something only Beasts have a power that helps with. A human has pretty good odds that anyone they pick is another human and not a splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>A vampire's Predatory Aura helps them identify other predatory supernatural splats; it only works on first seeing the person, but it's still there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T10:25:30-07:00","id":1111700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111619#post1111619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Exactly. This argument about humanity's greatest strength laying in its ability to create weapons, tools, shelter and other things associated with their high intellect doesn't hold up because the monsters in this situation can do the exact same thing.<br /> <br /> Humans aren't fighting mindless creatures in the CoD, they're fighting intelligent, thinking creatures who have lived among their population for thousands of years undetected. To use vampires as a basic example, I don't see them going to war with their bare fists, or taking shelter from the sun by burying themselves in the dirt (granted, some do). But no, they used the same arms and armor humans have been using throughout the ages, and they take shelter within human constructs. So to say technology is a trait exclusive to humanity is just bull.<br /> <br /> <br /> Humanity's strength is not its technological progress, it's the sheer numbers with which they overwhelm the supernatural population.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Here's a quote from the Requiem rule book:</b> Yeah, it sucks having to hide from your food. Yeah, you could take any mortal without thinking about it. When you can take out a few thousand of 'em, then you come talk to me. Until then, keep your fucking head down. ~Nosferatu, giving their thoughts about Mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the interesting side effects of humans creating all kinds of technological advantages is that humans also create organizations that have access to large amounts of those technological advantages. For example, police having access to military gear. So they have these numbers and they're often armed. Sure, supernaturals can access these armaments as well, but I still don't think that cancels out humanity's technological advantage. It might equalize that advantage at times, but that's about it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T12:15:01-07:00","id":1111767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111700#post1111700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the interesting side effects of humans creating all kinds of technological advantages is that humans also create organizations that have access to large amounts of those technological advantages. For example, police having access to military gear. So they have these numbers and they're often armed. Sure, supernaturals can access these armaments as well, but I still don't think that cancels out humanity's technological advantage. It might equalize that advantage at times, but that's about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And the supernaturals have done the same thing. Not every faction is devoted to mysticism and the occult. Seems like every time I mention the supernaturals have <i>blended in with human civilization</i>, it goes ignored.<br /> <br /> <b>Example 1: The Invictus</b> - Vampire shadow government who control the city from the inside out. I absolutely refuse to believe they don't have several high ranking officers / crime lords on their pay roll who can grant them and their ghouls access to large amounts of weaponry should they need it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Example 2: Iron Masters</b> - Werewolves who recognize the potential value of human civilization and choose to live in the cities, instead of out in the wilds. It would be very surprising if their packs didn't have connections with local gun runners and hunting associations to make their jobs easier when battling hostile spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> The monsters aren't hiding in the closest going <i>&quot;hee, hee, hee, you can't see me!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> No, they've infiltrated your society and are actually doing shit to ensure their continued functionality. Any system of government or social structure that you believe humanity can draw upon, supernaturals can do the exact same thing. There is no way they would have been able to remain hidden for this long if that was not the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T12:30:59-07:00","id":1111777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1111767#post1111767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> And the supernaturals have done the same thing. Not every faction is devoted to mysticism and the occult. Seems like every time I mention the supernaturals have <i>blended in with human civilization</i>, it goes ignored.<br /> <br /> <b>Example 1: The Invictus</b> - Vampire shadow government who control the city from the inside out. I absolutely refuse to believe they don't have several high ranking officers / crime lords on their pay roll who can grant them and their ghouls access to large amounts of weaponry should they need it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Example 2: Iron Masters</b> - Werewolves who recognize the potential value of human civilization and choose to live in the cities, instead of out in the wilds. It would be very surprising if their packs didn't have connections with local gun runners and hunting associations to make their jobs easier when battling hostile spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> The monsters aren't hiding in the closest going <i>&quot;hee, hee, hee, you can't see me!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> No, they've infiltrated your society and are actually doing shit to ensure their continued functionality. Any system of government or social structure that you believe humanity can draw upon, supernaturals can do the exact same thing. There is no way they would have been able to remain hidden for this long if that was not the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Invictus do not control the city inside and out. They have influence over mortal society, but it's far from absolute and doesn't grant them control over every mortal institution.<br /> <br /> Anyway, with all this goalpost shifting, I'm out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T20:58:03-07:00","id":1113087,"title":"","content":"My first post!<br /> <br /> I dont have a lot to add to this topic, because its sort of very... I dont know. Kind of hard to define. (despite using transhuman in my username, Im firmly of the belief that seeking transhumanity in the WoD or CoD is sort of foolish.)<br /> <br /> On the ghost personhood thing though, Its my personal opinion that they are validly the human that spawned them, Atleast as much as a Vampire is the human they were spawned from. Changed, possibly disconnected from the 'original' continuation, but still a valid continuation. A mildly to majorly warped version of 'me' is still 'me', just a mildly to majorly different 'me'. in fact, Ghosts that exist past one's ressurection, or that get spawned while one are still alive, would still be 'me' Just.. again, a mildly different me, since from their perspective they transformed into a ghost and some other 'them' inhabits their body. The validity of the ghost being 'me' only gets much more valid if I happen to remain dead, since there is no evidence that a 'true' soul exists, since the 'soul' doesnt seem to really carry much consciousness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1110462#post1110462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two significant domains in Book of the Dead make it plain that the gods of death can dredge up a blank slate that starts to act like the ghost of someone you desperately want to raise from the dead, that identifiers are fungible, and that it is the nature of human identity to gradually wash away in the tides of time and death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having recently got that book I only recall one domain that has a 'possible' God of death, and it actually makes it very vague as to whats really going on with such summoned ghosts, pretty much just running with the assumption that they are somehow simply revived. (as revived as a ghost gets anyway.) aside from an odd bout of amnesia that gets better over time. It does go on to suggest that the ghosts -might- be blank slates that are feeding off your memories of the one who summoned them, though even that is merely presented as a side theory.<br /> A far shot from 'making it plain' however.<br /> That being said, the fact I only recall one rather then two such domains does mean I may well be missing something. I did only read the book over once, and I probably skipped some stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On the other subject about bizzare ideas of what counts as an advantage and what counts as 'natural' I should point out that with ''Mirrors&quot; stuff such as Dark heros, Conviction, or Reason, can exist in any particular chronicle, which greatly bolster Normal mortal power by a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13637-transhumanmarina","name":"TranshumanMarina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T21:27:31-07:00","id":1113097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TranshumanMarina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113087#post1113087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having recently got that book I only recall one domain that has a 'possible' God of death, and it actually makes it very vague as to whats really going on with such summoned ghosts, pretty much just running with the assumption that they are somehow simply revived. (as revived as a ghost gets anyway.) aside from an odd bout of amnesia that gets better over time. It does go on to suggest that the ghosts -might- be blank slates that are feeding off your memories of the one who summoned them, though even that is merely presented as a side theory.<br /> A far shot from 'making it plain' however.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sentence <i>did</i> end <i>after</i> the bit about what Polydegmon can do, I hope you realize.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That being said, the fact I only recall one rather then two such domains does mean I may well be missing something. I did only read the book over once, and I probably skipped some stuff. </div> </div> </div>The Ocean of Fragments is an entire domain whose primary widget is the singular body of water where you can slough off and reincorporate &quot;all the things that make you you&quot; at increasing levels of significance. Multiple characters in that domain are specified to have not only lost much of who they used to be but also picked up and claimed bits that used to belong to somebody else. Between this and the way Mictlantecuhtli's summoned &quot;souls&quot; function, it's abundantly plain that the things that make up ghostly identity are fungible.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ghosts often lie and exaggerate&quot; is a thing that Geist directly says, the corebook introduces a Numen that allows a ghost to impersonate literally anybody's dead loved ones, Book of the Dead's Risks and Rewards section for Rescue hints at an outcome for &quot;resurrection&quot; that could indicate that the raised ghost is either displaying symptoms of the kind of drastic change that the Underworld is known to be able to affect on those who cross its thresholds or else is a flawed imitation being worn by a nameless <i>thing</i> from the deadlands.<br /> <br /> This is not a supernatural neck of the woods whose denizens are known for their honesty, much less for clarity as concerns what they really are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T22:46:22-07:00","id":1113122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TranshumanMarina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113087#post1113087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first post!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to the forums, then! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But I think your analogy of vampires and ghosts is a little inaccurate. The vampire has more credence to suggest it is the original person by virtue of it possessing at least some degree of a soul. That's how diablerie works, you absorb a vampire's soul along with their knowledge, power and (occasionally) their personality. The Vampire also makes a conscious effort to struggle against their monstrous urges and retain as much of its former identity as possible.<br /> <br /> A Ghost is just a pale imitation of somebody else who is driven by specific goals in mind. It doesn't even have a soul, as far as I'm aware.<br /> <br /> As to the subject of the &quot;true&quot; soul, I'm hard pressed to disagree. Conventional mythology states that a Ghost actually IS a soul that continues to persist after death. But that does not seem to be the case in CoD. People who spawn ghosts but survive the experience don't seem to show signs of becoming soulless. Or if they do, I haven't come across any information like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> I also wouldn't call transhumanism in the CoD all that foolish. I consider some of the splats are actually quite tolerable of an existence. To me, the horror and drama comes not from being a monster, but from all the constant bullshit they have to put up with, such as vicious rivals, cutthroat politics, hunter organizations and the like.<br /> <br /> Basically once you become a monster, everybody wants to kill you... But on the bright side, you get all kinds of super powers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-08-2017, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T23:13:36-07:00","id":1113129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113122#post1113122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think your analogy of vampires and ghosts is a little inaccurate. The vampire has more credence to suggest it is the original person by virtue of it possessing at least some degree of a soul. That's how diablerie works, you absorb a vampire's soul along with their knowledge, power and (occasionally) their personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is possible the soul does whatever usually happens to souls when one dies, then is remade at least in part by the Beast. Death is a necessary part of the Embrace, and the 'coming back as a vampire' part doesn't have to be immediate, giving plenty of time for a soul to fly away. And of course whether someone has a soul or not doesn't mean they're more or less of a person. Souls are interchangeable, you could take one from another and put it in the hole where yours was and not skip a beat unless you were the introspective type.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Vampire also makes a conscious effort to struggle against their monstrous urges and retain as much of its former identity as possible. </div> </div> </div>This could just be their memories, which to some makes them more of 'that person' than something like a soul.<br /> <br /> We discussed a variant of this idea in another thread, where someone wanted to have vampires in their game not be the people they were from, but instead be replaced by something else during the Embrace. From the point of view that they were going by, it didn't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T23:33:19-07:00","id":1113131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113129#post1113129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is possible the soul does whatever usually happens to souls when one dies, then is remade at least in part by the Beast. Death is a necessary part of the Embrace, and the 'coming back as a vampire' part doesn't have to be immediate, giving plenty of time for a soul to fly away. And of course whether someone has a soul or not doesn't mean they're more or less of a person. Souls are interchangeable, you could take one from another and put it in the hole where yours was and not skip a beat unless you were the introspective type.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why this question is so difficult to answer in the CoD world. It completely tears down what most people in the real world believe a soul is supposed to be and replaces it with its own obscure version.<br /> <br /> <br /> In literally every other form of media I've ever studied / come across, a soul is supposed to be the very essence of your being. Your body is just a container, the soul is what forms your personality, your ambitions, everything that makes you a person. Removing the soul has one of two consequences. Either A) your body collapses dead on the floor, or B) your body continues to function, but as an emotionless shell devoid of personality.<br /> <br /> Replacing a missing soul with a new one does not restore the body's original personality. It replaces it with that of the new soul. In other words, the transferred soul possesses the new body and claims it for their own, or seeks to return to its original body if at all possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> But in CoD, your soul is more like... I don't know, some kind of metaphysical battery system? It keeps the subject charged with motivation, but it's not the actual source of their motivation. A person's thoughts, actions and personality seem to be directly linked to either their physical body, or some other metaphysical aspect that nobody has mentioned here, yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's all very confusing and seemingly impossible to give a satisfactory answer to the nature of what makes a person real or false.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T01:03:09-07:00","id":1113146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113131#post1113131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why this question is so difficult to answer in the CoD world. It completely tears down what most people in the real world believe a soul is supposed to be and replaces it with its own obscure version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Try to keep in mind that your beliefs do not necessarily reflect those of 'most people in the real world.' It's influenced by a popular religion that much of the media caters to. The same idea flies in the face of things like, say, Buddhism. Chronicles' fits more with the idea of animism, appropriately.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In literally every other form of media I've ever studied / come across, a soul is supposed to be the very essence of your being. Your body is just a container, the soul is what forms your personality, your ambitions, everything that makes you a person. Removing the soul has one of two consequences. Either A) your body collapses dead on the floor, or B) your body continues to function, but as an emotionless shell devoid of personality. </div> </div> </div>You might watch something like Buffy or Supernatural. There when rendered soulless ones morality faces a shift, which is similar to Chronicles, except in the shows they usually become evil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But in CoD, your soul is more like... I don't know, some kind of metaphysical battery system? It keeps the subject charged with motivation, but it's not the actual source of their motivation. A person's thoughts, actions and personality seem to be directly linked to either their physical body, or some other metaphysical aspect that nobody has mentioned here, yet. </div> </div> </div>There's a lot more than motivation involved. Take a soul away and eventually a person is going to wither and die. It's similar to the spirit of an object.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's all very confusing and seemingly impossible to give a satisfactory answer to the nature of what makes a person real or false. </div> </div> </div>Like real life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-08-2017, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T04:04:08-07:00","id":1113177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113146#post1113146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Try to keep in mind that your beliefs do not necessarily reflect those of 'most people in the real world.' It's influenced by a popular religion that much of the media caters to. The same idea flies in the face of things like, say, Buddhism. Chronicles' fits more with the idea of animism, appropriately.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You might watch something like Buffy or Supernatural. There when rendered soulless ones morality faces a shift, which is similar to Chronicles, except in the shows they usually become evil.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's a lot more than motivation involved. Take a soul away and eventually a person is going to wither and die. It's similar to the spirit of an object.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Like real life.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I've never heard anything about there being multiple souls / pieces of a soul in Buddhism (CoD seems to suggest we have at least 3). And it supports my soul transfer idea by way of reincarnation in which one is often believed to share characteristics of their past lives instead of being an entirely brand new entity. The only religion I can think of where having multiple soul fragments was a thing is the ancient Egyptians, which would lead credence to Mummy being the answer here.<br /> <br /> <br /> The only character in Supernatural who I recall being rendered soulless was Sam and it rendered him devoid of empathy for others. He could still function as a Hunter, but his thoughts were focused entirely on completing the objective no matter what the sacrifice.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Buffy, I don't recall anybody in the show explicitly being referred to as soulless, with the exception of Vampires. But that's because they worked differently in the sense that when a person becomes a vampire, their corpse is possessed by a demon. Their original human soul is replaced by a malevolent spirit who craves the blood of the living. But once their soul is restored (such as with Angel), the vampire had little difficulty maintaining their humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T06:27:02-07:00","id":1113214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113177#post1113177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never heard anything about there being multiple souls / pieces of a soul in Buddhism (CoD seems to suggest we have at least 3).</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, in Buddhism there are no souls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only religion I can think of where having multiple soul fragments was a thing is the ancient Egyptians, which would lead credence to Mummy being the answer here. </div> </div> </div>Hinduism sort of have multiple &quot;souls&quot; (technically it only has one &quot;soul&quot;, but parts that would normally be considered part of ones soul such as your personality/desires/reasoning exist as different things separate to the soul). Multiple religions have soul split into &quot;Spirit&quot; and &quot;Psyche&quot; (including one Christian thing, but it isn't recognized), in Judaism the soul is in five parts. In Taoism people have two &quot;types&quot; of souls, and the exact number of how many of each type of soul people have is subject to debate (the one I see most is three hun and seven po).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T06:35:32-07:00","id":1113219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113122#post1113122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think your analogy of vampires and ghosts is a little inaccurate. The vampire has more credence to suggest it is the original person by virtue of it possessing at least some degree of a soul. That's how diablerie works, you absorb a vampire's soul along with their knowledge, power and (occasionally) their personality. The Vampire also makes a conscious effort to struggle against their monstrous urges and retain as much of its former identity as possible.<br /> <br /> A Ghost is just a pale imitation of somebody else who is driven by specific goals in mind. It doesn't even have a soul, as far as I'm aware.<br /> <br /> As to the subject of the &quot;true&quot; soul, I'm hard pressed to disagree. Conventional mythology states that a Ghost actually IS a soul that continues to persist after death. But that does not seem to be the case in CoD. People who spawn ghosts but survive the experience don't seem to show signs of becoming soulless. Or if they do, I haven't come across any information like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> I also wouldn't call transhumanism in the CoD all that foolish. I consider some of the splats are actually quite tolerable of an existence. To me, the horror and drama comes not from being a monster, but from all the constant bullshit they have to put up with, such as vicious rivals, cutthroat politics, hunter organizations and the like.<br /> <br /> Basically once you become a monster, everybody wants to kill you... But on the bright side, you get all kinds of super powers!</div> </div> </div> </div>Your too stuck on the idea of the soul being 'you'. The soul doesn't do it in CoD, therefore Vampires having one's soul (however tattered it is) does not make them 'you' any more then a lucid dead ghost being 'you'. (rank 2 and lucid dead ghosts, if you recall, have mostly functioning personalities and awareness. moreso with the latter then former.) <br /> <br /> Think about it. If 'true souls' dont exist in CoD (which is a possiblity.) then from your bodily strict perspective, you cease to be. However, from the ghosts perspective, it has your memories, personality, and possibly even is aware that its dead. For all intents and purposes, its just you, transformed, like any other supernatural. The only thing that confuses this matter is the fact that <br /> A. It doesnt have a soul, which as we have established, makes it different in some ways, but hardly makes it absolute that it is not you, since a human can still live and mostly function without a soul. and <br /> B. that a ghost can be made under oddball circumstances while someone is still alive, or brought back to life. All that does is establish that a ghost isnt a nessicary part of a 'living'you, which is easily adressed if you consider it 'a different version of you' or a branch off of some sort.<br /> <br /> (actually, my same arguments here could apply to Fetches before. So yes, I do consider fetches as valid 'you' as I consider ghosts a valid you. Merely that fetches 'split off' on a specific circumstance, rather then on death, leaving them to exist only in the confusing 'two of you' situation.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I think your Edit shows once again, how you percieve the CoD world to be in a way that kiiiind of contradicts pretty much every splat, other then maybe Sin-eaters. and that is less transhuman, and more a second chance with cool powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13637-transhumanmarina","name":"TranshumanMarina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T08:14:09-07:00","id":1113249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TranshumanMarina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113219#post1113219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your too stuck on the idea of the soul being 'you'. The soul doesn't do it in CoD, therefore Vampires having one's soul (however tattered it is) does not make them 'you' any more then a lucid dead ghost being 'you'. (rank 2 and lucid dead ghosts, if you recall, have mostly functioning personalities and awareness. moreso with the latter then former.)<br /> <br /> Think about it. If 'true souls' dont exist in CoD (which is a possiblity.) then from your bodily strict perspective, you cease to be. However, from the ghosts perspective, it has your memories, personality, and possibly even is aware that its dead. For all intents and purposes, its just you, transformed, like any other supernatural. The only thing that confuses this matter is the fact that<br /> A. It doesnt have a soul, which as we have established, makes it different in some ways, but hardly makes it absolute that it is not you, since a human can still live and mostly function without a soul. and<br /> B. that a ghost can be made under oddball circumstances while someone is still alive, or brought back to life. All that does is establish that a ghost isnt a nessicary part of a 'living'you, which is easily adressed if you consider it 'a different version of you' or a branch off of some sort.<br /> <br /> (actually, my same arguments here could apply to Fetches before. So yes, I do consider fetches as valid 'you' as I consider ghosts a valid you. Merely that fetches 'split off' on a specific circumstance, rather then on death, leaving them to exist only in the confusing 'two of you' situation.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I think your Edit shows once again, how you percieve the CoD world to be in a way that kiiiind of contradicts pretty much every splat, other then maybe Sin-eaters. and that is less transhuman, and more a second chance with cool powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Except that a Fetch isn't a form of transhumanism. The person it's based on didn't die or transition into a Fetch, they were abducted and the Fetch was used to supplant them. It is, for all intents and purposes, an impostor who's distracting your friends and family while you're chained up in a dungeon somewhere being tortured by some otherworldly creature. In addition to that, the Fetch is commonly described as being a generally more appealing version of the real you. When you finally escape, you come back to find that your Fetch did its best to make everybody love and trust them, which may not necessarily be how the original person behaved / acted or even wanted to behave / act.<br /> <br /> So even if it has all your memories and your appearance, the Fetch is still not a complete copy of you. It's a cheap imitation; one not too dissimilar from identity theft.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> I wouldn't say I'm stuck on the idea of the soul being you. Just that that's the interpretation I've been familiar with my entire life (turning 30 this year) and am only just now being presented with the idea that this isn't the case. It takes some getting used to when it comes to debating the nature of consciousness, personality, and self identification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T10:01:58-07:00","id":1113280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113177#post1113177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never heard anything about there being multiple souls / pieces of a soul in Buddhism (CoD seems to suggest we have at least 3). And it supports my soul transfer idea by way of reincarnation in which one is often believed to share characteristics of their past lives instead of being an entirely brand new entity. The only religion I can think of where having multiple soul fragments was a thing is the ancient Egyptians, which would lead credence to Mummy being the answer here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Milo v3 got this. There's plenty of religions and belief systems where there's no soul and the end is the end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Buffy, I don't recall anybody in the show explicitly being referred to as soulless, with the exception of Vampires. But that's because they worked differently in the sense that when a person becomes a vampire, their corpse is possessed by a demon. Their original human soul is replaced by a malevolent spirit who craves the blood of the living. But once their soul is restored (such as with Angel), the vampire had little difficulty maintaining their humanity. </div> </div> </div>It happened to regular human characters as well, they ended up acting like vampires. Not with the thirst for blood but with the lack of brakes upon their actions due to morality, the lack of caring. Which is what Chronicles does.<br /> <br /> Between that and Supernatural you already have a third example of what happens.<br /> <br /> If you've happened to watch the Simpsons, you have a fourth. These are much more like Chronicles. Even the TVTropes definition of 'Soulless' is closer to the Chronicles version.<br /> <br /> Nothing feels good anymore. Nothing feels worth it. You try at first, you use up all your Willpower, you do the easiest things you can to muster up more, losing Integrity in the process, but it starts running out anyways and so does your energy and then you're just broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T12:46:08-07:00","id":1113328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113249#post1113249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Except that a Fetch isn't a form of transhumanism. The person it's based on didn't die or transition into a Fetch, they were abducted and the Fetch was used to supplant them. It is, for all intents and purposes, an impostor who's distracting your friends and family while you're chained up in a dungeon somewhere being tortured by some otherworldly creature. In addition to that, the Fetch is commonly described as being a generally more appealing version of the real you. When you finally escape, you come back to find that your Fetch did its best to make everybody love and trust them, which may not necessarily be how the original person behaved / acted or even wanted to behave / act.<br /> <br /> So even if it has all your memories and your appearance, the Fetch is still not a complete copy of you. It's a cheap imitation; one not too dissimilar from identity theft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only are Fetches <i>not</i> restricted solely to that, it is still irrelevant. If a Fetch has all your memories and personality, it's arguably more authentic than the Changeling is (at least, for the hypothetical John Doe's life). They, at least, are still &quot;normal&quot; (as far as they might know), and have been actually living the life in question. Something some Changelings have to face is: they no longer have any claim to that life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T12:46:44-07:00","id":1113330,"title":"","content":"Re: never having thought of the soul as not being essential to the self, and never having thought of ghosts as not being the souls of the departed... that's par four the course in CofD. Atypical takes on common folklore are kind of CofD's thing. Most folks don't think of ghosts and spirits as different things. Most folks don't think of werewolves as human-Spirit hybrids. Most folks don't think of Frankenstein-style monsters as pilgrims seeking to become human. Most folks don't think of wizards as Gnostic \u00dcbermensch. Most folks don't think of fairies as abuse victims. Most folks don't think of Angels and demons as machines. These are not without precedent in associated folklore, but they're not part of the pop cultural image of those creatures. Presenting these unexpected spins on them is what CofD does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T13:03:20-07:00","id":1113340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113280#post1113280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Milo v3 got this. There's plenty of religions and belief systems where there's no soul and the end is the end.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It happened to regular human characters as well, they ended up acting like vampires. Not with the thirst for blood but with the lack of brakes upon their actions due to morality, the lack of caring. Which is what Chronicles does.<br /> <br /> Between that and Supernatural you already have a third example of what happens.<br /> <br /> If you've happened to watch the Simpsons, you have a fourth. These are much more like Chronicles. Even the TVTropes definition of 'Soulless' is closer to the Chronicles version.<br /> <br /> Nothing feels good anymore. Nothing feels worth it. You try at first, you use up all your Willpower, you do the easiest things you can to muster up more, losing Integrity in the process, but it starts running out anyways and so does your energy and then you're just broken.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I have to respectfully disagree with that. If your copy deviates from the choices you would have otherwise made in their place, then it is not a perfect copy of you. That is like saying a bootleg is just as good as the real thing, when often at times they were defective and poorly manufactured.<br /> <br /> <br /> And saying that a Changeling has no claim to their previous life just because horrible things have happened to them is also a dangerous statement. Would you say that an abductee no longer has a claim to their friends and family just because nobody was able to rescue them for several years? The Changeling didn't choose to be kidnapped and tortured, it was forced upon them. And when they finally manage to pull off a desperate escape attempt, they return to the world to find that their Keeper left behind yet another way to torment them.<br /> <br /> Any normal person in this scenario would immediately seek to alert their former life about the dangerous beings they've encountered. It would be incredibly suspicious if they looked past the Fetch's mask and thought to themselves <i>&quot;Yeah, this is better for all of them.&quot;</i> after they had just experienced first hand what the Fae are capable of. This is especially true for durances in which the Changeling barely noticed the passage of time. Which means that from their perspective, they were kidnapped, tortured for a few hours, broke free and then decided it would be better for everybody if they just carved out a new life. <b>That sounds like some dangerously low Clarity logic, right there.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Plus, killing your Fetch and reclaiming your old life is a totally viable option in Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T13:22:14-07:00","id":1113348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113340#post1113340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to respectfully disagree with that. If your copy deviates from the choices you would have otherwise made in their place, then it is not a perfect copy of you. That is like saying a bootleg is just as good as the real thing, when often at times they were defective and poorly manufactured.</div> </div> </div> </div>People are entirely capable of making different decisions on their own or letting decisions be taken out of their hands. If I flip a coin and let fate decide I'm still me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And saying that a Changeling has no claim to their previous life just because horrible things have happened to them is also a dangerous statement. </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure I didn't say anything like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T13:25:24-07:00","id":1113349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113348#post1113348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People are entirely capable of making different decisions on their own or letting decisions be taken out of their hands. If I flip a coin and let fate decide I'm still me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure I didn't say anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Right, accidentally mixed a reply to Vent0 in there.<br /> <br /> And sure, people are capable of making different decisions on their own. But that's for individual people. We're talking about somebody who is supposed to be an effective copy of you and believes itself to be the genuine article. If that were the case, then it should be making the exact same decisions you would have made. If it chooses something different, then that means it isn't a complete copy and therefor can not make the claim to being an extension of yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-08-2017, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T13:29:03-07:00","id":1113350,"title":"","content":"<br /> Pretty sure you mis-quoted there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113340#post1113340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to respectfully disagree with that. If your copy deviates from the choices you would have otherwise made in their place, then it is not a perfect copy of you.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's my point - it does/may make the same choices you would have. In fact, <i>you</i> might not be making the same choices you would have. Your entire argument pre-assumes the validity of one individual's identity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113340#post1113340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is like saying a bootleg is just as good as the real thing, when often at times they were defective and poorly manufactured.</div> </div> </div> </div>Closer comparison - a copy that is still intact when the original is scratched.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113340#post1113340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And saying that a Changeling has no claim to their previous life just because horrible things have happened to them is also a dangerous statement. Would you say that an abductee no longer has a claim to their friends and family just because nobody was able to rescue them for several years? The Changeling didn't choose to be kidnapped and tortured, it was forced upon them. And when they finally manage to pull off a desperate escape attempt, they return to the world to find that their Keeper left behind yet another way to torment them.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm saying that just because the Changeling remembers life &quot;before&quot; and returns after 10 years of being separated from their entire social network, this doesn't entitle them to say &quot;Hey, you know the person you've been friends/family with these past 10 years? Forget them - they're just fake. All their stuff, including relationships to you, are now mine. Now - what did I miss?&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Fetch was living their life - <i>they</i> were the ones making decisions, dealing with the consequences. What the Changeling went through in the between time is irrelevant to this point - they could have instead been asleep or cast forward in time. That life went on without them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113340#post1113340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any normal person in this scenario would immediately seek to alert their former life about the dangerous beings they've encountered. It would be incredibly suspicious if they looked past the Fetch's mask and thought to themselves <i>&quot;Yeah, this is better for all of them.&quot;</i> after they had just experienced first hand what the Fae are capable of. This is especially true for durances in which the Changeling barely noticed the passage of time. Which means that from their perspective, they were kidnapped, tortured for a few hours, broke free and then decided it would be better for everybody if they just carved out a new life. <b>That sounds like some dangerously low Clarity logic, right there.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>So, the Changeling kills their &quot;imposter&quot;, then tries to continue things as they were 10, 20 years ago? Or, ironically, attempt to &quot;imitate&quot; the person their Fetch was?<br /> <br /> To the outside observer - your friend/family has just been replaced by this alien thing pretending to be the one who you know (and failing, to varying degrees), and they claim <i>they</i> are the &quot;real&quot; one? And you should be fine with this?<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's going to turn out well.<br /> This isn't clear cut. The Changeling who goes &quot;Fetch == fake. Kill it and take its stuff.&quot; may be engaging in the murder of another sentient, and then ruining said sentient's relationships out of a sense of entitlement.<br /> <br /> Remind me again where that sits on the Clarity spectrum (especially in comparison to the Others)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113340#post1113340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, killing your Fetch and reclaiming your old life is a totally viable option in Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, it's viable. But it isn't <i>easy</i>, as pointed out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T13:35:42-07:00","id":1113353,"title":"","content":"Something to keep in mind as well, is that your Fetch doesn't know it's not the person whose life it remembers having lived. It didn't make the decision to replace you, It's just going about its business like it thinks it has always done. You could very well be a Fetch and not even know it. That's not to say the Changeling has no claim to their own previous life, but to treat the Fetch as some sort of abomination to be destroyed without remorse is extremely disturbing. Even if you don't buy that it having your memories gives it a valid claim to your identity, it's still a person. And an innocent person at that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-08-2017, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T14:06:19-07:00","id":1113365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113350#post1113350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure you mis-quoted there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But that's my point - it does/may make the same choices you would have. In fact, <i>you</i> might not be making the same choices you would have. Your entire argument pre-assumes the validity of one individual's identity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Closer comparison - a copy that is still intact when the original is scratched.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, I'm saying that just because the Changeling remembers life &quot;before&quot; and returns after 10 years of being separated from their entire social network, this doesn't entitle them to say &quot;Hey, you know the person you've been friends/family with these past 10 years? Forget them - they're just fake. All their stuff, including relationships to you, are now mine. Now - what did I miss?&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Fetch was living their life - <i>they</i> were the ones making decisions, dealing with the consequences. What the Changeling went through in the between time is irrelevant to this point - they could have instead been asleep or cast forward in time. That life went on without them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, the Changeling kills their &quot;imposter&quot;, then tries to continue things as they were 10, 20 years ago? Or, ironically, attempt to &quot;imitate&quot; the person their Fetch was?<br /> <br /> To the outside observer - your friend/family has just been replaced by this alien thing pretending to be the one who you know (and failing, to varying degrees), and they claim <i>they</i> are the &quot;real&quot; one? And you should be fine with this?<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's going to turn out well.<br /> This isn't clear cut. The Changeling who goes &quot;Fetch == fake. Kill it and take its stuff.&quot; may be engaging in the murder of another sentient, and then ruining said sentient's relationships out of a sense of entitlement.<br /> <br /> Remind me again where that sits on the Clarity spectrum (especially in comparison to the Others)?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sure, it's viable. But it isn't <i>easy</i>, as pointed out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1 - It sounds like you're saying I would make a different choice with prior knowledge of my previous choice and its consequences. Which is not the case we're debating in this scenario. If this thing is a carbon copy of myself and truly believes itself to be me, then nothing short of life altering trauma should give it the ability to deviate from doing exactly the same things I would have done in any given situation.<br /> <br /> 2 - That doesn't make sense. Just because the original is scratched doesn't allow the copy to deviate from the original. It just means the undamaged copy would perform in a way the original would have done, had it not been damaged.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3 - But the passage of time in a durance can vary wildly both on the inside and out. Even if you miss the passage of decades, if your durance seemed like only a few minutes, then your reaction is not going to be abandoning your old life and swearing oaths of loyalty to to an anachronistic society built around pagan mysticism. You're going to be scared, confused and understandably enraged. Your first course of action should be to either vent your frustrations on something (like the Fetch), or make at least some modicum of effort to reintegrate into your old life until it becomes clear that joining the Freehold may be a wiser option.<br /> <br /> 4 - I'm not 100% sure about this, but isn't there some way a Changeling can absorb their Fetch when attempting to reclaim their old life? One would think that might assist them in the reintegration process.<br /> <br /> 5 - Most Changelings wouldn't see the Fetch as a sentient thing. Unlike humans, they can see through the mask. They see their friends and family hanging out with a congealed pile of animal viscera, or discarded garbage. This thing is no different in the Changeling's eyes than a Hobgoblin, or a Hedgebeast, or even the True Fae themselves. It is an abomination that stole your life; and the fact nobody even notices the walking, talking pile of gore for what it truly is is bound to provoke some sort of violent reaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T15:47:58-07:00","id":1113427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113249#post1113249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that a Fetch isn't a form of transhumanism. The person it's based on didn't die or transition into a Fetch, they were abducted and the Fetch was used to supplant them. It is, for all intents and purposes, an impostor who's distracting your friends and family while you're chained up in a dungeon somewhere being tortured by some otherworldly creature. In addition to that, the Fetch is commonly described as being a generally more appealing version of the real you. When you finally escape, you come back to find that your Fetch did its best to make everybody love and trust them, which may not necessarily be how the original person behaved / acted or even wanted to behave / act.<br /> <br /> So even if it has all your memories and your appearance, the Fetch is still not a complete copy of you. It's a cheap imitation; one not too dissimilar from identity theft.</div> </div> </div> </div>you keep saying 'cheap' and 'shallow' when describing entities that for all intents and purposes have -all- (rank 0 and 1 ghosts aside.) of your memories and personality. That doesnt seem shallow to me. If its an imitation, then its a very deep, and very Precise imitation.<br /> <br /> Consider this idea: one day, you notice your being followed by a strange ogre like creature that sometimes looks like you, and seems like its trying to corner you. It seems mad, angry, and when it finally confronts you, says that you are in fact, a shallow imitation of it. You still remember your first scrape, you still have your same job, you are pretty much still -you- in absolutely every way, but apparently you are not in fact you, because the -real- you got kidnapped 5 years ago from this day, and wants its life back. but your not entirely convinced that the ogre looking thing has the best in store for your family/friends/life. (and that aside, what about you?)<br /> That is what its like to be a fetch. there is no evidence that they would make different decisions then their 'original' did, because they pretty much have everything the changeling had, And possibly have retained more of their normal personality then the changeling that they were spawned from.<br /> The same goes for ghosts, though atleast in the case of the Ghosts, they are the ones transformed by the 'splitting point' so to speak.<br /> <br /> It might help you to understand the idea if you imagine these beings less as 'imitations' so much as a 'split-off' or a 'fork'. Since the soul has no bearing on 'you' (ignoring the idea of a theoretical hidden 'real soul' of some sort.) aside from maybe representing some of the vitality of life, Then what matters is most of the other stuff that informs you. Identifiers, personality, memories.. all things ghosts and Fetchs have.<br /> But thats just my opinion, to be fair. I do accept the idea that my thought process here is far from universal, and its more of a philosphical position then something thats strictly without opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13637-transhumanmarina","user":"TranshumanMarina","date":". 07-08-2017, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13637-transhumanmarina","name":"TranshumanMarina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T15:52:14-07:00","id":1113429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113365#post1113365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - It sounds like you're saying I would make a different choice with prior knowledge of my previous choice and its consequences. Which is not the case we're debating in this scenario. If this thing is a carbon copy of myself and truly believes itself to be me, then nothing short of life altering trauma should give it the ability to deviate from doing exactly the same things I would have done in any given situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Exactly. There may be cases where the Fetch is <i>more</i> you than you (you being the Changeling).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113365#post1113365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 - That doesn't make sense. Just because the original is scratched doesn't allow the copy to deviate from the original. It just means the undamaged copy would perform in a way the original would have done, had it not been damaged.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I'm not sure your point is coming across? Let's use the example of a movie on DVD. The You is the movie data. When you make a copy, the Copy has the exact same data as the Original (2 Yous). The Original gets scratched. The Copy is thus more accurate (You) than the Original at this point.<br /> <br /> Of course, copies can be burned incorrectly. But we aren't talking about those cases, as the fidelity issues are obvious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113365#post1113365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 - But the passage of time in a durance can vary wildly both on the inside and out. Even if you miss the passage of decades, if your durance seemed like only a few minutes, then your reaction is not going to be abandoning your old life and swearing oaths of loyalty to to an anachronistic society built around pagan mysticism. You're going to be scared, confused and understandably enraged. Your first course of action should be to either vent your frustrations on something (like the Fetch), or make at least some modicum of effort to reintegrate into your old life until it becomes clear that joining the Freehold may be a wiser option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm not saying it wouldn't appear reasonable to the Changeling in such an instance. I'm saying that being understandable for the Changeling <i>doesn't matter</i>, insofar as it affects the consequences to others.<br /> <br /> It may make perfect sense to them (the Changeling) at the time - but lives are still ruined.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113365#post1113365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4 - I'm not 100% sure about this, but isn't there some way a Changeling can absorb their Fetch when attempting to reclaim their old life? One would think that might assist them in the reintegration process.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was an option in one of the supplements. And yeah, that would be a better outcome (like re-merging two forked branches).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113365#post1113365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 - Most Changelings wouldn't see the Fetch as a sentient thing. Unlike humans, they can see through the mask. They see their friends and family hanging out with a congealed pile of animal viscera, or discarded garbage. This thing is no different in the Changeling's eyes than a Hobgoblin, or a Hedgebeast, or even the True Fae themselves. It is an abomination that stole your life; and the fact nobody even notices the walking, talking pile of gore for what it truly is is bound to provoke some sort of violent reaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>So? Just because a Changeling is creeped out by what they see doesn't give them license to end another being's life. While not all Fetches are the same, some have every range of emotion, hopes, and dreams as humanity does. If I Changeling acts on those impulses without checking on the details first, <i>then that Changeling is a murderer</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-08-2017, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T16:23:49-07:00","id":1113444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113429#post1113429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Exactly. There may be cases where the Fetch is <i>more</i> you than you (you being the Changeling).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ...I'm not sure your point is coming across? Let's use the example of a movie on DVD. The You is the movie data. When you make a copy, the Copy has the exact same data as the Original (2 Yous). The Original gets scratched. The Copy is thus more accurate (You) than the Original at this point.<br /> <br /> Of course, copies can be burned incorrectly. But we aren't talking about those cases, as the fidelity issues are obvious.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, my point is that the Fetch used to take your place typically does what it can to earn the trust of everybody you know and care about. It lives your life, but does it better than you would have, so that in the event that you do come looking for revenge, your friends and family are more emotionally invested in the Fetch's protection than your own. There are cases in which the people taken away to Arcadia had pretty crappy lives or personalities before their durance, and came back to find the Fetch turned things around.<br /> <br /> Unless the Changeling was going to make a conscious decision to personally do the same thing prior to their abduction, then the Fetch can not be called their copy, because it did not adhere to the original personality's life choices. It may possess the original's memories, but it chooses to behave differently and is therefor not a perfect duplicate, but a mere imitation.<br /> <br /> A perfect duplicate of the original, who believes that it actually is the original would not make deviant choices. It would make the exact same choices for any given scenario, because it perceives itself as being the real thing and would therefor behave as if it were the real thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-08-2017, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T16:47:06-07:00","id":1113453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113444#post1113444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Okay, my point is that the Fetch used to take your place typically does what it can to earn the trust of everybody you know and care about. It lives your life, but does it better than you would have, so that in the event that you do come looking for revenge, your friends and family are more emotionally invested in the Fetch's protection than your own. There are cases in which the people taken away to Arcadia had pretty crappy lives or personalities before their durance, and came back to find the Fetch turned things around.<br /> <br /> Unless the Changeling was going to make a conscious decision to personally do the same thing prior to their abduction, then the Fetch can not be called their copy, because it did not adhere to the original personality's life choices. It may possess the original's memories, but it chooses to behave differently and is therefor not a perfect duplicate, but a mere imitation.<br /> <br /> A perfect duplicate of the original, who believes that it actually is the original would not make deviant choices. It would make the exact same choices for any given scenario, because it perceives itself as being the real thing and would therefor behave as if it were the real thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see the misconception. Fetches <i>don't</i> all behave one way. Some continue just as you would because they think they are you. Some know they are Fetches, and react in a variety of ways. Some are cold sociopaths. They vary. A Changeling that assumes they are all the same is in for sorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T23:20:48-08:00","id":1156590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1113350#post1113350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> So, the Changeling kills their &quot;imposter&quot;, then tries to continue things as they were 10, 20 years ago? Or, ironically, attempt to &quot;imitate&quot; the person their Fetch was?<br /> <br /> To the outside observer - your friend/family has just been replaced by this alien thing pretending to be the one who you know (and failing, to varying degrees), and they claim <i>they</i> are the &quot;real&quot; one? And you should be fine with this?<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's going to turn out well.<br /> This isn't clear cut. The Changeling who goes &quot;Fetch == fake. Kill it and take its stuff.&quot; may be engaging in the murder of another sentient, and then ruining said sentient's relationships out of a sense of entitlement.<br /> <br /> Remind me again where that sits on the Clarity spectrum (especially in comparison to the Others)?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sure, it's viable. But it isn't <i>easy</i>, as pointed out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, I just realized an epiphany regarding this easy solution. Changelings don't exactly walk around showing off their true form. Which means they look human to normal people.<br /> <br /> And there's the fact that Fetches revert to their true form in the event of their deaths.<br /> <br /> Soooo, proving your identity should be a simple matter of killing the imposter and showing your friends and family the evidence when the thing they thought was you dissolves into a pile of garbage and viscera.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I'm no medical expert, but I'm pretty sure human bodies aren't supposed to do that!&quot; </i><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T00:05:30-08:00","id":1156598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1156590#post1156590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's the fact that Fetches revert to their true form in the event of their deaths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nyr, they revert to their constituent materials <i>at some point after </i>they die. That can be as late as post-burial, which kind of puts a damper on the premature celebration when to all appearances you have simply straight-up murdered a dude who likely looks more like you than you do after an indeterminate amount of time in the time-warping mutagen pit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T00:13:53-08:00","id":1156599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1156598#post1156598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nyr, they revert to their constituent materials <i>at some point after </i>they die. That can be as late as post-burial, which kind of puts a damper on the premature celebration when to all appearances you have simply straight-up murdered a dude who likely looks more like you than you do after an indeterminate amount of time in the time-warping mutagen pit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, that would make things more difficult, I suppose. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T00:17:26-08:00","id":1156600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1156590#post1156590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I just realized an epiphany regarding this easy solution. Changelings don't exactly walk around showing off their true form. Which means they look human to normal people.<br /> <br /> And there's the fact that Fetches revert to their true form in the event of their deaths.<br /> <br /> Soooo, proving your identity should be a simple matter of killing the imposter and showing your friends and family the evidence when the thing they thought was you dissolves into a pile of garbage and viscera.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I'm no medical expert, but I'm pretty sure human bodies aren't supposed to do that!&quot; </i><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, you\u2019re saying if someone showed up tomorrow and killed your wife (or whatever loved one you care to use as the example), and the body turned into leaves and sticks, you\u2019d just welcome their murderer into your home, because they claim to be your <i>real</i> loved one?<br /> <br /> Granted, human bodies aren\u2019t supposed to turn into leaves and sticks, but seeing that happen doesn\u2019t prove the Changeling\u2019s Story is true; all it proves is that there\u2019s some kind of fuckery going on, and you have nothing but the Changeling\u2019s word for it that it wasn\u2019t fuckery on their part. And I don\u2019t know about you, but I\u2019m not particularly inclined to take the word of someone who would murder my loved one (and potentially turn them into leaves and sticks) just to try to prove a point.<br /> <br /> Hell, even if I do believe them, they\u2019re claiming that they\u2019ve been gone for however many years and I\u2019ve been living with the thing that turned into leaves and sticks that whole time. Loving it the whole time. And it\u2019s been loving me the whole time, or at least doing a convincing enough impression of loving me that I can\u2019t tell if it isn\u2019t genuine. It may not have been human, but it was still my loved one, and the person claiming to be my <i>real</i> loved one just fucking murdered it. There is absolutely no way I\u2019m taking that well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-07-2017, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T00:50:11-08:00","id":1156604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1156600#post1156600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, you\u2019re saying if someone showed up tomorrow and killed your wife (or whatever loved one you care to use as the example), and the body turned into leaves and sticks, you\u2019d just welcome their murderer into your home, because they claim to be your <i>real</i> loved one?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would be willing to hear them out, at the very least. They had just provided me with hard, physical evidence of what I could only describe as a supernatural event. Granted, common sense would dictate that I try to defend the imposter until after I saw the unnatural remains. But once they dissolved into refuse, I'd quickly demand an explanation.<br /> <br /> The concept of somebody being forcibly changed into a magical creature isn't that unbelievable. The story is plastered all over supernatural folk lore from nearly every religion, culture and ethnicity.<br /> <br /> If somebody told me that those close to me were magical imposters and had some way to prove their claims, I would reconsider my stance on thinking they were crazy.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, the idea of a Fetch and fairy abductions is exactly what the IRL changeling mythos is all about. Fairies steal somebody away and replace them with a disguised creature. Considering that I've heard about such things happening in other parts of the world, I'd probably have an easier time adjusting to the situation than somebody who has absolutely no idea what's going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-07-2017, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T01:01:40-08:00","id":1156607,"title":"","content":"You probably want to get your explanation in first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T01:50:33-08:00","id":1156618,"title":"","content":"...you guys are acting as if it's normal for human person to act rationally while under extreme emotional distress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T05:51:40-08:00","id":1156647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1156618#post1156618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...you guys are acting as if it's normal for human person to act rationally while under extreme emotional distress.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it normal for any sentient being to do so? Even the supernatural need a supernatural edge to help with that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T07:22:05-08:00","id":1156671,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah, the obvious reaction to encountering the supernatural for the first time isn't going to be <i>&quot;Oh, hey, monsters are real... that's neat.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> But the rate at which people adjust to the situation would be more of a personal case by case basis. <br /> <br /> Being diagnosed with a variety of psychological and social problems would probably make the adjustment process 'easier' than it would for healthy individuals.<br /> <br /> Like I said in the '<b>You As A'</b> threads, I've always wished to encounter stuff like this in the real world. I was a a true believer in magic during my youth and even now, I still have hope in its possible existence. And after the initial shock of <i>&quot;holy shit, magic!&quot;</i> wore off, I'd probably be very curious to learn as much as possible about the world I'd just been exposed to. And I'm not about to chase off my first and presumably only source of information on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T10:20:16-08:00","id":1156723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1156604#post1156604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would be willing to hear them out, at the very least. They had just provided me with hard, physical evidence of what I could only describe as a supernatural event. Granted, common sense would dictate that I try to defend the imposter until after I saw the unnatural remains. But once they dissolved into refuse, I'd quickly demand an explanation.<br /> <br /> The concept of somebody being forcibly changed into a magical creature isn't that unbelievable. The story is plastered all over supernatural folk lore from nearly every religion, culture and ethnicity.<br /> <br /> If somebody told me that those close to me were magical imposters and had some way to prove their claims, I would reconsider my stance on thinking they were crazy.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, the idea of a Fetch and fairy abductions is exactly what the IRL changeling mythos is all about. Fairies steal somebody away and replace them with a disguised creature. Considering that I've heard about such things happening in other parts of the world, I'd probably have an easier time adjusting to the situation than somebody who has absolutely no idea what's going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Mage would have a really easy time getting away with murdering people you care about, then,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T11:08:24-08:00","id":1156737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1156604#post1156604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The concept of somebody being forcibly changed into a magical creature isn't that unbelievable. The story is plastered all over supernatural folk lore from nearly every religion, culture and ethnicity.</div> </div> </div> </div>And whose to say that isn't what just happened to your love one right in front of you, turning them into a pile of leaves and sticks? Why would you trust the new doppleganger rather than the one you have been with?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T11:27:49-08:00","id":1156743,"title":"","content":"'I kind of miss old Nyrufa. New Nyrufa constantly complains about being tortured for what seems like an eternity by the Bell King and how we'll never understand what it's like. Plus his new friends are so creepy.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T11:38:02-08:00","id":1156744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1156737#post1156737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And whose to say that isn't what just happened to your love one right in front of you, turning them into a pile of leaves and sticks? Why would you trust the new doppleganger rather than the one you have been with?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, sure, that is a possibility, but it's not an idea that I'm familiar with. Having a doppleganger switched out when I wasn't paying attention makes sense. Having a doppleganger perform the switch right in front of my eyes doesn't. I know the Fae are supposed to be crazy, but that plan just sounds like they're trying too hard.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1156743#post1156743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'I kind of miss old Nyrufa. New Nyrufa constantly complains about being tortured for what seems like an eternity by the Bell King and how we'll never understand what it's like. Plus his new friends are so creepy.'</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm not really sure what that's supposed to mean.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1156723#post1156723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Mage would have a really easy time getting away with murdering people you care about, then,</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would apply to everybody on the planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-07-2017, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T11:50:53-08:00","id":1156748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1156744#post1156744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, sure, that is a possibility, but it's not an idea that I'm familiar with. Having a doppleganger switched out when I wasn't paying attention makes sense. Having a doppleganger perform the switch right in front of my eyes doesn't. I know the Fae are supposed to be crazy, but that plan just sounds like they're trying too hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your premise is that it seems believable that the newcomer is actually the real loved one; why wouldn't a Fae take advantage of that? The Fae comes in looking like your loved one, kills your loved one and makes their corpse turn into a pile of leaves ( or teleports them away and makes a pile of leaves appear; same difference), claims they were your loved one the whole time. Bam. Switch made. And since its so common a story that the newcomer is your real loved one, you buy it and they have succeeded, doesn't seem like they are trying very hard to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T11:55:01-08:00","id":1156751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1156748#post1156748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your premise is that it seems believable that the newcomer is actually the real loved one; why wouldn't a Fae take advantage of that? The Fae comes in looking like your loved one, kills your loved one and makes their corpse turn into a pile of leaves ( or teleports them away and makes a pile of leaves appear; same difference), claims they were your loved one the whole time. Bam. Switch made. And since its so common a story that the newcomer is your real loved one, you buy it and they have succeeded, doesn't seem like they are trying very hard to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I meant trying to hard to be crazy.<br /> <br /> But I do see you point, now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T11:58:04-08:00","id":1156753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1156744#post1156744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really sure what that's supposed to mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>The experiences a changeling has been through have changed their body and soul. It should also have changed their personality a bit.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in the real world, your friends and family are living with a duplicate who may have gone a different route than you but is generally the same person.<br /> <br /> Killing them would not erase their memories of being with the fetch, just like slipping back into their lives would not change your personality to that of how you were before you became a changeling. You have changed, and just because you spent years with them earlier does not mean that you would even want to slip into that same relationship. Certainly there's bound to be some animosity towards a fetch, but someone who has spent years and years with alien beings is not going to be working off the same frame of the world as the person who lived a mundane life beforehand. It's why people who were friends in high school don't always go off to college or other cities and stay close friends forever. You've changed. They've changed. You're not the same person they were friends with, or even family with.<br /> <br /> Then there's the inherent dangers of it. Killing a fetch duplicate just so you can spend time around your family is an inherently selfish act (providing the fetch isn't treating them badly), especially considering the fae manifestation of spirits of the hunt, as well as the predations of other changelings and supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Also while changelings look human, they don't always look like they human they were before, though this may change in second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T12:08:50-08:00","id":1156756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1156753#post1156753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The experiences a changeling has been through have changed their body and soul. It should also have changed their personality a bit.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in the real world, your friends and family are living with a duplicate who may have gone a different route than you but is generally the same person.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oooooh, okay! I understand now! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I thought the previous comment was directed as me personally.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T12:36:43-08:00","id":1156766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1107411-humanity-is-overrated?p=1156756#post1156756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the previous comment was directed as me personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yeah I originally used the name John but changed it to Nyrufa hoping it would get the idea across, sorry about that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}